{"ts":"2026-09-09T06:17:28.666117059Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"AskUserQuestion","tool_input":{"annotations":{},"answers":{"How should the exploration be produced? Org rules say never solo-design, but this is a leader-level plan document.":"I draft, specialists spike later (Recommended)","Is a PR/FAQ update in scope for this effort? A GUI arguably shifts the product thesis ('a GUI is what makes ethos real').":"Not yet — plan doc first (Recommended)","Where should the exploration document live?":"I would consider how you would setup a monorepo but it is sufficient to create one subdir now"},"questions":[{"header":"Doc home","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"e.g. docs/ui-exploration.md on a branch in this repo — keeps the plan next to the system it describes; the UI repo gets created later, when a phase earns it.","label":"ethos repo, docs/ (Recommended)"},{"description":"Create punt-labs/ethos-ui (or similar) immediately and put the plan there as its founding document.","label":"New sibling repo now"},{"description":"Draft in .tmp/ for iteration, promote to a tracked doc once you've reviewed it.","label":".tmp scratch first"}],"question":"Where should the exploration document live?"},{"header":"Process","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"I research (Block's buzz/goose, Tauri ecosystem) and write the phased plan myself — a plan doc is COO-authorable. Specialist missions execute the spikes it defines.","label":"I draft, specialists spike later (Recommended)"},{"description":"Instantiate the product pipeline (prfaq → design → …) with ghr/edt/mdm from the start. Slower, more ceremony, more perspectives.","label":"Full product pipeline now"},{"description":"I write the plan, then dispatch a review mission to edt (UX) and mdm before you see the final version.","label":"Hybrid: I draft + edt UX review"}],"question":"How should the exploration be produced? Org rules say never solo-design, but this is a leader-level plan document."},{"header":"PR/FAQ","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"Keep this exploration self-contained; touch prfaq.tex only if/when the UI direction is ratified.","label":"Not yet — plan doc first (Recommended)"},{"description":"Include a section in the plan noting exactly what the PR/FAQ would need to say about the GUI, ready to fold in.","label":"Yes, flag prfaq changes"}],"question":"Is a PR/FAQ update in scope for this effort? A GUI arguably shifts the product thesis ('a GUI is what makes ethos real')."}]},"tool_input_hash":"30a670a0c95070f62c233532f94b55c3fa278613f89d01e664f696e7c7dca0ca","tool_input_preview":"{\"annotations\":{},\"answers\":{\"How should the exploration be produced? Org rules say never solo-design, but this is a leader-level plan document.\":\"I draft, specialists spike later (Recommended)\",\"Is a..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-09T06:19:21.886917446Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Research Block buzz + goose desktop","name":"research-block","prompt":"Research task: I'm planning a Tauri-based desktop GUI for \"ethos\" (a local-first agent-identity/mission tool whose state lives as YAML/JSONL files in git repos). The founder wants it \"modelled off of what Block's buzz is built like.\"\n\nQuestions to answer, with sources:\n1. What is Block's \"buzz\"? (Block, Inc. — the Square/Cash App company, known for open-sourcing the \"goose\" AI agent.) It may be a 2026 open-source project. Find its repo, purpose, and tech stack. If \"buzz\" doesn't exist, say so plainly and identify what the founder most likely meant (goose desktop? another Block project?).\n2. How is Block's goose desktop app built? Frontend framework, Electron vs Tauri, how the UI talks to its backend (I believe there's a local daemon \"goosed\" — confirm transport: HTTP? stdio?), repo layout (monorepo? where does the desktop app live relative to the Rust core?).\n3. What architectural patterns from buzz/goose are worth copying for a local-first desktop app that fronts a Go CLI binary: daemon vs sidecar, API shape, packaging, auto-update.\n4. Any notable 2025-2026 Tauri desktop apps for developer tools worth studying as references (design + architecture).\n\nOutput: a compact structured report (markdown) with: what buzz is (or isn't), goose desktop architecture summary, a \"patterns to copy / patterns to avoid\" list, and links. Keep it under ~150 lines. Do not write any files; return the report as your final message.","subagent_type":"quarry:researcher"},"tool_input_hash":"65085c69d1a333004895b00a882271696d233b9c16806123ebb1ab8799db25c3","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"Research Block buzz + goose desktop\",\"name\":\"research-block\",\"prompt\":\"Research task: I'm planning a Tauri-based desktop GUI for \\\"ethos\\\" (a local-first agent-identity/mission tool wh..."}
