{"ts":"2026-09-09T06:19:44.161734032Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Survey ethos backend UI surfaces","name":"explore-backend","prompt":"Survey the ethos repo at \u003crepo\u003e to ground the design of a future desktop GUI. Search breadth: very thorough. READ-ONLY — change nothing.\n\nReport on:\n1. internal/ui/ — the existing `ethos ui` web UI: what pages/routes exist, what data it reads (missions, delegations, audit trails), how it reads them (direct file parsing? shared internal packages?), whether it exposes any JSON endpoints or only HTML, how the server is started/bound (port, auth?).\n2. Machine-readable CLI surfaces: which `ethos` commands support --json or --format output today (grep cmd/ethos for json flags); notably mission show/log/results, find missions, audit show, identity/team/role list.\n3. On-disk data shapes the GUI would render: for .punt-labs/ethos/ in this repo — the structure of a mission directory (contract/results/events files and their schemas, from internal/mission structs), missions.jsonl trace line shape, sessions/\u003cid\u003e/audit*.jsonl entry shape (internal/hook audit entry struct), and the sealed-chunk naming/sealing mechanism (internal/audit).\n4. Traceability joins available for an \"ethos blame\" feature: does anything currently join a git commit SHA to a delegation/mission id? Look for commit trailers written by hooks (plugin/hooks, internal/githook — commit-msg hook), fields in audit entries (delegation_id, session), missions.jsonl fields, and `ethos audit show --delegation` implementation. State precisely what chain exists: file line -\u003e git blame commit -\u003e ??? -\u003e mission.\n5. Anything else that looks purpose-built for a GUI (dashboard code, `ethos find missions` filters, event logs).\n\nOutput: a structured report with file:line references, under ~200 lines. Conclusions over file dumps.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"tool_input_hash":"547e3a66f0b3a