\"chip mono\" title=\"pinned content hash\"\u003esha256 9f31…c2\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003ewrite-set\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd class=\"mono\"\u003einternal/ui/** · cmd/ethos/blame.go\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003eticket\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd class=\"mono\"\u003eethos-b41k\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003ebudget\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd\u003e3 rounds · 2 used\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003eround 1\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chip fail\"\u003efail\u003c/span\u003e conf 0.71 — heuristic mislabeled as authoritative; reflected, re-scoped\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003eevidence\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd\u003ego test ✓ · golden schema ✓ · 2 files · +214 −61\u003c/dd\u003e\n            \u003c/dl\u003e\n          \u003c/details\u003e","old_string":"          \u003cdiv\u003e\n            \u003ch3\u003eTimeline\u003c/h3\u003e\n            \u003cdiv class=\"timeline\" style=\"margin-top:6px\"\u003e\n              \u003cdiv class=\"tl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"t\"\u003e14:02\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"dot2 seal\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan\u003eaudit sealed · 214 lines → chunk \u003cspan class=\"mono\"\u003e…320813\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n              \u003cdiv class=\"tl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"t\"\u003e13:57\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"dot2 pass\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan\u003eresult submitted · round 2 · pass\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n              \u003cdiv class=\"tl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"t\"\u003e13:12\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"dot2 acc\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan\u003edelegation d-2026-09-08-021 spawned · agent bwk\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n              \u003cdiv class=\"tl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"t\"\u003e11:48\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"dot2\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan\u003ereflection recorded · round 1 → 2\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n              \u003cdiv class=\"tl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"t\"\u003e09:30\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"dot2\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan\u003emission created · leader claude\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"d0cf66ea850a55f91e515cca953a4ab27d91614e4234166003a5dc68bf089d73","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"\\u003crepo\\u003e/desktop/mockups/ethos-desktop-mockup.html\",\"new_string\":\"          \\u003cdiv\\u003e\\n            \\u003ch3\\u003eTimeline\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n            \\u003cdiv class=\\\"time..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-09T13:56:40.337580909Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"\u003crepo\u003e/desktop/mockups/ethos-desktop-mockup.html","new_string":"          \u003cdiv\u003e\n            \u003ch3\u003eWhy this line exists\u003c/h3\u003e\n            \u003cdiv class=\"quote\" style=\"margin-top:8px\"\u003e\"Every occurrence of the home or repo prefix in a string is rewritten; sibling paths sharing the prefix are not corrupted.\"\u003c/div\u003e\n            \u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11.5px;color:var(--faint);margin-top:5px\"\u003esuccess criterion · mission \u003cspan class=\"mono\"\u003em-2026-08-22-011\u003c/span\u003e · \u003cspan class=\"chip pass\" style=\"font-size:10.5px\"\u003eclosed · pass\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003cdiv\u003e\n            \u003ch3\u003eThe ask\u003c/h3\u003e\n            \u003cdiv class=\"prompt\" style=\"margin-top:8px\"\u003e\n              \u003cdiv class=\"prompt-head\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"avatar\" style=\"width:16px;height:16px;font-size:8px\"\u003eCL\u003c/span\u003eclaude → rmh · \u003cspan class=\"mono\" style=\"color:var(--faint)\"\u003eprompt.md\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n              \u003cp\u003eCommitted mission records still carry personal home paths and emails. Build a PathRedactor that rewrites them to portable tokens — \u003cspan class=\"mono\"\u003e~\u003c/span\u003e and \u003cspan class=\"mono\"\u003e\u0026lt;repo\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e — without corrupting sibling paths that merely share the prefix. Evaluator is djb: treat this as leakage prevention, not cosmetics.\u003c/p\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003cdiv\u003e\n            \u003ch3\u003eWhat came back\u003c/h3\u003e\n            \u003cdiv class=\"prompt back\" style=\"margin-top:8px\"\u003e\n              \u003cdiv class=\"prompt-head\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"avatar\" style=\"width:16px;height:16px;font-size:8px\"\u003eRH\u003c/span\u003ermh · \u003cspan class=\"chip pass\"\u003epass\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"conf\" style=\"margin-left:auto\"\u003eround 2 · conf 0.86\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n              \u003cp\u003eRedactor rewrites every occurrence, wins repo-over-home on nested paths, and refuses unusable roots rather than guessing. The ethos-docs sibling case djb flagged in round 1 is now a boundary test.\u003c/p\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003cdiv\u003e\n            \u003ch3\u003eAudit trail\u003c/h3\u003e\n            \u003cdiv style=\"margin-top:8px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px\"\u003e\n              \u003cdiv style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)\"\u003e214 tool calls · sealed \u003cspan class=\"chip seal\"\u003ein this commit\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n              \u003cspan class=\"linkish\"\u003eOpen 214 audit lines →\u003c/span\u003e\n              \u003cspan class=\"linkish\"\u003eMission footprint: 4 commits, 9 files →\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003cdetails class=\"mech\"\u003e\n            \u003csummary\u003eMechanics — commit, delegation, hashes\u003c/summary\u003e\n            \u003cdl class=\"kv\" style=\"margin-top:10px\"\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003ecommit\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd class=\"mono\"\u003e6ca6bd4\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003edelegation\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd class=\"mono\"\u003ed-2026-08-22-007\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003eleader\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd\u003eclaude\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003eevaluator\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd\u003edjb \u003cspan class=\"chip mono\"\u003ehash pinned\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003ewrite-set\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd class=\"mono\"\u003einternal/mission/redact*.go\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003eevidence\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd\u003ego test -race ✓ · boundary cases ✓\u003c/dd\u003e\n            \u003c/dl\u003e\n          \u003c/details\u003e","old_string":"          \u003cdiv\u003e\n            \u003ch3\u003eMission\u003c/h3\u003e\n            \u003cdl class=\"kv\" style=\"margin-top:8px\"\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003eid\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd class=\"mono\"\u003em-2026-08-22-011\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003estatus\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chip pass\"\u003eclosed · pass\u003c/span\u003e round 2 of 3\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003eleader\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd\u003eclaude\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003eevaluator\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd\u003edjb \u003cspan class=\"chip mono\"\u003ehash pinned\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/dd\u003e\n              \u003cdt\u003ewrite-set\u003c/dt\u003e\u003cdd class=\"mono\"\u003einternal/mission/redact*.go\u003c/dd\u003e\n            \u003c/dl\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003cdiv\u003e\n            \u003ch3\u003eCriterion this line served\u003c/h3\u003e\n            \u003cdiv class=\"quote\" style=\"margin-top:8px\"\u003e\"Every occurrence of the home or repo prefix in a string is rewritten; sibling paths sharing the prefix are not corrupted.\"\u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003cdiv\u003e\n            \u003ch3\u003eVerdict\u003c/h3\u003e\n            \u003cdiv class=\"round-block\" style=\"margin-top:8px\"\u003e\n              \u003cdiv class=\"head\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eRound 2\u003c/b\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chip pass\"\u003epass\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"conf\"\u003econfidence 0.86\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n              \u003cdiv style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)\"\u003eevidence: go test -race ✓ · boundary cases ✓ · evaluator djb\u003c/div\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003cdiv\u003e\n            \u003ch3\u003eAudit trail\u003c/h3\u003e\n            \u003cdiv style=\"margin-top:8px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px\"\u003e\n              \u003cdiv style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)\"\u003edelegation \u003cspan class=\"mono\"\u003ed-2026-08-22-007\u003c/span\u003e · 214 tool calls · sealed \u003cspan class=\"chip seal\"\u003ein this commit\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n              \u003cspan class=\"linkish\"\u003eView spawn prompt →\u003c/span\u003e\n              \u003cspan class=\"linkish\"\u003eOpen 214 audit lines →\u003c/span\u003e\n              \u003cspan class=\"linkish\"\u003eMission footprint: 4 commits, 9 files →\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003c/div\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"e604ac62c87edcac6ff4e80122f74c005dc1251b481ffc5e05934076d7f83fcc","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"\\u003crepo\\u003e/desktop/mockups/ethos-desktop-mockup.html\",\"new_string\":\"          \\u003cdiv\\u003e\\n            \\u003ch3\\u003eWhy this line exists\\u003c/h3\\u003e\\n            \\u003cdiv ..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-09T13:56:48.964080613Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"\u003crepo\u003e/desktop/mockups/ethos-desktop-mockup.html","new_string":"  .quote { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding: 2px 0 2px 10px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }\n  .linkish { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 550; font-size: 12px; cursor: default; }\n\n  /* narrative blocks: the ask / what came back */\n  .prompt { background: var(--surface2); border: 1px solid var(--border-soft); border-radius: 10px; padding: 10px 12px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px; }\n  .prompt p { font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.55; }\n  .prompt-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 550; }\n  .prompt.back { background: transparent; border-style: dashed; }\n\n  /* mechanics disclosure: plumbing recedes */\n  .mech { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft); padding-top: 10px; }\n  .mech summary { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--faint); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; cursor: pointer; list-style: none; }\n  .mech summary::before { content: \"▸ \"; }\n  .mech[open] summary::before { content: \"▾ \"; }","old_string":"  .quote { border-left: 3px solid var(--border); padding: 2px 0 2px 10px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }\n  .linkish { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 550; font-size: 12px; cursor: default; }","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"622612beb212d0f18dff2e399deb70f23e5f0fb58483750d554b8af3174d488b","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"\\u003crepo\\u003e/desktop/mockups/ethos-desktop-mockup.html\",\"new_string\":\"  .quote { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding: 2px 0 2px 10px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }\\n..."}
