{"ts":"2026-09-09T13:59:45.12700074Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"\u003crepo\u003e/desktop/PLAN.md","new_string":"### 4.2 Total coverage: no dark data\n\n**Operator-ruled (2026-09-09): 100% of ethos data lands somewhere in the\nGUI.** Every entity and every field in the store has a declared home on some\nscreen. This composes with narrative-first (§ 4.4) rather than conflicting\nwith it: coverage governs *that* data lands; narrative-first governs *where\nin the hierarchy* it lands (`strict_preconditions` belongs in a Mechanics\ndisclosure — but it belongs). Secret-bearing values (`.ext/\u003cns\u003e.local.yaml`)\nrender masked, never omitted — the same honesty rule as audit redaction.\n\nEnforced, not asserted: a `validate-content`-style build gate walks every\nexported field of every GUI payload struct against a checked-in claims file\n(`desktop/coverage.yaml`, field → screen). A new backend field with no\ndeclared GUI home fails CI. Appendix C is the human-readable matrix the\nclaims file is generated from.\n\n### 4.3 Information architecture — six sections, one window","old_string":"### 4.2 Information architecture — five sections, one window","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"5bf107fd62cd4c685bf23210ae99ea1421763ca4a29fd22068ee03dc08cac9bc","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"\\u003crepo\\u003e/desktop/PLAN.md\",\"new_string\":\"### 4.2 Total coverage: no dark data\\n\\n**Operator-ruled (2026-09-09): 100% of ethos data lands somewhere in the\\nGUI.** Every entity and ..."}
