{"ts":"2026-09-09T14:02:43.262415877Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"\u003crepo\u003e/desktop/PLAN.md","new_string":"### 4.5 Design language\n\n**UX guideline: Linear** (operator-ruled 2026-09-09). Linear is the benchmark\nfor how the app *feels* — distinct from Berd, which remains the benchmark for\nhow it is *built*. The Linear idioms we adopt:\n\n- **Speed as a feature.** Every interaction under ~50 ms. Linear earns this\n  with a local sync engine; we earn it with the local daemon — same physics.\n- **List-first density.** The default Missions view is a grouped,\n  keyboard-navigable list (status glyphs, one row per mission); the board is\n  an alternate view, not the home.\n- **Peek before navigate.** Selection opens a side panel; a full page only on\n  explicit demand. Context is never lost to a route change.\n- **Keyboard everywhere.** ⌘K as the universal entry; j/k list navigation;\n  single-key actions surfaced contextually.\n- **One accent on monochrome.** A single structural accent over LCH-tuned\n  grays; hairline borders over shadows; Inter-class type at 13 px.\n\nThe trust-product stance survives inside Linear's idiom: this is still a\nledger. Color only where it means something — verdict green/red, seal amber,\nthe one accent — monospace reserved for IDs and hashes, dark and light themes\nfrom day one (system webviews differ; theme tokens are cheap early and\nexpensive late). S5's design review evaluates the prototype explicitly\nagainst Linear's bar.","old_string":"### 4.5 Design language\n\nThis is a *trust* product; the design language is ledger-like. Calm,\ntypographic, generous whitespace, monospace accents for IDs and hashes,\nrestrained color (verdict green/red and seal-state amber earn color; nothing\nelse does). Dark and light themes from day one (system webviews differ; theme\ntokens are cheap early and expensive late).","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"22f64741f5c219e66086eff795e9b948a425a2b455bcfd7a233d9294d88a677b","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"\\u003crepo\\u003e/desktop/PLAN.md\",\"new_string\":\"### 4.5 Design language\\n\\n**UX guideline: Linear** (operator-ruled 2026-09-09). Linear is the benchmark\\nfor how the app *feels* — dist..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-09T14:03:08.217832449Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"\u003crepo\u003e/desktop/PLAN.md","new_string":"| T5 | **Visual regression** — Playwright screenshots of component states (Ladle/Storybook), diffed | nightly | medium |\n\n**The agent visual loop (operator-ruled 2026-09-09: exists before any real\nwork).** Screenshots are not just T5's regression artifact — they are how the\nagents *see* what they build. Workers on UI missions are otherwise coding\nblind. Requirement: one command (`make shot SCREEN=\u003croute\u003e [STATE=\u003cfixture\u003e]`)\nboots the fixture daemon + vite, drives Playwright headless to the requested\nscreen/state, and writes a PNG the agent reads back in the same tool loop\n(Claude Code renders images natively). Edit → shot → look → iterate is the\ncore dev cycle for every UI mission; mission contracts for UI work must\nrequire screenshot evidence in results. True-Tauri window shots (native\nchrome, menus) ride the T4 WebdriverIO lane on Linux; the Playwright loop\ncovers everything else because the data path never touches Rust.","old_string":"| T5 | **Visual regression** — Playwright screenshots of component states (Ladle/Storybook), diffed | nightly | medium |","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"73eb944111ae6464cca67697f0501fe4576d5bf11c1ba5dde909c2f902197c1e","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"\\u003crepo\\u003e/desktop/PLAN.md\",\"new_string\":\"| T5 | **Visual regression** — Playwright screenshots of component states (Ladle/Storybook), diffed | nightly | medium |\\n\\n**The agent ..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-09T14:03:11.869529273Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"\u003crepo\u003e/desktop/PLAN.md","new_string":"The § 7 table, green in CI, against the walking skeleton: one real test in\nevery tier, path-filtered workflows, cost measured. Includes the **agent\nvisual loop**: `make shot` producing a PNG an agent can read back, proven on\nthis machine, before any feature mission dispatches.\n**Kill criterion:** none; exit is \"the pyramid runs, a PR that breaks each\ntier is demonstrably caught by it, and an agent has demonstrably iterated on\na screen using only `make shot` output.\"","old_string":"The § 7 table, green in CI, against the walking skeleton: one real test in\nevery tier, path-filtered workflows, cost measured.\n**Kill criterion:** none; exit is \"the pyramid runs and a PR that breaks each\ntier is demonstrably caught by it.\"","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"401928a619573c5347e81da4691eb85ee71de5430a1c9ea24b6848845ead0089","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"\\u003crepo\\u003e/desktop/PLAN.md\",\"new_string\":\"The § 7 table, green in CI, against the walking skeleton: one real test in\\nevery tier, path-filtered workflows, cost measured. Includes ..."}
