{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:01:48.850157003Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Verify ethos CLI surfaces + missions","name":"explore-ethos-cli","prompt":"READ-ONLY exploration in \u003crepo\u003e (and ~/.punt-labs/ethos). You may RUN read-only ethos CLI commands (list/show/find/session/identity — nothing that creates, closes, or modifies anything). Purpose: ground an 8-hour spike where a Go bridge daemon shells out to `ethos --json` CLI commands to feed a desktop UI, and where the work itself is managed via ethos missions in a NEW repo at ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk.\n\nReport precisely:\n\n1. **JSON shapes the daemon will consume** — run each against this repo and show a TRUNCATED sample (first mission / first 2 entries, elide long strings):\n   - `ethos mission list --json`\n   - `ethos find missions --format json` (2 lines)\n   - `ethos mission show \u003csome-closed-id\u003e --json`\n   - `ethos mission log \u003csame-id\u003e --json` (2 events)\n   - `ethos mission results \u003csame-id\u003e --json` (if a --json flag exists; else note format)\n   - `ethos identity list --json` (2 entries)\n   - `ethos session` (whatever format it has; note if --json works)\n   Note which of: prompt.md content, result prose, open_questions, artifacts listing are NOT reachable via any CLI flag (the gaps list matters).\n2. **Open-mission visibility**: does `mission list --json` include open/non-closed missions, or only closed (missions.jsonl)? Verify against the store (count dirs vs list output).\n3. **Mission dispatch mechanics for a fresh repo**: read cmd/ethos for `mission create --file` and `mission dispatch` flags; show the minimal valid contract YAML fields (read a real contract.yaml, e.g. any recent mission, and the Contract struct's required fields from internal/mission). Does `ethos mission create` work in a repo where ethos is NOT enabled (no .punt-labs/ethos)? What does `ethos enable` deposit in a fresh repo (read internal/enable or docs/ETHOS-SETUP.md — list the files it writes)?\n4. **Identity resolution for desk**: does ~/.punt-labs/ethos/identities/ exist and contain the org handles (bwk, adb, rmh, mdm, djb...)? (ls it.) Would a fresh repo with no repo-local store resolve them via the global layer (check internal/resolve default chain when no repo-only config)?\n5. **Pipeline `quick`**: stages and defaults (`ethos mission pipeline show quick` or read seed content).\n\nOutput: structured report, ≤150 lines, file:line refs where relevant, truncated JSON samples in fenced blocks. Conclusions over dumps.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"tool_input_hash":"134f0e407ec55c16d615a555c1996860e0bc057df0ea29224d21649b49ecdfdd","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"Verify ethos CLI surfaces + missions\",\"name\":\"explore-ethos-cli\",\"prompt\":\"READ-ONLY exploration in \\u003crepo\\u003e (and ~/.punt-labs/ethos). You may RUN read-only ethos CLI commands ..."}
