{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:02:01.377656985Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Tauri scaffold + sidecar facts","name":"explore-tauri-setup","prompt":"Research task (read-only; use the context7 MCP tools — resolve-library-id then query-docs — against Tauri v2 docs; supplement with WebSearch only if context7 lacks an answer). Purpose: ground an 8-hour spike that scaffolds a Tauri 2 app (React 19 + TypeScript + Vite, pnpm) at ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk, bundling a locally-built Go daemon binary as a sidecar, on Linux (Ubuntu, Wayland/X11), dev-loop only (no packaging/signing needed for the spike).\n\nAnswer precisely, with the exact config/code snippets:\n\n1. **Scaffold**: current `create-tauri-app` invocation for pnpm + React + TS template; what it generates; any Linux system deps needed for `tauri dev` (webkit2gtk version etc.) and the command to check/install them on Ubuntu.\n2. **Sidecar**: exact steps to bundle an external (Go) binary — `tauri.conf.json` `externalBin` entry, the target-triple filename suffix requirement (e.g. deskd-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu), the shell-plugin capability JSON to permit spawning it, and the Rust or JS code to spawn it with `Command.sidecar()` and read its stdout (to grab the port/token line). Also: in `tauri dev` mode, where must the sidecar binary sit?\n3. **Fetch to localhost**: does the webview fetch() to http://127.0.0.1:\u003cport\u003e work out of the box in Tauri 2, or does it need the http plugin / CSP / capability changes? Exact tauri.conf.json CSP or capability needed for a dev spike.\n4. **Env/token handoff**: simplest sanctioned way to pass a port+token from the spawned sidecar to the frontend (stdout line read in Rust then invoke/event, vs fixed port for spike).\n5. **Dev loop**: `pnpm tauri dev` behavior with Vite HMR; can the frontend ALSO run browser-only via plain `pnpm dev` against the daemon (no Tauri) for Playwright screenshots — any Tauri API imports that would break in a plain browser and the standard guard pattern.\n\nOutput: ≤120 lines, snippets in fenced blocks, each answer marked verified (context7/docs) vs inferred.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"tool_input_hash":"af23658f9085392ea8102fcfbe1e06dd5c2809f37358384b21c3a576dd0b16ff","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"Tauri scaffold + sidecar facts\",\"name\":\"explore-tauri-setup\",\"prompt\":\"Research task (read-only; use the context7 MCP tools — resolve-library-id then query-docs — against Tauri v2 ..."}
