{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:02:20.376517564Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"# Thin Slice: \"Real missions, real window\" — 8-hour spike plan (DRAFT)\n\n## Context\n\nDesk (new repo, `~/Coding/punt-labs/desk`) is the planned modular desktop\nworkspace; PLAN.md P1 calls for spikes before feature work. The operator\nwants an end-to-end thin slice in ~8 hours to validate the design:\nreal ethos data → daemon → Linear-styled UI → real Tauri window → agent\nscreenshot loop. Not production code. Constraints from the operator:\n\n- Use ethos missions + local code reviews for the work itself.\n- PRs may be merged only OFF the critical path; critical-path work stays on\n  a branch, unmerged.\n- UX must follow established patterns (no invention), user-focused, with\n  progressive disclosure.\n- Research tools: ethos, quarry, context7.\n\n## Research inputs (pending)\n\n- [ ] explore-ethos-cli: exact `--json` shapes, open-mission visibility,\n      mission-create mechanics in a fresh repo, global identity resolution,\n      `quick` pipeline stages.\n- [ ] explore-tauri-setup: create-tauri-app scaffold, Go sidecar config +\n      capability, localhost fetch policy, port/token handoff, browser-only\n      dev mode for Playwright shots.\n\n## Established UX patterns (no invention — named authorities)\n\n| Pattern | Authority | Where used |\n|---|---|---|\n| Master-detail with side peek | Linear (issue list + peek), macOS Mail | Missions list + detail panel |\n| Grouped dense list with status glyphs | Linear issue list | Missions default view |\n| Progressive disclosure | NN/g principle; GitHub \"Show more\"; Linear collapsed sections | Narrative first → Mechanics `\u003cdetails\u003e`; episodes → entries → raw |\n| Command palette | Linear/VS Code ⌘K | Deferred beyond spike (stub only) |\n| Attribution banding | GitHub blame commit bands | Deferred to Blame phase (not in slice) |\n\n## Skeleton (to be filled after research)\n\n1. Preconditions \u0026 setup (ethos enable in desk?, branch discipline)\n2. Mission breakdown (contracts, workers/evaluators, write-sets)\n3. Hour-by-hour schedule with dependency graph\n4. API contract for spike daemon (from verified CLI shapes)\n5. Screen scope (Missions list + peek; progressive disclosure mapping)\n6. Review gates (3 local review agents per slice)\n7. Verification \u0026 demo script\n8. Deliverables (running window, latency numbers, CLI-gaps list, spike\n   report appended to desk/PLAN.md §9)\n9. Out of scope\n","file_path":"~/.claude/plans/come-up-with-a-optimized-quilt.md"},"tool_input_hash":"fa75d71b5192f618339da73c1158e4e794a7c5d1ee626663dbe587eb9b3ee2f7","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"# Thin Slice: \\\"Real missions, real window\\\" — 8-hour spike plan (DRAFT)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nDesk (new repo, `~/Coding/punt-labs/desk`) is the planned modular desktop\\nworkspace; PLAN.md P1..."}
