{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:04:47.066682492Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/.claude/plans/come-up-with-a-optimized-quilt.md","new_string":"- [x] explore-tauri-setup (partial): VERIFIED — scaffold via\n      `pnpm create tauri-app desk --template react-ts --manager pnpm`\n      (Vite on 1420); Ubuntu deps incl. libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev; sidecar via\n      `pnpm tauri add shell` + `bundle.externalBin: [\"binaries/deskd\"]` +\n      target-triple-suffixed binary that MUST exist before `tauri dev`\n      (`deskd-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` under `src-tauri/binaries/`);\n      capability `shell:allow-execute` with `sidecar: true`; Rust-side spawn\n      in `.setup()` reads stdout for `{\"port\":...,\"token\":\"...\"}` line.\n      KEY RISK FOUND: webview origin on Linux is `http://tauri.localhost`\n      (not configurable) and WebKitGTK often sends empty/absent Origin —\n      so the daemon must send permissive-for-spike CORS headers\n      (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`-style) rather than an origin\n      allowlist. Awaiting tail: exact headers, token handoff choice,\n      browser-only mode guard pattern.","old_string":"- [ ] explore-tauri-setup: create-tauri-app scaffold, Go sidecar config +\n      capability, localhost fetch policy, port/token handoff, browser-only\n      dev mode for Playwright shots.","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"73f4864425009da7e8e0f6e5bb50a199cf2d405e1d0ecfba2d6bdcd67f612c55","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.claude/plans/come-up-with-a-optimized-quilt.md\",\"new_string\":\"- [x] explore-tauri-setup (partial): VERIFIED — scaffold via\\n      `pnpm create tauri-app desk --template react-ts --m..."}
