{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:05:31.772356867Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/.claude/plans/come-up-with-a-optimized-quilt.md","new_string":"      capability `shell:allow-execute` with `sidecar: true`; Rust-side spawn\n      in `.setup()` reads stdout for `{\"port\":...,\"token\":\"...\"}` line.\n      SETTLED DECISIONS from the report:\n      (a) CORS not CSP is the localhost-fetch blocker (webview origin\n      `http://tauri.localhost`, not configurable; WebKitGTK often sends\n      empty Origin) → daemon emits `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`,\n      `-Headers: authorization, content-type`, `-Methods: GET, POST,\n      OPTIONS`, answers OPTIONS 204; token rides the Authorization header\n      (never a cookie; `*` incompatible with credentials). Plain fetch();\n      NO tauri http plugin (it would break the browser-only path).\n      (b) Port/token handoff: managed state + `daemon_info` #[tauri::command]\n      filled by the stdout parser; frontend `invoke` with short retry.\n      No emit-from-setup (race). ~30 lines.\n      (c) Browser-only mode for Playwright: `pnpm dev` + `VITE_DESKD_URL`/\n      `VITE_DESKD_TOKEN` env; Tauri API only behind `isTauri` guard with\n      dynamic import so the browser path never evaluates it.\n\n- [x] explore-ethos-cli (partial, tail pending): installed binary 4.15.0 vs\n      checkout 4.16.1 → daemon pins binary path and asserts `ethos version`\n      at startup. VERIFIED SHAPES: `mission show \u003cid\u003e --json` is the fat\n      object and embeds full `results[]` (prose + open_questions) — one\n      call serves the whole detail panel. `find missions --format json` =\n      rich JSONL but CLOSED-only (missions.jsonl); `mission list --json`\n      defaults to open-only and is thin (6 fields; key `mission_id` vs\n      find's `id` — field-name mismatch, goes on the gaps list).\n      `mission results --json` works (structured files_changed).\n      `mission log --json` is coarse (2–3 events/mission) — timeline UI\n      must not promise granularity the data lacks. `identity list --json`\n      thin (no email/github; use `identity get`); `session --json` = live\n      roster, the one real-time surface.\n      DAEMON DESIGN IMPLICATION: /api/missions = merge(find-missions JSONL\n      for closed ∪ mission-list --status all for open, with show fan-out\n      for the few open ones); /api/missions/{id} = show (+ log; + prompt.md\n      file read pending contradiction resolution).\n      OPEN: prompt.md existence contradiction (prior survey saw\n      delegations/\u003cdid\u003e/prompt.md on disk; this agent grepped only\n      internal/mission) — resolution requested; also pending: fresh-repo\n      mission-create mechanics, global identity resolution, quick pipeline.","old_string":"      capability `shell:allow-execute` with `sidecar: true`; Rust-side spawn\n      in `.setup()` reads stdout for `{\"port\":...,\"token\":\"...\"}` line.\n      KEY RISK FOUND: webview origin on Linux is `http://tauri.localhost`\n      (not configurable) and WebKitGTK often sends empty/absent Origin —\n      so the daemon must send permissive-for-spike CORS headers\n      (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`-style) rather than an origin\n      allowlist. Awaiting tail: exact headers, token handoff choice,\n      browser-only mode guard pattern.","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"afee406925627583bd39c5926baec623c8c7bda79c08a682e8c1a2d990c32dc3","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.claude/plans/come-up-with-a-optimized-quilt.md\",\"new_string\":\"      capability `shell:allow-execute` with `sidecar: true`; Rust-side spawn\\n      in `.setup()` reads stdout for `{\\\"po..."}
