{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:06:01.257093034Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/.claude/plans/come-up-with-a-optimized-quilt.md","new_string":"      RESOLVED: prompt.md EXISTS — 98 on disk at\n      missions/\u003cmid\u003e/delegations/\u003cdid\u003e/prompt.md, written by\n      internal/hook/pretooluse_dispatch.go → delegation.go (prompt first,\n      then record.yaml; redacted before write; prompt_hash in record).\n      REVISED GAPS (daemon must read FS, precedent = internal/ui does):\n      artifacts/ (16 dirs, no CLI read), delegations discovery (no\n      `delegation list`; enumerate dirs), prompt.md content. Result prose +\n      open_questions ARE CLI-reachable.\n      OPEN-MISSION TRUTH: `mission list --status all` = 125 authoritative\n      (repo ∪ global, repo-wins); bare `mission list` defaults to\n      --status open ([] here reads as empty store — daemon must pass\n      --status all); missions.jsonl = 105 closed-only.\n      FRESH-REPO CREATE: works with just `git init` (nothing consults the\n      enabled marker); minimal contract = leader, worker,\n      evaluator{handle}≠worker, write_set[≥1], success_criteria[≥1],\n      budget{rounds 1-10, reflection_after_each}; `ethos mission scaffold\n      contract` generates it. `ethos enable` (optional, later) deposits\n      guide+hooks; does NOT create identities.\n      PENDING (tail): global identity resolution for fresh repo; quick\n      pipeline stages.","old_string":"      OPEN: prompt.md existence contradiction (prior survey saw\n      delegations/\u003cdid\u003e/prompt.md on disk; this agent grepped only\n      internal/mission) — resolution requested; also pending: fresh-repo\n      mission-create mechanics, global identity resolution, quick pipeline.","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"47dbe944d994728d05acdb1c9ccd22368c80c7eab5e80d4ed5bcc43cf4178f68","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.claude/plans/come-up-with-a-optimized-quilt.md\",\"new_string\":\"      RESOLVED: prompt.md EXISTS — 98 on disk at\\n      missions/\\u003cmid\\u003e/delegations/\\u003cdid\\u003e/prompt.md,..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:08:25.617167257Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"# Thin Slice: \"Real missions, real window\" — 8-hour spike plan\n\n## Context\n\nDesk (`~/Coding/punt-labs/desk`, new repo, no remote) is the modular desktop\nworkspace planned in `desk/PLAN.md`; its P1 calls for spikes before feature\nwork. The operator wants an end-to-end thin slice in ~8 hours validating the\ndesign: **this ethos repo's real mission data (125 missions) → a Go bridge\ndaemon shelling out to the `ethos --json` CLI → the Linear-styled Missions UI\n→ a real Tauri window on the operator's desktop → agent-screenshot loop\nthroughout.** Explicitly not production code. Operator constraints: work runs\nas ethos missions with local code reviews; critical-path work stays on an\nunmerged branch (PR merges allowed only off critical path); UX follows\nestablished patterns only, user-focused, progressive disclosure.\n\nAll schedule-relevant facts below were verified this session by three\nresearch agents (ethos CLI shapes, fresh-repo mission mechanics, Tauri 2\nscaffold/sidecar/CORS/dev-loop).\n\n## What this slice validates (exit questions)\n\n1. Does \"GUI features are CLI features with pixels\" survive literal contact —\n   can the UI be fed almost entirely by `ethos --json` + minimal FS reads?\n2. Does real data (125 missions, long criteria, weird states) break the\n   Linear list+peek design that fake data validated?\n3. Is exec-per-request fast enough for the zero-spinner bar (S2's daemon-vs-\n   exec question, answered with numbers)?\n4. Does the Tauri sidecar model work on this machine (spawn, port/token\n   handoff, webview fetch)?\n5. Can agents build UI end-to-end using the screenshot loop as their eyes?\n\n## Established UX patterns (mandate: no invention)\n\n| Pattern | Authority | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| Master-detail, side peek | Linear issue peek; macOS Mail | Missions list + detail panel |\n| Grouped dense list, status glyphs | Linear | Missions default view |\n| Progressive disclosure (3 levels) | NN/g principle; Linear collapsed sections; GitHub `\u003cdetails\u003e` | L1 row → L2 peek narrative (ask, result prose, criteria, timeline) → L3 collapsed \"Mechanics\" (hashes, budget, write-set, IDs) |\n| Skeleton-free instant loads | Linear (local sync) | All-local daemon; latency budget enforced |\n| Keyboard list nav (j/k, enter) | Linear/Vim convention | Stretch; ⌘K stubbed only |\n\nNot in slice: Blame (needs S1), Audit episodes, board/lanes views.\n\n## Repo/branch/process discipline\n\n- All work in `desk` on branch **`spike/thin-slice`** — critical path ⇒\n  branch stays **unmerged** (operator rule). Commits land there\n  continuously; mission records (`.punt-labs/ethos/missions/`) commit with\n  the work. No remote, no PRs on this path. The ethos repo is untouched\n  (its `chore/doc-hygiene` branch stays parked).\n- Missions are created **in the desk repo** — verified: `mission create`\n  needs only `git init` (no `ethos enable`); identities (bwk/adb/rmh/mdm/\n  rsc/kth/edt/dna…) resolve from the global store (35 identities; layered\n  resolution when `resolution:` is absent). `ethos enable` deliberately\n  deferred to P1-proper.\n- Contracts via `ethos mission scaffold contract` → `.tmp/missions/*.yaml`\n  → `ethos mission create --file` → spawn worker via `Agent(subagent_type,\n  background)` — dispatch is two operations. Every contract carries the\n  commit-per-step criterion. Spike quality gates (no Makefile ceremony):\n  `gofmt`/`go vet` for Go, `tsc --noEmit` + prettier for TS.\n\n## Missions (4) — disjoint write-sets, overlap-safe creation order\n\nCreated at T0 (disjoint): M1, M2, M3. M4 created only after M2 closes\n(its write-set is inside M2's, and overlap checks apply to open missions\nonly — verified).\n\n### M1 — `deskd` bridge daemon · worker **bwk**, evaluator **rsc**\n\nWrite-set: `spike/deskd/**`. Go, stdlib-only.\nEndpoints (all `Authorization: Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e`, CORS: `Access-Control-\nAllow-Origin: *`, `-Headers: authorization, content-type`, `-Methods: GET,\nPOST, OPTIONS`, OPTIONS→204 — token in header, never cookie):\n\n- `GET /api/missions` — union: `ethos find missions --format json` (closed,\n  rich JSONL) ∪ `ethos mission list --json --status all` (authoritative\n  125; NEVER bare `mission list` — it defaults to open-only) with\n  `mission show --json` fan-out for open ones. Normalize the verified\n  `id` vs `mission_id` field mismatch.\n- `GET /api/missions/{id}` — `mission show --json` (embeds full results:\n  prose, open_questions) + `mission log --json` + FS reads for the CLI\n  gaps: `delegations/\u003cdid\u003e/prompt.md` (98 exist; enumerate dirs — no\n  `delegation list` command; precedent: `internal/ui` reads FS directly)\n  and `artifacts/` listing (16 dirs).\n- `GET /api/identities` (`identity list --json`), `GET /api/session`\n  (`session --json` — the live roster).\n- Startup: `--repo \u003cpath\u003e` + `--token` or generated; first stdout line\n  `{\"port\":N,\"token\":\"...\"}`; pin ethos binary path, assert\n  `ethos version` (installed 4.15.0 ≠ checkout 4.16.1 — log it).\n- **Latency log**: one line per request — endpoint, CLI cmd(s), ms each,\n  total ms. This IS the S2 measurement.\n\n### M2 — Tauri shell + shot rig · worker **adb**, evaluator **kth**\n\nWrite-set: `apps/desk/**`, `tools/shot/**`, `Makefile`, `.gitignore`.\nVerified recipe: `pnpm create tauri-app desk --template react-ts --manager\npnpm` (Vite:1420) → `pnpm tauri add shell` → build deskd to\n`src-tauri/binaries/deskd-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` (must exist before\n`tauri dev`; `beforeDevCommand` builds it) → capability\n`shell:allow-execute` with `sidecar: true` → `.setup()` spawns sidecar,\nparses stdout line into managed state → `daemon_info` command (no\nemit-from-setup race; frontend invokes with short retry). Scaffold `src/`\ncommitted as-generated, then untouched (M4 owns it). `make shot\nSCREEN=\u003croute\u003e`: boots deskd + `pnpm dev`, Playwright (reuse installed\n`.tmp/shotkit` Chromium) → PNG. `make dev` = `pnpm tauri dev`.\n\n### M3 — Missions UI kit (fixture-driven) · worker **edt**, evaluator **dna**\n\nWrite-set: `spike/ui/**`. Plain Vite sandbox; step 1 captures fixture JSON\nfrom the real CLI (`ethos mission show/find/list` outputs → `spike/ui/\nfixtures/`). Builds the Linear-pattern components per the mockup\n(`desk/mockups/ethos-desktop-mockup.html` is the visual spec): grouped\nlist + status glyphs, peek panel with L2 narrative (the ask from\nprompt.md, result prose, criteria, coarse timeline — log has only 2–3\nevents/mission, verified; the UI must not fake granularity) and L3\n`\u003cdetails\u003e` Mechanics. TanStack Query + Tailwind v4. **Screenshot evidence\nrequired in the mission result** (`make shot`-style rig or vite+playwright\ndirectly). dna evaluates the mental model; edt the density/hierarchy.\n\n### M4 — Integration · worker **edt**, evaluator **dna** (created after M2 closes)\n\nWrite-set: `apps/desk/src/**`. Port spike/ui components into the app;\ndaemon client with the verified `isTauri` guard (dynamic\n`@tauri-apps/api/core` import; browser path uses `VITE_DESKD_URL/TOKEN`) so\n`pnpm dev` stays Playwright-drivable. Real-data pass: all 125 missions\nrender; empty/missing fields handled visibly, not blankly.\n\n## Hour-by-hour\n\n| Hour | Track |\n|---|---|\n| 0–0.5 | Leader: branch, contracts, create+dispatch M1/M2/M3; **operator action: run the apt deps install** (webkit2gtk-4.1 etc. — needs sudo; fallback if blocked: browser-only demo, degraded exit) |\n| 0.5–2.5 | M1 ∥ M2 ∥ M3 run in background; leader monitors via filesystem, captures interim shots |\n| 2.5–3 | M1/M2/M3 results + close; create+dispatch M4 |\n| 3–5 | M4 integration; leader drives `make shot` iterations against real data; SSE/fs-watch stretch ONLY if ahead here |\n| 5–6 | End-to-end in the Tauri window; latency numbers off the daemon log vs zero-spinner bar; real-data findings list |\n| 6–7 | Local reviews on the full branch diff: `code-reviewer`, `silent-failure-hunter`, `invariant-completeness-reviewer`; fix critical findings, log the rest as spike debt |\n| 7–8 | Demo to operator (Phase-3-style confirmation in the running window); spike report appended to `desk/PLAN.md` §9 (results, latency table, CLI-gaps list, design verdicts); final commit |\n\n## Verification (end of slice)\n\n1. `make dev` on the operator's machine → native window, sidecar-spawned\n   daemon, real missions listed, peek shows a real prompt.md ask + result\n   prose, Mechanics collapses. Operator clicks through and confirms.\n2. `make shot SCREEN=missions` → PNG; agent reads it back (loop proof).\n3. Daemon latency log: p50/p95 per endpoint vs the \u003c50 ms interaction bar\n   (list may exec 2 CLIs; peek 2–3 + FS reads) — recorded either way; this\n   answers daemon-vs-exec with data.\n4. Review agents' findings addressed or logged.\n5. Deliverables in repo: spike code, mission records with results +\n   screenshot evidence, updated PLAN.md §9 spike report.\n\n## Out of scope (spike)\n\nAuth beyond bearer token, tests beyond smoke, Blame/Audit/Team screens,\nboard/lanes views, ⌘K (visual stub only), packaging/signing, SSE (stretch),\n`ethos enable` in desk, any merge of `spike/thin-slice`.\n\n## Known risks \u0026 fallbacks\n\n- **sudo apt deps** — operator-gated; fallback: browser-only end-to-end\n  (daemon + Vite + Playwright), Tauri window deferred to next session.\n- **Ethos binary lag (4.15.0)** — daemon asserts version; if a 4.16.x\n  surface is required, operator runs `make install` from a shell (never\n  self-install from Claude Code).\n- **Exec latency misses the bar** — that's a valid spike RESULT, not a\n  failure: it argues for the linked-daemon path in S2-proper.\n- **Pipeline-instantiate partial-persist caveat** (verified) — we use\n  individual `mission create --file`, not `pipeline instantiate`, so the\n  sequential-persist trap doesn't apply.\n","file_path":"~/.claude/plans/come-up-with-a-optimized-quilt.md"},"tool_input_hash":"9edef009be429173bfc82d1445d9b3ca068c79813e455267e881f46fc9de9072","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"# Thin Slice: \\\"Real missions, real window\\\" — 8-hour spike plan\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nDesk (`~/Coding/punt-labs/desk`, new repo, no remote) is the modular desktop\\nworkspace planned in `desk..."}
