{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:10:47.508003423Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"M1: build deskd bridge daemon","name":"worker-deskd","prompt":"You are the worker on ethos mission m-2026-09-11-005. First: cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice — verify with git branch, do NOT switch branches) and run `ethos mission show m-2026-09-11-005` for your contract.\n\nBuild the spike bridge daemon at spike/deskd/ (Go, stdlib only, go.mod module deskd). This is spike-grade code validating a design, not production — bias to working software fast, but keep it clean (gofmt, go vet).\n\nKey facts verified for you:\n- Data source: the SIBLING repo \u003crepo\u003e (pass as --repo flag). Shell out to the `ethos` binary at ~/.local/bin/ethos with cwd set to that repo. Assert `ethos version` at startup and log it (installed is 4.15.0).\n- `ethos mission list --json` DEFAULTS TO OPEN-ONLY — always pass --status all (returns ~125 entries, thin 6-field objects, key \"mission_id\"). `ethos find missions --format json` emits rich JSONL for CLOSED missions only (key \"id\" — normalize to one field name in your API). Merge strategy: find-missions rows are authoritative for closed; list-all rows not present there are open → fan out `ethos mission show \u003cid\u003e --json` for those few to enrich.\n- `mission show \u003cid\u003e --json` embeds contract + full results[] (prose, open_questions). `mission log \u003cid\u003e --json` gives events (only 2-3 per mission).\n- CLI gaps you must read from the FS under \u003crepo\u003e/.punt-labs/ethos/missions/\u003cmid\u003e/: delegations/\u003cdid\u003e/prompt.md (enumerate delegation dirs; no CLI for this) and artifacts/ file listing.\n- HTTP: bind 127.0.0.1, random port; generate a token; FIRST stdout line must be exactly one JSON line {\"port\":N,\"token\":\"...\"} then flush. Require Authorization: Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e on /api/*. CORS on every response: Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *, Access-Control-Allow-Headers: authorization, content-type, Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, POST, OPTIONS; answer OPTIONS with 204 (no auth check on OPTIONS). Token must never be a cookie.\n- Endpoints: GET /api/missions (merged list, sorted newest first), GET /api/missions/{id} (show + log + prompt_md excerpts per delegation + artifacts names), GET /api/identities (`identity list --json`), GET /api/session (`session --json`; if it errors outside a session, return {\"participants\":[]}).\n- Latency: log one line per request to stderr: METHOD path total_ms [cli_cmd=ms ...]. Add a simple in-process cache for /api/missions (30s TTL) but log both cold and cached timings — the cold numbers are the spike's measurement.\n\nDefinition of done: `go run ./spike/deskd --repo ../ethos` prints the port/token line; curl with the token returns real mission JSON for all four endpoints; gofmt+go vet clean; committed incrementally on spike/thin-slice (one commit per logical step, never switch branches). Then submit a mission result: check `ethos mission result --help` for the submission command shape and submit a result with verdict, what works, latency observations (paste a few log lines), and any CLI-surface gaps you hit. Report the same in your final message.","subagent_type":"bwk"},"tool_input_hash":"3e126ce08f41ddb647973fa6d4dad24d097695e85442a8b70b1017075cee858f","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"M1: build deskd bridge daemon\",\"name\":\"worker-deskd\",\"prompt\":\"You are the worker on ethos mission m-2026-09-11-005. First: cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice — veri..."}
