{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:10:59.851713245Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"M2: Tauri shell + shot rig","name":"worker-shell","prompt":"You are the worker on ethos mission m-2026-09-11-006. First: cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice — verify, never switch) and run `ethos mission show m-2026-09-11-006` for your contract.\n\nBuild the Tauri 2 shell + screenshot rig. Spike-grade, working fast beats perfect. Verified recipe — follow it:\n\n1. Check system deps directly (dpkg -l | grep webkit2gtk). Required Ubuntu packages: libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev build-essential libxdo-dev libssl-dev libayatana-appindicator3-dev librsvg2-dev. You CANNOT sudo — if missing, note it prominently in your result and proceed with everything that doesn't need a webview build (scaffold, config, Rust code, Makefile, shot rig against plain vite).\n2. Scaffold: from apps/: `pnpm create tauri-app desk --template react-ts --manager pnpm` (answer the identifier prompt e.g. com.puntlabs.desk, or patch tauri.conf.json after; check the create command's --help for non-interactive flags). cd apps/desk \u0026\u0026 pnpm install. Vite dev server is on 1420.\n3. `pnpm tauri add shell`.\n4. Sidecar: the daemon is being built in parallel at spike/deskd (Go). Add a package.json script build:daemon: `go build -o src-tauri/binaries/deskd-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu ../../spike/deskd` — if spike/deskd doesn't compile yet, create a tiny placeholder Go main (own dir tools/shot/stub/) that prints {\"port\":0,\"token\":\"stub\"}\\n and sleeps forever, build THAT to the triple-suffixed path so tauri dev can start; swap to the real daemon when it lands (watch for spike/deskd/*.go appearing on the branch). The triple-suffixed binary MUST exist before `tauri dev` runs. Wire beforeDevCommand: \"pnpm build:daemon \u0026\u0026 pnpm dev\".\n5. tauri.conf.json: bundle.externalBin: [\"binaries/deskd\"]. Capability in src-tauri/capabilities/default.json: add {\"identifier\":\"shell:allow-execute\",\"allow\":[{\"name\":\"binaries/deskd\",\"sidecar\":true,\"args\":true}]} alongside core:default.\n6. src-tauri/src/lib.rs .setup(): app.shell().sidecar(\"deskd\") → spawn with args [\"--repo\",\"\u003crepo\u003e\"], read CommandEvent::Stdout lines, parse first JSON line {\"port\":N,\"token\":\"...\"} into a managed Mutex\u003cOption\u003cDaemonInfo\u003e\u003e; expose #[tauri::command] fn daemon_info(...) returning it. Do NOT emit events from setup (race).\n7. Commit the scaffolded src/ AS GENERATED, then never touch src/ again — mission m-2026-09-11-007's owner takes it over.\n8. Repo-root Makefile: `make dev` = cd apps/desk \u0026\u0026 pnpm tauri dev; `make shot` = SCREEN=\u003croute\u003e boots deskd (go run, capture port/token from stdout) + pnpm dev, then a Playwright screenshot via the node install at \u003crepo\u003e/.tmp/shotkit (chromium already downloaded there; invoke its npx playwright screenshot, pass VITE_DESKD_URL/VITE_DESKD_TOKEN env into pnpm dev) writing .tmp/shots/\u003cscreen\u003e.png in desk. tools/shot/ for helper scripts. Also .gitignore: node_modules, target, .tmp, src-tauri/binaries/*.\n9. Verify: `pnpm tauri dev` opens a window (if system deps exist) with the scaffold app and the sidecar spawns (stub or real). `make shot SCREEN=/` produces a PNG. Paste command output as evidence.\n\nCommit incrementally on spike/thin-slice, one commit per logical step. Then submit a mission result (`ethos mission result --help` for the shape) with verdict, what works, what's blocked (esp. system deps), and evidence. Report the same in your final message.","subagent_type":"adb"},"tool_input_hash":"9ecc80a07cc9df4aabd99dba686f0645f37445982500248ba35db6bf3ccab2f1","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"M2: Tauri shell + shot rig\",\"name\":\"worker-shell\",\"prompt\":\"You are the worker on ethos mission m-2026-09-11-006. First: cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice — verify,..."}
