{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:11:12.028901034Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"M3: Missions UI kit on fixtures","name":"worker-ui","prompt":"You are the worker on ethos mission m-2026-09-11-007. First: cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice — verify, never switch) and run `ethos mission show m-2026-09-11-007` for your contract.\n\nBuild the Missions UI kit at spike/ui/ — a plain Vite React-TS sandbox (pnpm create vite . --template react-ts inside spike/ui, then pnpm install; add Tailwind v4). Fixture-driven: NO daemon dependency. Spike-grade but this is the DESIGN CENTERPIECE — visual quality matters most.\n\nStep 1 — capture real fixtures (read-only commands, run with cwd \u003crepo\u003e):\n- `ethos find missions --format json` → fixtures/find-missions.jsonl\n- `ethos mission list --json --status all` → fixtures/mission-list.json\n- `ethos mission show \u003cid\u003e --json` for 3 diverse missions (pick from the JSONL: one multi-round with a fail round, one single-round pass, one with open_questions) → fixtures/show-\u003cid\u003e.json\n- `ethos mission log \u003cid\u003e --json` for the same 3 → fixtures/log-\u003cid\u003e.json\n- Copy 2 real prompt.md files from .punt-labs/ethos/missions/*/delegations/*/prompt.md → fixtures/\nAll saved under ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/ui/fixtures/.\n\nStep 2 — build the screen. The visual spec is ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/mockups/ethos-desktop-mockup.html — screenshot it first (chromium is installed at \u003crepo\u003e/.tmp/shotkit: from that dir, npx playwright screenshot --viewport-size=1720,1000 \"file://~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/mockups/ethos-desktop-mockup.html\" out.png) and Read the PNG to study the Missions screen. Reproduce that design in real React components fed by the REAL fixtures:\n- Linear-pattern grouped dense list (status glyph, mono short-id, title, right-aligned meta, avatar initials), grouped by status; master-detail with side peek panel (Linear / macOS Mail pattern).\n- Progressive disclosure, 3 levels (NN/g): L1 = the row. L2 = peek narrative: \"The ask\" (prompt.md content, quoted), \"What came back\" (result prose + verdict + confidence), success criteria, open_questions when present, coarse timeline (2-3 events — render honestly, no fake granularity). L3 = collapsed \u003cdetails\u003e \"Mechanics\": write-set, budget/rounds, evaluator+hash, ticket, raw ids.\n- Real-data honesty: missions with no results, no prompt.md, or empty criteria render visible \"not recorded\" affordances — never blank gaps.\n- Dark theme default matching the mockup tokens (#08090a ground, #5e6ad2 accent family). Keyboard j/k + enter selection if cheap.\n- Established patterns ONLY — no invented idioms; when in doubt copy the mockup/Linear.\n\nStep 3 — the loop: screenshot your running vite app with the same playwright chromium, READ the PNG, fix what looks wrong, repeat at least twice. Final shots under spike/ui/shots/, referenced in your result.\n\ntsc --noEmit clean. Commit incrementally on spike/thin-slice, one commit per logical step. Then submit a mission result (`ethos mission result --help` for the shape) with verdict, screenshots referenced, and design findings from real data (long titles, weird states, missing fields). Report the same in your final message.","subagent_type":"edt"},"tool_input_hash":"2b625b5dbdb92d52af2d02a2b6eacc1769b6686f7efa9b6aa6e78b168f68f7fd","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"M3: Missions UI kit on fixtures\",\"name\":\"worker-ui\",\"prompt\":\"You are the worker on ethos mission m-2026-09-11-007. First: cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice — verif..."}
