{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:11:26.728491331Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"---\nname: bias-to-real-work\ndescription: Operator feedback — build real things; don't burn time/money on process hygiene and meta-work\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nDuring the desk thin-slice spike (2026-09-11), the operator interrupted:\n\"Make sure you do real work and not waste all of our time and money on\nhygiene. Seems to be your new thing.\"\n\n**Why:** Sessions had drifted toward process output — plan polish, extra\ncritique passes, ceremony around dispatching — while the deliverable (working\nsoftware) waited. The operator pays for tokens and time; meta-work reads as\nwaste.\n\n**How to apply:** Default to building. Dispatch workers early and in\nparallel; skip optional self-critique/fork-review passes on spike-grade\nwork; keep plan documents short and stop editing them once ratified; do\nhygiene (lint fixes, doc tidying, memory writes) in the gaps while workers\nrun, never as the main thread. When choosing between another review round\nand shipping the next increment, ship.\n","file_path":"~/.claude/projects/-home-jfreeman-Coding-punt-labs-ethos/memory/bias-to-real-work.md"},"tool_input_hash":"ca2be2dca488a7656379aa517c633f4a34cf5609018d33ddc94863eb496496f4","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"---\\nname: bias-to-real-work\\ndescription: Operator feedback — build real things; don't burn time/money on process hygiene and meta-work\\nmetadata:\\n  type: feedback\\n---\\n\\nDuring the d..."}
