{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:19:41.380045304Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git add spike/deskd/identity.go spike/deskd/.gitignore \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nspike(deskd): treat non-JSON `session --json` output as no session\n\n`ethos session --json` prints the plain-text line \"No active session.\"\nwith exit 0 (not an error, not JSON) when run from a process outside\nany tracked session -- which is deskd's own case, since its ethos\ncalls run from a detached daemon process. Guard on json.Valid, not\njust the exec error, so the fallback {\"participants\":[]} response\nstill fires.\n\nAlso ignore the local build artifact.\nEOF\n)\" -- spike/deskd/identity.go spike/deskd/.gitignore","description":"Commit session JSON-gap fix and gitignore"},"tool_input_hash":"d1c109f1934d48f7409e98913c09a87d4b1224a42777bfc721b86cddec0c05e8","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git add spike/deskd/identity.go spike/deskd/.gitignore \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"$(cat \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\nspike(deskd): treat non-JSON `session -..."}
