{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:29:51.856119176Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/.tmp\nfor i in 1 2 3 4 5 6; do\n  ./deskd-shot --repo \u003crepo\u003e --addr 127.0.0.1 \u003e /tmp/o$i.log 2\u003e /tmp/e$i.log \u0026\n  PID=$!\n  sleep 3\n  if [[ -s /tmp/o$i.log ]]; then\n    echo \"run $i: OK pid=$PID\"\n    kill $PID 2\u003e/dev/null\n  else\n    echo \"run $i: HUNG pid=$PID -- inspecting\"\n    ps --forest -o pid,ppid,stat,wchan:32,cmd -g $(ps -o pgid= -p $PID) 2\u003e\u00261\n    cat /proc/$PID/status 2\u003e\u00261 | grep -E \"State|PPid\"\n    ls -la /proc/$PID/fd 2\u003e\u00261 | head -20\n    kill $PID 2\u003e/dev/null\n    break\n  fi\ndone","description":"Reproduce the hang and inspect process state while stuck","timeout":40000},"tool_input_hash":"6b9ccb29fbe0066303687b808c0d406fa070c5feccfebdda630016b8cc96edfc","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/.tmp\\nfor i in 1 2 3 4 5 6; do\\n  ./deskd-shot --repo \\u003crepo\\u003e --addr 127.0.0.1 \\u003e /tmp/o$i.log 2\\u003e /tmp/e$i.log \\u0026\\n  PID=$!\\n  sl..."}
