{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:30:26.282292522Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# tools/rust-local/install.sh — extract a Rust toolchain from apt's .deb\n# packages into $HOME/.local/rust-apt/root, without `apt install` (no root)\n# and without reaching rustup.rs (this host's sandbox denies raw curl/wget;\n# `apt-get download` and `cargo`'s registry fetch are the two egress paths\n# that are actually permitted).\n#\n# Ubuntu 24.04's rustc/cargo package is 1.75.0. That is NOT new enough to\n# build Tauri 2's current dependency tree — `cargo check` on the scaffolded\n# desk app fails with:\n#   error: package `dlopen2_derive v0.4.3` requires the Cargo feature\n#   `edition2024`, which is not stabilized until rustc ~1.85.\n# (dlopen2_derive is pulled in by `tao`, Tauri's windowing crate.) This\n# script exists so a Rust-shaped hole in the sandbox doesn't block writing\n# and syntax-checking Rust code, not to claim it fully unblocks `cargo\n# build`. See the m-2026-09-11-006 mission result for the full story.\n#\n# Idempotent: re-running is a no-op once the toolchain is present.\nset -euo pipefail\n\nPREFIX=\"${RUST_LOCAL_PREFIX:-$HOME/.local/rust-apt}\"\nROOT=\"$PREFIX/root\"\nPKGS=\"$PREFIX/pkgs\"\n\nif [[ -x \"$ROOT/usr/bin/cargo\" ]]; then\n  echo \"rust-local: already installed at $ROOT\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n\nmkdir -p \"$PKGS\" \"$ROOT\"\n\n# rustc/cargo plus every runtime lib their apt packages depend on that\n# Ubuntu doesn't already ship by default (checked against a stock\n# noble desktop install; adjust if a future base image differs):\n#   - libstd-rust-1.75 / libstd-rust-dev: the actual rustc/std bits\n#   - libgit2-1.7, libssh2-1t64: cargo's registry/git support\n#   - libllvm17t64: rustc's codegen backend\n#   - libhttp-parser2.9: transitively required by cargo\nPACKAGES=(\n  rustc cargo\n  libstd-rust-1.75 libstd-rust-dev\n  libgit2-1.7 libssh2-1t64\n  libllvm17t64 libhttp-parser2.9\n)\n\necho \"rust-local: downloading ${PACKAGES[*]}\"\n(cd \"$PKGS\" \u0026\u0026 apt-get download \"${PACKAGES[@]}\")\n\necho \"rust-local: extracting into $ROOT\"\nfor deb in \"$PKGS\"/*.deb; do\n  dpkg-deb -x \"$deb\" \"$ROOT\"\ndone\n\necho \"rust-local: done. Add to PATH/LD_LIBRARY_PATH with:\"\necho \"  export PATH=\\\"$ROOT/usr/bin:\\$PATH\\\"\"\necho \"  export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\\\"$ROOT/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu:\\$LD_LIBRARY_PATH\\\"\"\n\"$ROOT/usr/bin/rustc\" --version\n\"$ROOT/usr/bin/cargo\" --version\n","file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/tools/rust-local/install.sh"},"tool_input_hash":"9a6fcc168475c09b8d7ba591da41149d6bc1088601e5ea6452b5f11772cb3e7c","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# tools/rust-local/install.sh — extract a Rust toolchain from apt's .deb\\n# packages into $HOME/.local/rust-apt/root, without `apt install` (no root)\\n# and without ..."}
