{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:31:01.848431495Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"build: make dev / make shot + the screenshot rig\n\nmake dev: pnpm tauri dev (needs a webview toolchain + Rust \u003e=~1.85 —\nneither present here, see mission result for m-2026-09-11-006).\nmake shot SCREEN=\u003croute\u003e: tools/shot/shot.sh builds the real deskd\nsidecar (spike/deskd), boots it, boots vite on :1420 with\nVITE_DESKD_URL/VITE_DESKD_TOKEN, screenshots the route with the\nPlaywright install at ethos/.tmp/shotkit, and tears both processes\ndown on exit (trap, not best-effort). Poll budgets are 30s, not 10s:\ndeskd's startup path shells out to \\`ethos version\\` and can queue\nbehind another concurrent agent's ethos session-store lock on this\nshared host.\n\ntools/rust-local/install.sh: extracts a portable Rust 1.75 toolchain\nfrom apt's .deb packages (no root, no rustup.rs — this sandbox's\negress allowlist covers apt and cargo's registry but not raw\ncurl/wget) into ~/.local/rust-apt/root. Documented as infra-as-code\nsince it's the only way this environment produces a rustc/cargo at\nall, even though 1.75 turns out to be too old for Tauri 2's tao/dlopen2\ndependency chain (needs edition2024, stabilized ~1.85) — used here to\nwrite and syntax-check the sidecar Rust code, not to fully build it.\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -10","description":"Commit Makefile and shot/rust-local tooling"},"tool_input_hash":"9e4cc8697cfe9cf13f7f1859ebaaebcdffb0b190869342e49ebf1bb382435e71","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"build: make dev / make shot + the screenshot rig\\n\\nmake dev: pnpm tauri dev (needs a webview toolchain + Rust \\u003e=~1.85 —\\nnei..."}
