{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:32:27.395655531Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Contract amended — m-2026-09-11-006's write_set n…","message":"Contract amended — m-2026-09-11-006's write_set now covers .gitignore, Makefile, apps/desk/**, tools/** (leader edit of contract.yaml, noted for the spike report; root cause was the dispatch CLI treating repeated --write-set flags as override-not-append). Submit your result now. Include in it: what works, the system-deps situation (did `pnpm tauri dev` actually open a window on this machine, or is webkit missing?), and whether `make shot` produced a PNG.","recipient":"worker-shell","summary":"Write-set widened; submit your result","to":"worker-shell","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"17be923e39b496ac265f9b2fa865b248f9c4c01c354f20285f2f36590c4c543d","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Contract amended — m-2026-09-11-006's write_set n…\",\"message\":\"Contract amended — m-2026-09-11-006's write_set now covers .gitignore, Makefile, apps/desk/**, tools/** (leader edit of..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:32:31.004571139Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"# Fixtures\n\nAll files here are unmodified output of real `ethos` CLI commands, run\nread-only against the `ethos` repo's live mission store (plus one live\nmission from this very `desk` repo — see below). Nothing is hand-edited or\nsynthesized.\n\n| File | Command |\n|---|---|\n| `find-missions.jsonl` | `ethos find missions --format json` (run from `ethos` repo) |\n| `mission-list.json` | `ethos mission list --json --status all` (run from `ethos` repo) |\n| `show-\u003cid\u003e.json` | `ethos mission show \u003cid\u003e --json` |\n| `log-\u003cid\u003e.json` | `ethos mission log \u003cid\u003e --json` |\n| `prompts/*.md` | Copied verbatim from `\u003cmission\u003e/delegations/\u003cid\u003e/prompt.md` |\n\n## Chosen missions\n\nThree real missions were selected for full-depth (`show`+`log`) capture,\ncovering the most diverse states actually present in the local store:\n\n- **`m-2026-07-21-001`** — 3-round pass, rich per-round reflection prose\n  including a genuine deferred-scope (\"open question\") passage in round 1.\n  Has a captured `prompt.md`.\n- **`m-2026-07-11-004`** — single-round administrative fail (mission\n  abandoned, closed as failed during a freeze reconciliation). Has no\n  delegation, so no `prompt.md` exists for it — a real \"not recorded\" case,\n  not a fixture gap.\n- **`m-2026-09-11-007`** — the live, in-progress mission this very UI kit\n  was built under (open, round 1 of 2, zero results, zero delegations at\n  capture time). Demonstrates the in-flight/empty state with completely\n  real data rather than a mocked placeholder.\n\n## Load-bearing findings from working with real data\n\nThese surfaced while building the UI kit and should inform the eventual\nproduction data layer, not just this spike:\n\n1. **There is no title field anywhere in the mission data model.**\n   `find`, `list`, and `show` all lack one. The UI derives a row headline\n   from `success_criteria[0]` (first sentence, if the criterion is a long\n   run-on paragraph), falling back to `context`, then `ticket`, then an\n   honest \"(no description recorded)\". See `src/lib/format.ts#headline`.\n2. **`ethos find missions` and `ethos mission list` return different,\n   only-partially-overlapping id sets** from the same local store (105 vs\n   125 records here, ~30 ids only in `find`, ~50 only in `list`). A client\n   relying on either alone misses real missions. The UI unions both and\n   marks `list`-only rows as a visibly thinner \"list-only record\".\n3. **Per-criterion completion state does not exist.** `success_criteria`\n   is a flat string list with no done/not-done flag; only round results\n   carry a real per-item checklist (`evidence[]`, freeform names, not\n   index-aligned to criteria). The peek panel renders criteria as plain\n   bullets and evidence as a separate real checklist — it does not\n   pretend criteria are individually checked off.\n4. **Round-level verdict has four real values**, not two:\n   `pass | fail | escalate | abandoned`. `escalate` is not a failure and\n   is styled distinctly (amber, not red).\n5. **No mission in the local store has a fail-then-pass round history**\n   or a structured \"open questions\" field. Deferred/open-question content\n   exists only as prose inside reflection/result text — the mission\n   contract asked for one example of each; the closest honest substitutes\n   are documented above rather than fabricated to fit the ask.\n","file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/ui/fixtures/README.md"},"tool_input_hash":"ac3be64359475e60fd65f139ec043107cc27ae26f7ab098a699d1c064acedbcd","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"# Fixtures\\n\\nAll files here are unmodified output of real `ethos` CLI commands, run\\nread-only against the `ethos` repo's live mission store (plus one live\\nmission from this very `desk` ..."}
