{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:33:34.53998582Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nspike/ui: build the Missions screen with Tailwind v4 + real fixtures\n\nImplements the Linear-pattern grouped list + side peek panel from\nmockups/ethos-desktop-mockup.html, wired entirely to the real ethos\nmission fixtures (no fabricated data anywhere on screen).\n\nProgressive disclosure, three levels: dense grouped row (status glyph,\nshort id, headline, round/verdict badges, avatar); peek narrative (the\nask from a real prompt.md, result prose + evidence, plain-bullet\ncriteria, a coarse 2-3 point real timeline); collapsed Mechanics\n\u003cdetails\u003e (write-set, budget, evaluator+hash, ticket, raw ids).\n\nMissing/thin data renders as a visible \"not recorded\" affordance\ninstead of a blank gap — exercised for real by a genuinely open\nin-flight mission (this very mission, m-2026-09-11-007), a mission\nwith no captured prompt.md, and 51 real \"list-only\" thin records where\n`ethos find missions` and `ethos mission list` disagree on the id set.\nFindings from working the real data are written up in fixtures/README.md.\n\ntsc --noEmit is clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 \[REDACTED:email]\u003e\nEOF\n)\" -- spike/ui","description":"Commit the Missions screen implementation"},"tool_input_hash":"878b984225fa3330b6abc4612d453b9587fce3f49812c496b5fa734faedf146e","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"$(cat \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\nspike/ui: build the Missions screen with Tailwind v4 + real fixtures\\n\\nImplements the Linear-pattern group..."}
