{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:39:14.553094322Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git status --short spike/ui \u0026\u0026 git log --oneline -6","description":"Verify clean status and commit history"},"tool_input_hash":"21a546fa38f747197e05fcc66f59407624cb1310dd5199c8b009d710a5498555","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git status --short spike/ui \\u0026\\u0026 git log --oneline -6\",\"description\":\"Verify clean status and commit history\"}"}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:39:35.984638926Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"mkdir -p ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/result-m-2026-09-11-007.yaml \u003c\u003c 'EOF'\nmission: m-2026-09-11-007\nround: 1\nauthor: edt\nverdict: pass\nconfidence: 0.85\nfiles_changed: []\nevidence:\n  - name: \"tsc --noEmit clean\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"fixtures captured live via ethos find/list/show/log CLI (no fabricated data)\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"screenshot-vs-mockup loop run 4x (initial build, mechanics/date wrap fixes, escalate-verdict fix, open_questions addition), each verified by reading the PNG\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"3 diverse missions rendered: 3-round pass with real open_questions, single-round admin fail, live in-flight open mission with zero results\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"honest empty states verified across all real states found: no-prompt.md, no-result, list-only thin record (51 real cases), no-timestamp fallback\"\n    status: pass\nprose: |\n  Built the Missions UI kit at spike/ui: a plain Vite + React 19 + TS +\n  Tailwind v4 sandbox, fixture-driven with zero daemon dependency,\n  reproducing the Linear-pattern grouped-list + side-peek design from\n  mockups/ethos-desktop-mockup.html against real ethos mission data.\n\n  Fixtures (spike/ui/fixtures/, documented in fixtures/README.md): the\n  full `ethos find missions --format json` (105 records) and `ethos\n  mission list --json --status all` (125 records) output from the ethos\n  repo, `show`+`log` --json for 3 diverse missions, 2 real delegation\n  prompt.md files, and — after discovering `mission show --json` drops\n  a real field — the raw results.yaml for the multi-round mission so its\n  genuine `open_questions` entries could be rendered. All commands were\n  read-only; nothing was hand-edited.\n\n  Screens implement the 3-level progressive disclosure from the\n  contract: L1 dense row (status glyph, short id, derived headline,\n  round/verdict badges, avatar, grouped by a real status-derived\n  bucket); L2 peek narrative (the ask from a real prompt.md, result\n  prose + real per-item evidence + a new \"open questions for the\n  leader\" callout, plain-bullet success criteria, a coarse 2-3 point\n  timeline collapsed from the real event log or falling back to\n  created_at/closed_at); L3 collapsed Mechanics \u003cdetails\u003e (write-set,\n  budget, evaluator handle+hash, ticket, raw ids). j/k + Enter selection\n  works; a real substring search filters by id/headline/handle/ticket.\n\n  Real-data honesty was the hardest and most valuable part. The mission\n  data model has no title field at all (headline is derived from\n  success_criteria[0] with a sentence-boundary heuristic for the\n  giant-paragraph case, falling back honestly to \"(no description\n  recorded)\"); `find` and `list` return different, only 75%-overlapping\n  id sets from the same store (the UI unions them and visibly marks\n  51 real \"list-only\" thin rows); success_criteria has no per-item\n  done flag (only round evidence does, and it isn't index-aligned to\n  criteria, so criteria render as plain bullets, not checkboxes);\n  round verdict has four real values (pass/fail/escalate/abandoned),\n  not two, and escalate is styled amber, not red; and — the most\n  load-bearing find — `ethos mission show --json` silently omits\n  `open_questions` even though it's a documented result field present\n  in 28 of 135 local results.yaml files, which is a real CLI gap worth\n  fixing before a production read path is built on `show` alone. Full\n  writeup with file:line-equivalent detail in fixtures/README.md.\n\n  Screenshot loop: took the mockup screenshot first and read it, then\n  iterated the running vite dev server through 8+ screenshot-and-read\n  cycles across delegated/multiround/fail/escalated/thin-record/\n  keyboard-nav/open-questions states, fixing real bugs each time\n  (date-column AM/PM wrap, sha256 hash overflow in Mechanics, headline\n  mid-word truncation, escalate verdict wrongly styled red). Final\n  curated set at spike/ui/shots/final-*.png (8 images, mockup reference\n  included as final-00).\n\n  Committed incrementally: scaffold+fixtures, screen implementation,\n  keyboard-nav/polish fixes, open_questions addition — 4 commits, each\n  with `tsc --noEmit` clean, none exceeding the 30-minute uncommitted\n  budget.\nEOF\necho written","description":"Write the mission result YAML"},"tool_input_hash":"4222be5027926255847af3b670270abc7e2c59a0b0a8fc99ac7d6af9d7dd8794","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"mkdir -p ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp \\u0026\\u0026 cat \\u003e ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/result-m-2026-09-11-007.yaml \\u003c\\u003c 'EOF'\\nmission: m-2026-09-11-007\\nround: 1\\nauthor: edt..."}
