{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:53:18.482558779Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Fair pushback, and you're right my inference didn…","message":"Fair pushback, and you're right my inference didn't establish intent, only ruled out my stash as cause. Update: the team lead independently checked this and told me directly \"the spike/ui deletions are that worker's own template cleanup\" (referring to whoever built spike/ui — sounds like worker-shell/adb's Vite scaffold, stripping the default template assets as part of building the real Missions UI) and has asked that worker to confirm their files are intact. Team lead is treating it as handled — going in the spike report as a process note, no further escalation. So it has an owner now, not unattributed; you shouldn't need to hold off on the dangling stash commit account of this. Thanks for pressing on it rather than taking my first pass at face value — that's exactly the check that should've happened before I called it resolved myself.","recipient":"explore-tauri-setup","summary":"team lead already investigated and attributed the deletions","to":"explore-tauri-setup","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"f4e0a1872402f8886994a20fd14df2ab620fad33a8bff603cbbed5e284525f0c","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Fair pushback, and you're right my inference didn…\",\"message\":\"Fair pushback, and you're right my inference didn't establish intent, only ruled out my stash as cause. Update: the team le..."}
