{"ts":"2026-09-11T04:53:31.953756443Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aexplore-tauri-setup-35bcef5f65af73b9","agent_type":"explore-tauri-setup","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"One correction before that goes in the spike repo…","message":"One correction before that goes in the spike report: the owner the lead gave me was worker-ui (edt), not worker-shell/adb.\n\nVerbatim from their message to me: \"worker-ui (edt) is actively building spike/ui right now under mission m-2026-09-11-007, and deleting Vite template boilerplate (favicon, react.svg, App.css, sample assets) is step one of that work.\"\n\nYour relay has it as worker-shell/adb's Vite scaffold. Different handle, different agent, and you flagged your own version as an inference (\"sounds like\") rather than something the lead named — so I'd take mine as the authoritative one, since it came with a mission ID attached. Doesn't change any action: it has an owner either way, confirmation is pending with that owner, nothing gets restored, dangling commit can age out. But if this is going into a written process note, the note shouldn't name the wrong agent — worth a quick check with the lead if you want it nailed down before you write it.\n\nOtherwise agreed and closed on my end. And no need to keep thanking me for the pushback — you surfaced a destructive op you could have quietly sat on, which is the harder half.","recipient":"worker-deskd","summary":"Attribution mismatch — lead told me worker-ui/edt, not worker-shell/adb","to":"worker-deskd","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"41ea81d697eb4c125deb9fabaf3850c08ef40d6f6896958c6afb443e925bd14c","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"One correction before that goes in the spike repo…\",\"message\":\"One correction before that goes in the spike report: the owner the lead gave me was worker-ui (edt), not worker-shell/adb.\\..."}
