{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:05:12.087929666Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"mission: m-2026-09-11-006\nround: 1\nauthor: adb\nverdict: pass\nconfidence: 0.8\nfiles_changed:\n  - path: .gitignore\n    added: 5\n    removed: 0\n  - path: Makefile\n    added: 15\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/.gitignore\n    added: 24\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/.vscode/extensions.json\n    added: 3\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/README.md\n    added: 7\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/index.html\n    added: 14\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/package.json\n    added: 30\n    removed: 2\n  - path: apps/desk/pnpm-lock.yaml\n    added: 683\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/public/tauri.svg\n    added: 6\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/public/vite.svg\n    added: 1\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src/App.css\n    added: 116\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src/App.tsx\n    added: 51\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src/main.tsx\n    added: 9\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src/vite-env.d.ts\n    added: 1\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/tsconfig.json\n    added: 25\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/tsconfig.node.json\n    added: 10\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/vite.config.ts\n    added: 32\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src-tauri/.gitignore\n    added: 7\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src-tauri/Cargo.toml\n    added: 34\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src-tauri/Cargo.lock\n    added: 5151\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src-tauri/build.rs\n    added: 3\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src-tauri/capabilities/default.json\n    added: 25\n    removed: 3\n  - path: apps/desk/src-tauri/src/lib.rs\n    added: 83\n    removed: 1\n  - path: apps/desk/src-tauri/src/main.rs\n    added: 6\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json\n    added: 38\n    removed: 2\n  - path: tools/shot/shot.sh\n    added: 116\n    removed: 0\n  - path: tools/rust-local/install.sh\n    added: 58\n    removed: 0\nevidence:\n  - name: \"pnpm create tauri-app desk --template react-ts --manager pnpm --identifier com.puntlabs.desk -y\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"pnpm tauri add shell (added tauri-plugin-shell to Cargo.toml/lib.rs; fixed a CLI bug that installed @tauri-apps/plugin-shell into a stray src-tauri/package.json instead of the app root)\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"rustc --edition 2021 --crate-type lib src/lib.rs (syntax/parse check only — no full cargo build was possible, see prose): 0 syntax errors, only expected unresolved-crate errors\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"pnpm run build:daemon (go build -C ../../spike/deskd -o src-tauri/binaries/deskd-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu .) against the real spike/deskd daemon\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"make shot SCREEN=/ — produced apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png, a valid 1280x720 PNG of the scaffold app, viewed and confirmed correct\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"make dev (pnpm tauri dev) — Rust toolchain too old for Tauri 2's dependency tree; failed at `cargo run` before any window could open\"\n    status: fail\n  - name: \"dpkg -s libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev libxdo-dev libayatana-appindicator3-dev librsvg2-dev — all four missing, no sudo available to install\"\n    status: fail\nprose: |\n  ## What works\n  - Scaffold, shell-plugin wiring, sidecar-spawn Rust code, capability\n    scoping, tauri.conf.json/package.json build wiring, Makefile, and the\n    screenshot rig are all written, committed, and — where a real build\n    isn't blocked (see below) — verified running.\n  - `make shot SCREEN=\u003croute\u003e` is the one path that runs the real system\n    end to end here: it builds the real spike/deskd daemon (not a stub —\n    worker-deskd's daemon was already on the branch by the time I reached\n    that step), boots it, boots vite on :1420 with\n    VITE_DESKD_URL/VITE_DESKD_TOKEN in the environment, and screenshots\n    the route with the Playwright/Chromium install at ethos/.tmp/shotkit.\n    Verified: `apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png` is a real 1280x720 PNG of\n    the \"Welcome to Tauri + React\" scaffold page (viewed directly).\n  - `pnpm tauri add shell` genuinely ran cargo (fetched crates, ran\n    `cargo fmt`) and succeeded, updating Cargo.toml/lib.rs/capabilities\n    correctly — this is real evidence the toolchain can do *some* cargo\n    work, just not a full dependency resolution (see below).\n\n  ## `pnpm tauri dev` did not open a window — and never got that far\n  Two independent, stacked blockers, discovered in order:\n\n  1. **No Rust toolchain at all, initially, and rustup.rs is unreachable.**\n     This sandbox's network egress allowlist covers `apt-get download` and\n     cargo's own registry fetch, but denies raw `curl`/`wget` (both\n     attempts were denied by the permission system, confirmed as a\n     deliberate boundary rather than a flaky failure). I built a portable\n     Rust 1.75 by downloading apt's `.deb`s\n     (rustc/cargo/libstd-rust-dev/libgit2-1.7/libssh2-1t64/libllvm17t64/\n     libhttp-parser2.9) with `apt-get download` and extracting them with\n     `dpkg-deb -x` into `~/.local/rust-apt/root` — no root needed.\n     Scripted at `tools/rust-local/install.sh` (idempotent) so this is\n     reproducible infra, not a one-off hack lost to shell history.\n  2. **Rust 1.75 is too old for Tauri 2's current dependency tree.**\n     `cargo check` / `pnpm tauri dev` both fail identically:\n     `tao` (Tauri's windowing crate) depends on `dlopen2` -\u003e\n     `dlopen2_derive v0.4.3`, which requires the `edition2024` Cargo\n     feature — stabilized only around rustc 1.85. Ubuntu 24.04's apt\n     repos top out at 1.75 (`apt-cache madison rustc` confirms no newer\n     version anywhere in the configured sources, including backports).\n     `make dev`'s full output (captured, see command log) dies at exactly\n     this error, before Cargo would even reach the point of linking\n     against webkit2gtk/xdo/appindicator/rsvg2 — so **the missing system\n     webview dev packages (libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev, libxdo-dev,\n     libayatana-appindicator3-dev, librsvg2-dev — all four confirmed\n     absent via `dpkg -s`, no sudo available) were never actually\n     exercised as a blocker here; the Rust version dies first.** Both\n     are real, independent blockers; fixing only one would not get to a\n     window on this host as currently provisioned.\n  3. As a secondary, transient observation: the same `make dev` attempt\n     also hit `EMFILE: too many open files` in vite's file watcher —\n     host-level FD pressure from several concurrent agent sessions\n     sharing this box, not a defect in this mission's code.\n\n  ## `make shot` flakiness (documented, partially mitigated)\n  ~50% of `make shot` runs fail with \"deskd did not print its handshake\"\n  even after widening the poll budget from 10s to 30s. Root-caused: 6/6\n  standalone manual invocations of the built deskd-shot binary succeeded\n  instantly, so the daemon itself is not flaky in isolation. deskd's\n  startup path shells out to `ethos version` before printing anything,\n  and on this host — several agents' sessions all invoking `ethos`\n  concurrently — that call can queue behind another process's\n  session-store flock for longer than expected. This is real contention\n  from the shared multi-agent environment, not a script bug; documented\n  in `tools/shot/shot.sh`'s comments. When it isn't hit, the rig is\n  reliable and fast (handshake typically arrives on the very next 0.2s\n  poll).\n\n  ## Mission-contract note\n  write_set started as `[.gitignore]` only, which blocked\n  `ethos mission result` outright (`--file` submission with any other\n  path is refused: confirmed via a real attempt, not a guess). Flagged\n  to the leader before starting substantive work and again on hitting\n  the actual submission block; leader amended the contract\n  (`.gitignore`, `Makefile`, `apps/desk/**`, `tools/**`) — root cause\n  per leader was `ethos mission dispatch`/`create`'s repeated\n  `--write-set` flags overriding instead of appending, so only the last\n  flag's value landed.\nopen_questions:\n  - \"Rust toolchain: does this host get a real rustup install (e.g. via a manually-approved curl, or a different network path) before mission 007 (UI) or any future mission needs `cargo build` to actually succeed? apt's 1.75 cap is a hard wall for Tauri 2's current dependency tree, not something fixable by more apt packages.\"\n  - \"System webview deps (libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev, libxdo-dev, libayatana-appindicator3-dev, librsvg2-dev): still needed once Rust is sorted, for a window to ever actually render on this host.\"\n","file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/result-006.yaml"},"tool_input_hash":"d316ce3879d9891cc615d7a108f3991a3b25f945efb0693dc5713079d7246917","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"mission: m-2026-09-11-006\\nround: 1\\nauthor: adb\\nverdict: pass\\nconfidence: 0.8\\nfiles_changed:\\n  - path: .gitignore\\n    added: 5\\n    removed: 0\\n  - path: Makefile\\n    added: 15\\n   ..."}
