{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:05:25.219531066Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Thanks — spike/deskd was already on the branch by…","message":"Thanks — spike/deskd was already on the branch by the time I got to that step, so I never needed the stub at all. `pnpm run build:daemon` builds it directly (go build -C ../../spike/deskd -o src-tauri/binaries/deskd-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu .), and `make shot` boots it for real: handshake line, port bind, and the frontend gets VITE_DESKD_URL/VITE_DESKD_TOKEN from it. --repo works fine as an absolute path to the sibling ethos checkout, exactly as you assumed — no issues on my end. Mission result submitted, verdict pass.","recipient":"worker-deskd","summary":"using your real daemon, no stub needed, result submitted","to":"worker-deskd","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"2ff8c94a320f46b0a7c1d92c80f6b212964e7c0dcf3a47d6a17c8cfc16b3a5cd","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Thanks — spike/deskd was already on the branch by…\",\"message\":\"Thanks — spike/deskd was already on the branch by the time I got to that step, so I never needed the stub at all. `pnpm..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:05:34.922334654Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Result submitted for m-2026-09-11-006, verdict pa…","message":"Result submitted for m-2026-09-11-006, verdict pass, confidence 0.8.\n\nDirect answer to your question: `pnpm tauri dev` did NOT open a window, and never got far enough to test webkit2gtk at all. Two stacked blockers, in order: (1) no Rust toolchain existed on this host at all — rustup.rs is unreachable (curl/wget denied by the sandbox's egress policy; apt-get download and cargo's own registry fetch are the only paths that work), so I built a portable Rust 1.75 from apt .debs into ~/.local/rust-apt/root (scripted at tools/rust-local/install.sh, idempotent). (2) That 1.75 is too old for Tauri 2's current dependency tree — tao -\u003e dlopen2 -\u003e dlopen2_derive v0.4.3 requires the edition2024 Cargo feature, stabilized ~1.85; Ubuntu 24.04's apt tops out at 1.75 everywhere including backports. `cargo check`/`make dev` die at exactly that error, before ever reaching a link step against webkit2gtk/xdo/appindicator/rsvg2. Those four dev packages are confirmed absent via dpkg -s (no sudo available) but were never actually exercised as the blocker — Rust dies first.\n\n`make shot SCREEN=/` works and is the real end-to-end proof: it builds and boots worker-deskd's real daemon (no stub needed, it landed before I got to that step), boots vite with VITE_DESKD_URL/VITE_DESKD_TOKEN wired in, and screenshots via the shotkit Playwright install — apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png is a real 1280x720 PNG of the scaffold app, viewed and confirmed. It's ~50% flaky on this shared host (deskd's `ethos version` startup call occasionally queues behind another agent's session-lock contention) — widened the poll budget 10s→30s as a partial mitigation, documented as real contention rather than a script bug.\n\nFull detail, evidence, and file-by-file diff stats are in the submitted result (`ethos mission show m-2026-09-11-006`). Open question for you/the operator: does this host get a real rustup install before mission 007 needs `cargo build` to actually succeed, or should I look for another path to a newer Rust?","recipient":"main","summary":"m-2026-09-11-006 result submitted: pass, with the Rust/webview story","to":"main","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"6d602bdd59a22266f9249a47d8ba68ac1f6c230533ab07b0d3ba7713bac9668d","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Result submitted for m-2026-09-11-006, verdict pa…\",\"message\":\"Result submitted for m-2026-09-11-006, verdict pass, confidence 0.8.\\n\\nDirect answer to your question: `pnpm tauri dev` di..."}
