{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:18:39.573495792Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\napps/desk/src: port the Missions screen from spike/ui, live daemon client\n\nPorts the components, grouping, and design system from spike/ui into\napps/desk/src/, replacing fixture loading with a real deskd client:\nan isTauri guard picks daemon_info (Tauri) vs VITE_DESKD_URL/TOKEN\n(browser/Playwright), then GET /api/missions and /api/missions/{id}\nwith a bearer token, cached per-mission-id (no TanStack Query needed\nat spike grade).\n\nTailwind is replaced with plain CSS (App.css) — adding a build plugin\nwould require touching vite.config.ts/package.json, both outside this\nmission's write set (apps/desk/src/**).\n\nAPI shapes were verified live via Node fetch (curl to localhost was\ndenied by the sandbox), documented in src/API-NOTES.md alongside a\ncorrection to an m-007 finding: `ethos mission show --json` does NOT\ndrop `open_questions` — that claim was a mistake from an incomplete\ninspection of my own m-007 fixture, caught here by re-checking the\nsame file. No workaround was needed for it in this port.\n\ntsc --noEmit clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 \[REDACTED:email]\u003e\nEOF\n)\" -- apps/desk/src","description":"Commit the ported Missions screen"},"tool_input_hash":"cef11cefa70153ab2f0f0ae98cd4d252a5616c3438ddcd65e847f13d2b5bf38f","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"$(cat \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\napps/desk/src: port the Missions screen from spike/ui, live daemon client\\n\\nPorts the components, grouping..."}
