{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:25:26.224582881Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"mkdir -p ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/result-m-2026-09-11-011.yaml \u003c\u003c 'EOF'\nmission: m-2026-09-11-011\nround: 1\nauthor: edt\nverdict: pass\nconfidence: 0.85\nfiles_changed: []\nevidence:\n  - name: \"tsc --noEmit clean in apps/desk\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"GET /api/missions and /api/missions/{id} probed live via Node fetch (curl to localhost was sandbox-denied) and adapted types to the real response shapes, not the Go source\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"All 155 real missions render, grouped by real status, with a real substring search and j/k+Enter nav ported unchanged\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"peek panel loads detail lazily per mission id (cached), rendering real prompt excerpts, result prose, open_questions, evidence, criteria, timeline, and Mechanics from the live daemon\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"isTauri guard + daemon_info poll path implemented per spec; browser path (VITE_DESKD_URL/TOKEN) verified working via make shot and a manual instance\"\n    status: pass\n  - name: \"make shot SCREEN=/ run to completion (2 attempts, 1st hit the documented lock-contention flake, 2nd succeeded) — screenshot captured a real but incomplete moment (loading state) due to a rig timing gap unrelated to my code; supplemented with a manual --wait-for-selector run proving full correct render, both included below\"\n    status: pass\nprose: |\n  Ported the spike/ui Missions screen into apps/desk/src/, replacing all\n  fixture loading with a real deskd client. Nothing outside apps/desk/src/\n  was touched — Tailwind was replaced with hand-written plain CSS\n  (App.css) specifically because adding a build plugin would have required\n  editing vite.config.ts/package.json, both outside the write set.\n\n  Daemon client (src/lib/daemon.ts, src/lib/api.ts): isTauri() checks\n  `'__TAURI_INTERNALS__' in window`; the Tauri path dynamic-imports\n  @tauri-apps/api/core and polls `daemon_info` (already a declared\n  dependency — no new install needed); the browser path reads\n  VITE_DESKD_URL/VITE_DESKD_TOKEN. Every /api/ call sends the bearer\n  token. Mission detail is cached per id in a module-level Map (spike-\n  grade per the contract, no TanStack Query needed).\n\n  API shapes were verified live, not assumed from the Go source: I built\n  and ran deskd manually, then hit both endpoints with Node's fetch\n  (curl to localhost was denied by this session's sandbox for an\n  unrelated reason). Findings written to src/API-NOTES.md:\n    - GET /api/missions returns 155 uniform missionSummary objects with\n      no description field at all (no success_criteria, no context, no\n      title) — a real gap, not a client artifact. Row headline is\n      honestly derived from type+ticket (src/lib/format.ts#rowHeadline).\n    - GET /api/missions/{id} passes the raw `mission show`/`log --json`\n      straight through as nested objects (not JSON-encoded strings —\n      res.json() already parses them). delegations[] carries a\n      500-char-capped excerpt per delegation, not the full prompt.md;\n      the UI labels it as an excerpt and notes when more delegations\n      exist (see Mechanics).\n    - CORRECTION to an m-007 finding: `ethos mission show --json` does\n      NOT drop `open_questions`. My m-007 result claimed it did; that\n      was wrong. Verified two ways: the live probe here shows the field\n      populated, and re-grepping my own m-007 fixture file\n      (spike/ui/fixtures/show-m-2026-07-21-001.json) shows it was there\n      all along — I just never checked for that key when I inspected it\n      in m-007. No workaround was needed in this port; open_questions is\n      read directly off contract.results[]. Flagging this since spike/ui\n      is outside this mission's write set and still carries the\n      now-unneeded yaml-parsing workaround and the incorrect README\n      finding.\n\n  Verification: `make shot SCREEN=/` was run twice — first attempt hit\n  the documented ~50% lock-contention flake (deskd's `ethos version`\n  check queued behind another session's flock, exact failure mode the\n  script's own comment describes), second attempt succeeded end-to-end\n  (deskd up, vite up, screenshot written). The screenshot\n  (apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png) shows the shell rendering correctly\n  but the missions pane still reading \"Connecting to deskd…\" — this is a\n  real, reproducible gap in tools/shot/shot.sh itself, not my code: its\n  `npx playwright screenshot` call has no --wait-for-selector/timeout, so\n  it screenshots on the page's `load` event, before my post-mount fetch\n  resolves. I did not modify shot.sh (outside my write set); instead I\n  proved the code is correct with a manual instance (same deskd binary,\n  same env vars, same vite dev server) and\n  `playwright screenshot --wait-for-selector=\".mission-row\"`, which shows\n  all 155 real missions, grouped correctly, with full peek-panel detail\n  including real prompt excerpts, result prose, native open_questions, an\n  escalate-verdict mission, and Mechanics with real write-sets and\n  evaluator hashes. Screenshots (apps/desk/.tmp/shots/, not committed —\n  outside write set):\n    - root.png — official `make shot` output (shell renders, honest\n      loading state, proves no runtime crash)\n    - manual-01-loaded.png — full list + peek, wait-for-selector proof\n    - manual-02-scrolled.png / manual-03-mechanics.png — criteria,\n      timeline, and Mechanics (write-set, evaluator+hash, delegations,\n      artifacts) all real\n    - manual-04-multiround.png — 3-round mission, delegation-count note\n    - manual-05-escalated.png — escalate verdict styled amber end-to-end\n\n  Recommend shot.sh gain `--wait-for-selector=\".mission-row, .empty-state\"`\n  (or equivalent) before this rig is trusted for any app whose first\n  paint precedes its data fetch — true of any deskd-backed screen, not\n  just this one.\nEOF\necho written","description":"Write the mission result YAML for m-011"},"tool_input_hash":"59d855f31fce9399bfca399fee3e8dc81cad9b8a887368dd5b6a2d5ea85dbbc1","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"mkdir -p ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp \\u0026\\u0026 cat \\u003e ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/result-m-2026-09-11-011.yaml \\u003c\\u003c 'EOF'\\nmission: m-2026-09-11-011\\nround: 1\\nauthor: edt..."}
