{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:26:36.606350194Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"One small follow-up fix (mechanical, no new missi…","message":"One small follow-up fix (mechanical, no new mission — commit directly to spike/thin-slice under spike/deskd/): GET /api/missions items currently carry no description-shaped field, so the UI row headline falls back to type+ticket. The find-missions JSONL you already parse has success_criteria[] for closed missions, and your show-enrichment fan-out gets it for the rest. Add success_criteria (or at minimum a derived headline string = first criterion) to each /api/missions item where available; omit when absent. Bump nothing else. gofmt/go vet, one commit, reply done.","recipient":"worker-deskd","summary":"Small fix: add headline fields to list API","to":"worker-deskd","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"f1a849bb1fba92a4baebdc29633d6b1aa08eb416c3c1993393d5cd38d963c36d","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"One small follow-up fix (mechanical, no new missi…\",\"message\":\"One small follow-up fix (mechanical, no new mission — commit directly to spike/thin-slice under spike/deskd/): GET /api/m..."}
