{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:27:00.549930568Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/tools/shot/shot.sh","new_string":"# worker-ui's official run caught \"Connecting to deskd...\" instead of\n# rendered data: the screenshot fires on page load, before the app's\n# post-mount fetch to deskd resolves. Wait for a selector that only\n# appears once real data has rendered — overridable per-screen via\n# WAIT_FOR, since not every route renders mission rows. If the selector\n# never shows up (a screen that doesn't use it, or deskd data genuinely\n# isn't there), fall back to the plain screenshot rather than failing the\n# whole rig.\nWAIT_FOR=\"${WAIT_FOR:-.mission-row}\"\nWAIT_TIMEOUT_MS=\"${WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS:-15000}\"\n\necho \"==\u003e screenshotting http://localhost:1420$SCREEN -\u003e $OUT (wait-for: $WAIT_FOR)\"\nif ! (cd \"$SHOTKIT\" \u0026\u0026 npx --yes playwright screenshot \\\n  --wait-for-selector \"$WAIT_FOR\" --timeout \"$WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS\" \\\n  \"http://localhost:1420$SCREEN\" \"$OUT\"); then\n  echo \"==\u003e '$WAIT_FOR' did not appear within ${WAIT_TIMEOUT_MS}ms; falling back to an unconditional screenshot\" \u003e\u00262\n  (cd \"$SHOTKIT\" \u0026\u0026 npx --yes playwright screenshot \"http://localhost:1420$SCREEN\" \"$OUT\")\nfi\n\necho \"==\u003e wrote $OUT\"","old_string":"echo \"==\u003e screenshotting http://localhost:1420$SCREEN -\u003e $OUT\"\n(cd \"$SHOTKIT\" \u0026\u0026 npx --yes playwright screenshot \"http://localhost:1420$SCREEN\" \"$OUT\")\n\necho \"==\u003e wrote $OUT\"","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"155a215179dcf6ca1594db5cce875f5aca612e4063a4d2894806106af82204b2","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/tools/shot/shot.sh\",\"new_string\":\"# worker-ui's official run caught \\\"Connecting to deskd...\\\" instead of\\n# rendered data: the screenshot fires on page load, bef..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:27:02.316236199Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Review spike branch: silent failures","name":"review-silent","prompt":"Hunt silent failures in the spike branch at ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice; all code is new: spike/deskd/ Go daemon shelling out to the ethos CLI, apps/desk/src/ React app with a daemon client, tools/shot/shot.sh, Makefile). READ-ONLY.\n\nSpike-grade calibration — the question is not \"is error handling production-complete\" but \"does any error path LIE\": swallowed CLI exec failures that render as empty-but-healthy UI states, JSON parse failures that silently drop missions from the 155-mission union (making counts wrong), fetch failures the UI renders as 'no missions' instead of 'connection failed', the daemon_info retry loop giving up silently, shot.sh exiting 0 on a failed screenshot, cache serving stale data with no indication after upstream failure. Also: the known-accepted guards (json.Valid() on `ethos session --json` prose output) — verify they fail LOUD (logged) not silent.\n\nOutput: findings ranked by severity with file:line, the exact scenario where a failure masquerades as success, and suggested fix. State explicitly which of the paths I listed you checked and found clean.","subagent_type":"silent-failure-hunter"},"tool_input_hash":"af2e18df96051b4008855eb3d483d57ab8ffdb03de51e7607838d54d78b10670","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"Review spike branch: silent failures\",\"name\":\"review-silent\",\"prompt\":\"Hunt silent failures in the spike branch at ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice; all code is new: sp..."}
