{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:27:13.234654815Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Review spike: claimed invariants","name":"review-invariants","prompt":"Verify claimed invariants in the spike branch at ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice). READ-ONLY. The spike's REPORT will make claims; your job is to falsify or confirm them against the code before they're written down:\n\n1. CLAIM: \"GET /api/missions returns the union of find-missions (closed) and mission-list --status all (open+all), 155 missions, each id exactly once.\" Check spike/deskd's merge for dedup correctness, the id vs mission_id normalization, and whether any category (failed/abandoned/escalated missions absent from the trace log) can be dropped or duplicated.\n2. CLAIM: \"Every /api/* request requires the bearer token; OPTIONS is exempt.\" Check middleware ordering — is any route registered outside the auth wrapper; does the OPTIONS exemption leak into GET.\n3. CLAIM: \"The UI renders missing data honestly — 'not recorded' affordances, never fabricated placeholders.\" Check apps/desk/src (and spike/ui) for any default/mock/sample values that could render as if real (fake confidences, placeholder names, invented timestamps).\n4. CLAIM (from mission m-007's report, later self-corrected): \"ethos mission show --json drops open_questions\" — the correction says it does NOT drop it. Verify which is true by reading a fixture under spike/ui/fixtures/ and desk's API handling, so the spike report records the corrected truth with evidence.\n5. CLAIM: \"apps/desk/src work touched only apps/desk/src/**\" (mission m-011 write-set). Verify via git: commit bffb8cf touches nothing outside that path.\n\nOutput: per claim — CONFIRMED or FALSIFIED with file:line evidence, one line each; plus any OTHER claim-shaped comment/README assertion in the repo that is untrue (e.g. the known stale spike/ui/fixtures/README.md open_questions claim — confirm it's stale and say what the correct statement is).","subagent_type":"invariant-completeness-reviewer"},"tool_input_hash":"169fff8079c52825247ded9ac002a1c90236610bf42c7b47f66d5d0123c8deda","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"Review spike: claimed invariants\",\"name\":\"review-invariants\",\"prompt\":\"Verify claimed invariants in the spike branch at ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice). READ-ONLY. Th..."}
