{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:29:23.517508045Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git commit tools/shot/shot.sh -m \"fix(shot): wait for rendered data before screenshotting\n\nworker-ui's official run of make shot caught 'Connecting to deskd...'\ninstead of the Missions list: the screenshot fired on page load,\nbefore the app's post-mount fetch to deskd resolved. Add\n--wait-for-selector (default .mission-row, overridable via WAIT_FOR\nfor screens that don't render mission rows), 15s timeout via\nWAIT_TIMEOUT_MS. Falls back to an unconditional screenshot if the\nselector never appears, so non-deskd screens still shoot instead of\nfailing the whole rig.\n\nVerified: make shot SCREEN=/ (after two known-flaky retries — deskd's\nethos-session-lock contention, then vite EMFILE under concurrent\nagent load, both pre-existing and unrelated to this change) produced\napps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png showing the real Missions list (129\nclosed missions, detail pane), not the loading placeholder.\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -10","description":"Commit only the shot.sh fix"},"tool_input_hash":"fc9b87ae186e2ab7b48a0868a6547adf6c955756f2e57b676acdbb9fa0824d3b","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git commit tools/shot/shot.sh -m \\\"fix(shot): wait for rendered data before screenshotting\\n\\nworker-ui's official run of make shot caught 'Connecti..."}
