{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:29:50.040233998Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"areview-code-ddc0eec3e3bdb5cf","agent_type":"review-code","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"~/.local/bin/ethos find missions --format json \u003e ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/trace.jsonl 2\u003e/dev/null; ~/.local/bin/ethos mission list --json --status all \u003e ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/list.json 2\u003e/dev/null; python3 - \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nimport json, os, collections\nt=[json.loads(l) for l in open('~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/trace.jsonl') if l.strip()]\nl=json.load(open('~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/list.json'))\ntid={x['id'] for x in t}; lid={e['mission_id'] for e in l}\nprint(\"trace\",len(tid),\"list\",len(lid),\"union\",len(tid|lid))\nghosts = tid - lid\nprint(\"trace-only (ghosts, no list entry):\",len(ghosts), sorted(ghosts)[:5])\nprint(\"list-only (need enrich):\",len(lid-tid))\ndirs=set(os.listdir('\u003crepo\u003e/.punt-labs/ethos/missions'))\nprint(\"union ids with NO on-disk dir:\", len((tid|lid)-dirs), sorted((tid|lid)-dirs)[:5])\n# created_at formats\nfmts=collections.Counter()\nfor x in t: fmts[('trace',len(x.get('created_at') or ''))]+=1\nfor e in l: fmts[('list',len(e.get('created_at') or ''))]+=1\nprint(fmts)\nprint(\"sample trace created_at:\", t[0].get('created_at'), \"| status:\",t[0].get('status'))\n# dup status disagreement between trace and list\ndis=[(i, [x for x in t if x['id']==i][0]['status'], [e for e in l if e['mission_id']==i][0]['status']) for i in sorted(tid\u0026lid)]\nbad=[d for d in dis if d[1]!=d[2]]\nprint(\"status disagreements trace vs list:\",len(bad), bad[:5])\nEOF","description":"Analyze merge union, ghosts, and timestamp formats"},"tool_input_hash":"918970ec5d4912d821ad49eef70d8f1225c78bb4ba57dda86b613f75a215370a","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"~/.local/bin/ethos find missions --format json \\u003e ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/trace.jsonl 2\\u003e/dev/null; ~/.local/bin/ethos mission list --json --status all \\u003e ~/Coding/punt-la..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:29:53.911705624Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"areview-silent-00671012b421ba6f","agent_type":"review-silent","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Silent-failure audit of spike/thin-slice done (re…","message":"Silent-failure audit of spike/thin-slice done (read the working tree, which includes the uncommitted edits to missions.go and shot.sh). Two paths lie; four are degraded; the rest of your list is clean. Findings ranked:\n\nHIGH 1 — /api/session swallows real exec failures as a healthy empty roster; the accepted guard does NOT fail loud. spike/deskd/identity.go:27-32: `if err != nil || !json.Valid(out)` collapses BOTH the documented benign case (no active session / prose-on-stdout CLI gap) AND any genuine bridge failure (ethos binary missing, repo deleted, ethos crash — execEthos even captures stderr into err, then it's discarded) into `{\"participants\":[]}` with the single undifferentiated note `session=empty`. The error string never reaches any log. Scenario that lies: ethos starts crashing mid-run → /api/session forever returns a healthy empty roster; stderr shows only \"session=empty\", indistinguishable from the expected case. Fix (2 lines): when err != nil, rec.note(\"session_err=\"+err.Error()); when err == nil but !json.Valid, note \"session=no-active-session (prose stdout)\". Mitigating: nothing in apps/desk/src consumes /api/session or /api/identities yet, so impact is latent — but the endpoint contract lies today.\n\nHIGH 2 — Tauri sidecar reader discards deskd's stderr, exit, and unparseable stdout, so the daemon_info timeout misdiagnoses every startup failure. apps/desk/src-tauri/src/lib.rs:61-76: the event loop handles only CommandEvent::Stdout; (a) `if let Ok(info) = serde_json::from_str` drops a malformed handshake line with no log, (b) CommandEvent::Stderr is never read — deskd's fatal diagnostics (\"deskd: ethos version check failed: ...\", main.go:56) vanish, (c) CommandEvent::Terminated is ignored — sidecar death is invisible. Scenario: deskd exits 1 at startup (hardcoded SPIKE_REPO wrong, ethos not installed) → reader loop ends silently → daemon_info stays None → after 10s the UI shows \"deskd sidecar did not report its port/token within 10s\" (daemon.ts:32). Not silent in the UI, but the message is a wrong diagnosis and the true cause is unrecoverable. Fix: eprintln! Stderr lines, log Terminated with code, log a parse-failed stdout line.\n\nMEDIUM 3 — shot.sh exits 0 on a fallback screenshot of a broken app. tools/shot/shot.sh:125-130 (the uncommitted edit): if `.mission-row` never appears — including because deskd returned 500 and the app renders \"Failed to load missions\" — it takes an unconditional screenshot, prints \"==\u003e wrote $OUT\", exits 0. The fallback IS announced on stderr, so not silent, but exit status and the final line masquerade as success; anything gating on `make shot`'s exit code will call a broken-app PNG good. Note the fallback also fires on legitimately row-less screens, so a hard exit-1 is wrong; suggest naming the artifact `$SLUG-fallback.png` and/or a distinct final line so the two outcomes can't be confused. (Everything else in shot.sh fails loud: handshake timeout and vite timeout both dump logs and exit 1; the head -n1 partial-line race is benign — the sed patterns reject incomplete lines and the -z check exits 1.)\n\nMEDIUM 4 — a failed daemon connection is cached forever. apps/desk/src/lib/daemon.ts:53-58 memoizes the connection promise with no rejection cleanup: after one 10s timeout, every later fetch (list, every peek-panel open) replays the same cached rejection even if the sidecar came up at t=11s. The UI looks like it's retrying (panels remount, show fresh \"failed to load\") while nothing is retried. Fix: clear `connection` on rejection, mirroring detailCache's delete-on-error at api.ts:33-35.\n\nLOW 5 — missionDetailHandler maps every `mission show` failure to 404 (missions.go:115-118), including timeout/binary-missing. Message text survives to the UI so not silent, just misclassified.\n\nLOW 6 — mergedMissions (missions.go:150-164): a valid-JSON trace line lacking \"id\" (or duplicate ids) silently keys byID[\"\"]/overwrites — would render a ghost/merged row rather than erroring. Speculative given current CLI output. Related inconsistency: identitiesHandler (identity.go:10-15) pipes CLI stdout verbatim with no json.Valid guard — the exact prose-on-stdout gap sessionHandler documents would ship invalid JSON as application/json (client res.json() throws, so loud downstream). Trivial: excerpt() (fs.go:84-89) cuts at byte 500, can split a UTF-8 rune → mojibake before the ellipsis.\n\nPaths from your list checked and CLEAN:\n- Swallowed CLI exec failures → empty-but-healthy UI: clean for missions. execEthos wraps every failure with captured stderr (ethos.go:21-27); handlers return 500; App.tsx:41-43 renders an explicit \"Failed to load missions: ...\" error state, never an empty list.\n- JSON parse failures silently dropping missions from the union: clean. Every Unmarshal error in mergedMissions aborts the whole request (missions.go:156, 171, 191) — fail-loud 500, no per-line skip-and-continue, so the count cannot silently shrink. (Only crack is the missing-id edge in LOW 6.)\n- Fetch failure rendered as \"no missions\": clean — LoadState has a dedicated error arm; the empty-state string appears only on a genuinely empty ready result.\n- daemon_info retry loop giving up silently: not silent — it throws after 10s and the UI shows it — but see HIGH 2 (cause lost) and MEDIUM 4 (rejection cached).\n- Cache serving stale data after upstream failure: clean. cache.get (cache.go:20-23) never returns expired data, errors are never cached (set only on success, missions.go:107), so a failed refresh surfaces as a 500 rather than stale-but-healthy. Within-TTL 30s staleness is by design and flag-disclosed.\n- PeekPanel/timeline degradation: coarseTimeline's fallback is honestly labeled in code and the panel shows the fetch error in all three data sections, so the record-derived timeline doesn't mask the failure.\n\nNet: for a spike, the error architecture is genuinely good — typed LoadState in the UI, fail-loud parsing in the daemon, stderr capture on exec. The two fixes worth doing before anyone trusts a demo are HIGH 1 (two rec.note lines) and HIGH 2 (log Stderr/Terminated in lib.rs); both are minutes of work.","recipient":"team-lead","summary":"Silent-failure audit of spike branch complete","to":"team-lead","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"8c1cb6643ef9cb8a6bafb437edb39cff625208bf8956fcfa85389557bc4d3ce7","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Silent-failure audit of spike/thin-slice done (re…\",\"message\":\"Silent-failure audit of spike/thin-slice done (read the working tree, which includes the uncommitted edits to missions.go a..."}
