{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:31:41.846253169Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cat \u003e ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/probe-sc.mjs \u003c\u003c 'EOF'\nconst res = await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:42889/api/missions', {\n  headers: { Authorization: '[REDACTED:bearer]' }\n});\nconst data = await res.json();\nconsole.log('count', data.length);\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(data[0], null, 2));\nconst noCriteria = data.filter(m =\u003e !m.success_criteria || m.success_criteria.length === 0);\nconsole.log('rows with no success_criteria:', noCriteria.length);\nEOF\nnode ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/probe-sc.mjs","description":"Verify success_criteria present in live API response"},"tool_input_hash":"5a61ef92360ce5c6bb6f1837bb5f043cb032a127416c4317b0d8c2f1dffd78e9","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cat \\u003e ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/probe-sc.mjs \\u003c\\u003c 'EOF'\\nconst res = await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:42889/api/missions', {\\n  headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer 4ba797357cbca..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:31:46.273605215Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"areview-code-ddc0eec3e3bdb5cf","agent_type":"review-code","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"python3 - \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nimport json, subprocess\nids=set()\nfor l in open('~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/trace.jsonl'):\n    if l.strip(): ids.add(json.loads(l)['id'])\nfor e in json.load(open('~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/list.json')): ids.add(e['mission_id'])\nE='~/.local/bin/ethos'\nshow_fail=[]; log_fail=[]\nfor i in sorted(ids):\n    s=subprocess.run([E,'mission','show',i,'--json'],capture_output=True,cwd='\u003crepo\u003e')\n    l=subprocess.run([E,'mission','log',i,'--json'],capture_output=True,cwd='\u003crepo\u003e')\n    if s.returncode!=0: show_fail.append(i)\n    if l.returncode!=0: log_fail.append(i)\nprint(\"total ids:\",len(ids))\nprint(\"show fails (-\u003e HTTP 404):\",len(show_fail), show_fail[:6])\nprint(\"log fails:\",len(log_fail), log_fail[:6])\nprint(\"show OK but log fails (-\u003e HTTP 500):\",len([i for i in log_fail if i not in show_fail]))\nEOF","description":"Measure detail-endpoint failure blast radius across all 155 missions"},"tool_input_hash":"e083d356ab1e0898e5b39f2b274cbfd496030ea829ad4a9458349b77b31c781d","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"python3 - \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\nimport json, subprocess\\nids=set()\\nfor l in open('~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/trace.jsonl'):\\n    if l.strip(): ids.add(json.loads(l)['id'])\\nfor e in json.l..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:31:50.61148451Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"areview-invariants-318c24525bb29751","agent_type":"review-invariants","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Invariant audit of spike/thin-slice: all 5 claims…","message":"Invariant audit of spike/thin-slice: all 5 claims CONFIRMED; several claim-shaped prose assertions in the repo are stale or wrong. Note: the branch advanced mid-review — fae82d1 (\"surface success_criteria on GET /api/missions\") is now HEAD above bffb8cf, and it invalidates some prose written at bffb8cf (details below).\n\n1. Union/dedup — CONFIRMED. Merge is a map keyed on normalized id (spike/deskd/missions.go:149-205): trace lines keyed \"id\" (missions.go:15), list entries \"mission_id\" (missions.go:32), enrichment contract \"mission_id\" (missions.go:44) all land in missionSummary.ID — map keys make \"each id exactly once\" structural. Verified live against the ethos store: find=105 lines (104 unique), list=125, union=155 (30 find-only, 51 list-only); merged status distribution computed independently = closed 129, failed 18, abandoned 7, escalated 1 — exactly matches API-NOTES.md:29-30. No category dropped: 6 of the 7 abandoned and most failed missions are absent from the trace log and arrive via the list+enrich path. One data quirk the merge silently tolerates: `find missions` emits m-2026-07-26-013 twice (differing only in closed_at: 2026-08-07 vs 2026-08-21); last-line-wins in the map. Harmless today (same status/verdict), but if duplicate trace lines ever disagreed on verdict, the earlier one is discarded without notice.\n\n2. Bearer auth / OPTIONS — CONFIRMED. All four routes are /api/* and registered on one mux (main.go:67-71) wrapped whole by withMiddleware (main.go:85); the auth check (middleware.go:66-76) applies to every non-OPTIONS /api/* request. OPTIONS returns 204 pre-auth with no body and never reaches a handler (middleware.go:61-64) — the exemption cannot leak into GET (exact method equality). Structural caveat worth one line in the report: enforcement is a path-prefix string check, not a wrapper around route registration — a future route registered outside /api/ (e.g. /healthz) would be silently unauthenticated. True today because no such route exists.\n\n3. UI honesty — CONFIRMED with ONE defect, opposite polarity: apps/desk/src/lib/timeline.ts:83 labels a row that has created_at but no closed_at as source:'none', so PeekPanel.tsx:140,156 renders \"not recorded — no created/closed timestamps on this record\" while created_at IS recorded (and a real created point was even built at timeline.ts:73-75, then discarded). Contradicts timeline.ts's own doc comment (lines 52-58, \"fall back to the two real timestamps the list row already carries\"). Latent — no open mission exists in the live dataset — but the open-mission fixture m-2026-09-11-007 shape hits it. Everything else is clean: NotRecorded affordances throughout PeekPanel, prompt excerpt labeled \"capped at 500 chars\" (PeekPanel.tsx:66), missing prompt.md labeled (line 71), Sidebar/TopBar mark unbuilt nav \"not built in this kit\", no mock/fake/sample values anywhere in apps/desk/src, avatars fall back to handle initials never invented names (roster.ts:26-28).\n\n4. open_questions correction — CONFIRMED: `mission show --json` does NOT drop it. Three independent proofs: (a) the m-007 fixture itself, spike/ui/fixtures/show-m-2026-07-21-001.json, has \"open_questions\" at lines 230, 445, 669 — one per round, matching the raw results-m-2026-07-21-001.yaml (lines 105, 262, 420) item-for-item; (b) live `ethos mission show m-2026-07-21-001 --json | grep -c open_questions` = 3; (c) API-NOTES.md:56-71 records the same two checks plus how the original error happened. Therefore spike/ui/fixtures/README.md finding 5 (lines 59-71) and the parenthetical at lines 24-25 are STALE AND FALSE — correct statement: \"mission show --json carries open_questions on each round result; spike/ui's raw-YAML workaround was unnecessary.\" The spike report should record the correction and flag that README as needing the fix.\n\n5. Write-set (bffb8cf) — CONFIRMED: all 23 files in the commit are under apps/desk/src/ (verified via git show --name-only; includes src/assets/, src/vite-env.d.ts — all inside).\n\nOther untrue claim-shaped assertions found:\n- API-NOTES.md:10-12,34-35 (\"no per-source variation... no success_criteria at all\") and the matching justification in format.ts:17-23 and types.ts MissionSummary (\"mirror what deskd actually returns\", no success_criteria field) were true at bffb8cf but are FALSIFIED by fae82d1: deskd now serializes SuccessCriteria on GET /api/missions (missions.go:76,163,213), and all 105 live find rows carry non-empty success_criteria. rowHeadline's \"no cheap description\" rationale no longer holds; the report should not repeat the \"155 objects of exactly this shape\" sentence as-is.\n- spike/ui/fixtures/README.md finding 4 (\"Round-level verdict has four real values: pass|fail|escalate|abandoned\") — misattributed level. Live round-level results.yaml verdicts across the whole store: pass 80, fail 7, escalate 8, zero abandoned; 'abandoned' exists only as a MISSION-level verdict (find-missions.jsonl, e.g. m-2026-08-21-007). apps/desk types.ts gets this right (MissionResult.verdict is three-valued, top-level Verdict four-valued); the README wording is wrong.\n- grouping.ts:22-31 comment: \"no cheap way to tell delegated from reflecting\" is overstated — deskd's summaryFromContract sets verdict from the last submitted result (missions.go:215-217), so an open mission with a landed result WOULD carry row.verdict, a free distinguisher. Also \"every open row defaults to delegated\" understates the default branch: groupFor's default (grouping.ts:43-44) swallows any unknown future status as 'delegated', not just 'open'.\n\nFiles: ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/deskd/{missions,middleware,main}.go, ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/src/{API-NOTES.md,types.ts,lib/{format,grouping,timeline}.ts,components/PeekPanel.tsx}, ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/ui/fixtures/README.md.","recipient":"team-lead","summary":"Invariant audit: 5 claims verified, plus stale prose","to":"team-lead","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"dcaa39cb8f9bf951a4b300b33bbaab9a13c8338dd160f749363a63fb546dd047","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Invariant audit of spike/thin-slice: all 5 claims…\",\"message\":\"Invariant audit of spike/thin-slice: all 5 claims CONFIRMED; several claim-shaped prose assertions in the repo are stale or..."}
