{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:32:08.318271907Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Add these to your current pass (all mechanical, f…","message":"Add these to your current pass (all mechanical, from the invariant review): (1) apps/desk/src/lib/timeline.ts:83 — a row with created_at but no closed_at is labeled source:'none' so the UI says \"not recorded\" while created_at IS recorded (the built created point at :73-75 gets discarded); fix so the real timestamp renders — this is an honesty defect in the opposite direction. (2) Since you're wiring success_criteria: update the now-stale prose it falsifies — API-NOTES.md:10-12,34-35 (\"no success_criteria at all\"), format.ts:17-23 rationale, types.ts MissionSummary comment. (3) grouping.ts:22-31 comment overstates \"no cheap way to tell delegated from reflecting\" (deskd sets row.verdict from the last result — a free distinguisher; use it or soften the comment), and note the default branch swallows unknown statuses as 'delegated'. (4) spike/ui/fixtures/README.md — two corrections, fine to commit there too since it's your own m-007 area: finding 5 (open_questions dropped) is FALSE, replace with \"show --json carries open_questions per round; the raw-YAML workaround was unnecessary\"; finding 4's four verdict values are MISSION-level — round-level is three-valued (pass/fail/escalate), fix the wording. One or two commits, tsc clean, reply done.","recipient":"worker-ui","summary":"Add invariant-review fixes to your pass","to":"worker-ui","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"956dbd48f12d4d92abf5529a0d616a50d37f7c56bd77b9149514fe508e8cadfc","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Add these to your current pass (all mechanical, f…\",\"message\":\"Add these to your current pass (all mechanical, from the invariant review): (1) apps/desk/src/lib/timeline.ts:83 — a row ..."}
