{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:32:29.537133148Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"All four fixed in one commit (de362de, spike/desk…","message":"All four fixed in one commit (de362de, spike/deskd/{fs,identity,missions}.go):\n\n- session_err=\u003cerr\u003e vs session=no-active-session, distinctly logged, still returns the empty roster either way.\n- mission-show 404 only when the CLI's error names a missing mission (isNotFoundErr checks \"no mission matching\"/\"not found\"); everything else is 500.\n- identities gets the same json.Valid guard as session — 500 + identities=invalid-json note on non-JSON stdout.\n- excerpt() cuts on a rune boundary now (converts to []rune first), can't split a multi-byte UTF-8 char.\n\ngofmt/vet clean. Verified live: no-session case logs \"session=no-active-session\", bad mission ID still 404 with the CLI's own text. (Side note: hit a filename collision testing this — another live deskd-inspect process was writing to the same .tmp/deskd3.out/err path I'd picked; not mine, didn't touch it, just moved my own verification to a private .tmp subdir and cleaned it up after.)","recipient":"team-lead","summary":"silent-failure review findings fixed, done","to":"team-lead","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"135b303079164e36ef60397cc7b27a5db27428566f1ca0296060c823cf8ba3ca","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"All four fixed in one commit (de362de, spike/desk…\",\"message\":\"All four fixed in one commit (de362de, spike/deskd/{fs,identity,missions}.go):\\n\\n- session_err=\\u003cerr\\u003e vs session=..."}
