{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:32:46.473043553Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"ps -o pid,ppid,lstart,cmd -p 2139020 2\u003e\u00261\nreadlink -f /proc/2139020/cwd 2\u003e\u00261","description":"Inspect the process holding port 1420"},"tool_input_hash":"7bb645d5a873cfee852e231b1d1de148ebea54ba4e244a5ee3b58589cc5dcbd8","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"ps -o pid,ppid,lstart,cmd -p 2139020 2\\u003e\\u00261\\nreadlink -f /proc/2139020/cwd 2\\u003e\\u00261\",\"description\":\"Inspect the process holding port 1420\"}"}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:32:48.485518383Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git commit apps/desk/src-tauri/src/lib.rs tools/shot/shot.sh -m \"fix: surface sidecar failures, distinguish fallback screenshots\n\nReview findings (HIGH + MEDIUM):\n\n- lib.rs sidecar event loop was silently dropping deskd's stderr,\n  Terminated, and Error events, and any stdout line that failed to\n  parse as the {port,token} handshake — every real startup failure\n  was indistinguishable from 'still starting,' surfacing to the\n  frontend only as the generic 10s daemon_info timeout. Now eprintln!s\n  each case with the actual cause.\n\n- tools/shot/shot.sh's wait-for-selector fallback wrote the same\n  filename and printed the same success line whether the app rendered\n  correctly or the selector never showed. A row-less screen and a\n  broken app now produce visibly different artifacts: \u003cslug\u003e.png on\n  the happy path, \u003cslug\u003e-fallback.png with an explicit 'wrote\n  FALLBACK ...' line otherwise. Exit code stays 0 either way — a\n  row-less screen is a legitimate shot, just not the same one.\n\nVerified: make shot SCREEN=/ (several retries — deskd's ethos-lock\nhandshake flake, and this run also caught a real transient\n'Failed to load missions: Failed to fetch' from deskd's /api/missions\nunder the same host contention, correctly landing in\nroot-fallback.png instead of masquerading as success). A clean run\nproduced apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png showing the live Missions list\nrendered from real deskd data.\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -10","description":"Commit the review fixes"},"tool_input_hash":"c4fb1be6c919dc373c6cc595390f5c49928ed75930cff41d9783592a8a9e7ae4","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git commit apps/desk/src-tauri/src/lib.rs tools/shot/shot.sh -m \\\"fix: surface sidecar failures, distinguish fallback screenshots\\n\\nReview findings..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:32:52.316711393Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"areview-code-ddc0eec3e3bdb5cf","agent_type":"review-code","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 python3 - \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nimport json, collections, os, glob\n# 1. created_at ties among the 155\nt=[json.loads(l) for l in open('.tmp/trace.jsonl') if l.strip()]\nc=collections.Counter(x['created_at'] for x in t)\nprint(\"duplicate created_at values in trace:\", [k for k,v in c.items() if v\u003e1][:5], \"count:\",len([k for k,v in c.items() if v\u003e1]))\n# 2. byte-slicing prompt.md at 500 -\u003e split rune?\nbad=[]\nfor p in glob.glob('\u003crepo\u003e/.punt-labs/ethos/missions/*/delegations/*/prompt.md'):\n    b=open(p,'rb').read()\n    if len(b)\u003c=500: continue\n    try: b[:500].decode('utf-8')\n    except UnicodeDecodeError: bad.append(p)\nprint(\"prompt.md files where a 500-BYTE cut splits a UTF-8 rune:\", len(bad))\nfor p in bad[:3]: print(\"  \", p.split('missions/')[1])\nEOF","description":"Check created_at ties and UTF-8 rune splitting at 500 bytes"},"tool_input_hash":"4771286aa0cd16acd172a1aca43b4a3e31e68350713582cb041c7567bcad40a3","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 python3 - \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\nimport json, collections, os, glob\\n# 1. created_at ties among the 155\\nt=[json.loads(l) for l in open('.tmp/trace.json..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:32:56.094731247Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Done — commit 85a12c1 on spike/thin-slice, apps/d…","message":"Done — commit 85a12c1 on spike/thin-slice, apps/desk/src-tauri/src/lib.rs + tools/shot/shot.sh only.\n\nHIGH (lib.rs:61-76): sidecar event loop now eprintln!s CommandEvent::Stderr lines verbatim, CommandEvent::Terminated with code/signal, CommandEvent::Error, and any stdout line that fails to parse as the handshake (with the parse error) — no more silent drops masquerading as the generic timeout.\n\nMEDIUM (shot.sh): fallback screenshot now writes \u003cslug\u003e-fallback.png (not \u003cslug\u003e.png) with a distinct \"==\u003e wrote FALLBACK ...\" line; exit stays 0.\n\nVerified with make shot SCREEN=/ — took several retries, and usefully one of them caught a real transient \"Failed to load missions: Failed to fetch\" from deskd under the same host contention, which correctly landed in root-fallback.png instead of reading as success (exactly the failure mode the fix targets). A clean run produced apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png showing the live Missions list rendered from real deskd data — viewed and confirmed.","recipient":"main","summary":"done: both review fixes committed and verified, PNG confirmed","to":"main","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"7c9dc3a15b7f42e12b9a796d3e321a7fbae790ba3f4daa33a8ef688e489855c3","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Done — commit 85a12c1 on spike/thin-slice, apps/d…\",\"message\":\"Done — commit 85a12c1 on spike/thin-slice, apps/desk/src-tauri/src/lib.rs + tools/shot/shot.sh only.\\n\\nHIGH (lib.rs:61..."}
