{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:35:45.226617632Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Final batch from code review, one commit under sp…","message":"Final batch from code review, one commit under spike/deskd/ (note: your de362de already covered the rune-split and identities-guard items — skip those): (1) middleware/handler: validate the id path param against ^m-\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}-\\d{3}$ at the top of missionDetailHandler → 400 on mismatch (closes an argv-injection-shaped gap: /api/missions/--help currently runs `ethos mission show --help`, and a %2e%2e traversal reaches filepath.Join latently). (2) fs reads should use the resolved contract's mission_id, not the raw URL param, so a prefix id can never blank delegations/artifacts as \"not recorded\" (belt to the regex's suspenders). (3) sessionHandler: return 200-empty ONLY when output matches the known \"No active session.\" prose; 5xx otherwise (a broken bridge must not read as an idle one — your de362de log split is good, now fix the HTTP contract too since it's 2 lines). (4) missions.go sort: SliceStable + ID tiebreak (unstable sort + 13 duplicate created_at values = rows jitter every cache refresh). (5) enrich loop: one bad `mission show` currently kills the whole /api/missions — skip-and-log the bad id instead, and surface a \"degraded\":[\"\u003cid\u003e\"...] field so it's not silent. gofmt/vet, verify /api/missions/--help → 400 and one degraded-path case, reply done with commit.","recipient":"worker-deskd","summary":"Final daemon batch: 5 review items","to":"worker-deskd","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"0d2a5c1c2236f32011366e772453bee776feda413498c0d877200a170f5f1a7c","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Final batch from code review, one commit under sp…\",\"message\":\"Final batch from code review, one commit under spike/deskd/ (note: your de362de already covered the rune-split and identiti..."}
