{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:36:18.047663124Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/src/lib/timeline.ts","new_string":" * Coarse, honest timeline: 1-3 checkpoints, never a padded fabrication.\n * With a real log, collapse to first event + last result (if any) + close\n * (if any). Without one — the detail fetch failed, or is still in\n * flight — fall back to whichever of the list row's own real timestamps\n * exist (created_at always if the row has one; closed_at too if set).\n */","old_string":" * Coarse, honest timeline: 2-3 checkpoints, never a padded fabrication.\n * With a real log, collapse to first event + last result (if any) + close\n * (if any). Without one — the detail fetch failed, or is still in\n * flight — fall back to the two real timestamps the list row already\n * carries (created_at, closed_at).\n */","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"1cf8d7749adf5b4a8663adee800107671eb3357b350b8946aa31f4d4554fe86f","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/src/lib/timeline.ts\",\"new_string\":\" * Coarse, honest timeline: 1-3 checkpoints, never a padded fabrication.\\n * With a real log, collapse to first event..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:36:24.750229258Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git add apps/desk/src-tauri/src/lib.rs \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"fix(lib.rs): own the sidecar child, kill it on app exit\n\n`let (mut rx, _child) = ...spawn()` dropped the CommandChild the\ninstant .setup() returned — CommandChild's Drop does not kill the\nprocess (per tauri-plugin-shell's own docs), so deskd's fate past\nthat point was either 'orphaned' or 'whatever the OS process-group\nteardown happens to do,' unknowable without actually running the\nTauri leg on a host with the webview toolchain. Now the child is\nstashed in managed state (SidecarChild) and killed explicitly from\nthe RunEvent::Exit handler — .run() is split from .build() so that\nhandler has somewhere to live.\n\nCorrect-by-inspection + rustc parse-check on this sandbox's apt\ntoolchain (still too old for a full cargo build, see\nm-2026-09-11-006's result — 17 unresolved-import errors, 0 syntax\nerrors, same shape as the prior two passes): cannot run-verify the\nTauri leg here without the webview libs and a newer Rust.\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -6","description":"Commit sidecar-ownership fix"},"tool_input_hash":"0cb4180c054050e5648aebc72983acc126bb29a1b47168bec670bfd5d264722b","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git add apps/desk/src-tauri/src/lib.rs \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"fix(lib.rs): own the sidecar child, kill it on app exit\\n\\n`let (mut rx, _child)..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:36:33.172663419Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/src/lib/grouping.ts","new_string":"/**\n * `GET /api/missions` doesn't carry round/current_round for an `open`\n * mission, but deskd's `verdict` field IS a free distinguisher: it's set\n * from the last result's verdict (summaryFromContract), which only\n * exists once a result has landed. So an open row with a `verdict` has a\n * result in and is \"reflecting\" (leader hasn't advanced/closed yet); an\n * open row with none is \"delegated\" (worker hasn't submitted). No extra\n * per-row detail fetch needed. In the live ethos repo dataset this daemon\n * serves, no mission is currently `open` at all (statuses observed:\n * closed/failed/abandoned/escalated only), so neither bucket has been\n * exercised with real data through this API yet.\n */\nexport function groupFor(row: MissionSummary): GroupKey {\n  switch (row.status) {\n    case 'closed':\n      return 'closed'\n    case 'failed':\n      return 'failed'\n    case 'escalated':\n      return 'escalated'\n    case 'abandoned':\n      return 'abandoned'\n    case 'open':\n      return row.verdict ? 'reflecting' : 'delegated'\n    default:\n      // Not one of MissionStatus's five values — an unrecognized status\n      // string the type doesn't model. Falls into \"delegated\" as a\n      // visible catch-all bucket rather than being silently dropped from\n      // the list; this is an assumption for an unmodeled case, not a\n      // verified classification.\n      return 'delegated'\n  }\n}","old_string":"/**\n * `GET /api/missions` carries no round/result info for an `open` mission\n * (deskd's missionSummary is deliberately thin — see types.ts), so there\n * is no cheap way to tell \"delegated\" (no result yet) from \"reflecting\"\n * (result landed, leader hasn't advanced) without an extra per-row detail\n * fetch. Every open row defaults to \"delegated\" — the more common case —\n * and this is a stated assumption, not a hidden one. In the live ethos\n * repo dataset this daemon serves, no mission is currently `open` at all\n * (statuses observed: closed/failed/abandoned/escalated only), so neither\n * bucket has ever been exercised with real data through this API.\n */\nexport function groupFor(row: MissionSummary): GroupKey {\n  switch (row.status) {\n    case 'closed':\n      return 'closed'\n    case 'failed':\n      return 'failed'\n    case 'escalated':\n      return 'escalated'\n    case 'abandoned':\n      return 'abandoned'\n    default:\n      return 'delegated'\n  }\n}","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"4fb6c3d20c7319c83bc227d7a3581f3b196b4b9721bf8b79d32022c5f071566d","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/src/lib/grouping.ts\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * `GET /api/missions` doesn't carry round/current_round for an `open`\\n * mission, but deskd's `verdict` field ..."}
