{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:37:13.601847178Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/src/API-NOTES.md","new_string":"Returns a flat array of 155 `missionSummary` objects (verified count).\nEvery object has exactly this shape — no per-source variation, no \"thin\"\nvs \"rich\" distinction like the m-007 spike's client-side union had:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"m-2026-08-22-053\",\n  \"status\": \"closed\",\n  \"type\": \"implement\",\n  \"leader\": \"claude\",\n  \"worker\": \"bwk\",\n  \"evaluator\": \"rsc\",\n  \"ticket\": \"ethos-268t\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T16:29:34Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-22T17:00:48Z\",\n  \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n  \"success_criteria\": [\"Bugbot MEDIUM finding on internal/hook/format_output.go …\", \"…\"]\n}\n```\n\nStatus distribution observed: `closed: 129, failed: 18, abandoned: 7,\nescalated: 1`. No `open` mission exists in this dataset — deskd is\npinned to the `ethos` repo (see `src-tauri/src/lib.rs`'s `SPIKE_REPO`\nconstant), which has none in flight at capture time.\n\n**Resolved gap.** `success_criteria` was originally absent from this\nendpoint (no description field at all — no criteria, no `context`, no\ntitle), forcing the row headline to fall back to `type` + `ticket`. Fixed\nserver-side in deskd commit `fae82d1`: `success_criteria[]` is now carried\nthrough from both merge sources (the find-missions trace log and\n`mission show`'s contract), `omitempty` when a mission genuinely has none.\n0 of 155 live missions currently lack it. `rowHeadline()`\n(`src/lib/format.ts`) prefers it (first criterion, sentence-boundary\ntrim) and only falls back to `type`/`ticket`/id for the record that has\nnone. The still-true \"no title field at all\" finding lives on in\n`../../spike/ui/fixtures/README.md` finding 1 — `success_criteria` is a\nreal criterion list, not a title, it's just usably title-shaped often\nenough to serve as one.","old_string":"Returns a flat array of 155 `missionSummary` objects (verified count).\nEvery object has exactly this shape — no per-source variation, no \"thin\"\nvs \"rich\" distinction like the m-007 spike's client-side union had:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"m-2026-08-22-053\",\n  \"status\": \"closed\",\n  \"type\": \"implement\",\n  \"leader\": \"claude\",\n  \"worker\": \"bwk\",\n  \"evaluator\": \"rsc\",\n  \"ticket\": \"ethos-268t\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T16:29:34Z\",\n  \"closed_at\": \"2026-08-22T17:00:48Z\",\n  \"verdict\": \"pass\"\n}\n```\n\nStatus distribution observed: `closed: 129, failed: 18, abandoned: 7,\nescalated: 1`. No `open` mission exists in this dataset — deskd is\npinned to the `ethos` repo (see `src-tauri/src/lib.rs`'s `SPIKE_REPO`\nconstant), which has none in flight at capture time.\n\n**Gap, real and worth fixing server-side:** there is no description field\nat all — no `success_criteria`, no `context`, no title. `type` + `ticket`\nis the only text a row can show without an extra per-mission fetch. The\nUI's `rowHeadline()` (`src/lib/format.ts`) is honest about this rather\nthan fabricating a title; see the same finding recorded for the spike-grade\nfixture set in `../../spike/ui/fixtures/README.md` finding 1 — it holds\njust as true against the live daemon.","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"08b86350e7aa099db8a16532a3d42474051b637c1ddf3ca1f6a9175685d3c5eb","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/src/API-NOTES.md\",\"new_string\":\"Returns a flat array of 155 `missionSummary` objects (verified count).\\nEvery object has exactly this shape — no per-s..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:37:16.932866943Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/deskd/cache.go","new_string":"func (c *missionsCache) set(data []byte, ttl time.Duration) {\n\tc.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer c.mu.Unlock()\n\tc.data = data\n\tc.expires = time.Now().Add(ttl)\n}\n\n// idSetsCache holds the two raw id views fetchIDSets computes, shared by\n// the missions list and detail handlers so a burst of detail requests\n// doesn't repeat the find-missions/mission-list pair per id.\ntype idSetsCache struct {\n\tmu      sync.Mutex\n\ttrace   map[string]missionSummary\n\tlisted  map[string]bool\n\texpires time.Time\n}\n\nfunc (c *idSetsCache) get() (map[string]missionSummary, map[string]bool, bool) {\n\tc.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer c.mu.Unlock()\n\tif time.Now().Before(c.expires) {\n\t\treturn c.trace, c.listed, true\n\t}\n\treturn nil, nil, false\n}\n\nfunc (c *idSetsCache) set(trace map[string]missionSummary, listed map[string]bool, ttl time.Duration) {\n\tc.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer c.mu.Unlock()\n\tc.trace = trace\n\tc.listed = listed\n\tc.expires = time.Now().Add(ttl)\n}","old_string":"func (c *missionsCache) set(data []byte, ttl time.Duration) {\n\tc.mu.Lock()\n\tdefer c.mu.Unlock()\n\tc.data = data\n\tc.expires = time.Now().Add(ttl)\n}","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"5a1d1ae95ee884988000623b93a94d6db5802d58f3a8689c3252d96fbf79f894","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/deskd/cache.go\",\"new_string\":\"func (c *missionsCache) set(data []byte, ttl time.Duration) {\\n\\tc.mu.Lock()\\n\\tdefer c.mu.Unlock()\\n\\tc.data = data\\n\\tc.expi..."}
