{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:37:20.878932596Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk \u0026\u0026 npx tsc --noEmit 2\u003e\u00261 \u0026\u0026 echo CLEAN","description":"Type-check apps/desk after review fixes"},"tool_input_hash":"14a9369b7612c11a0a189d54f1807eafa33598edac82553b592d23fa07ed5fc9","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk \\u0026\\u0026 npx tsc --noEmit 2\\u003e\\u00261 \\u0026\\u0026 echo CLEAN\",\"description\":\"Type-check apps/desk after review fixes\"}"}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:37:24.036218143Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/deskd/main.go","new_string":"// server holds the state shared by every handler: where the data comes\n// from (repo, ethos binary) and the caches for /api/missions.\ntype server struct {\n\trepo     string\n\tethosBin string\n\tcache    *missionsCache\n\tidSets   *idSetsCache\n\tcacheTTL time.Duration\n}","old_string":"// server holds the state shared by every handler: where the data comes\n// from (repo, ethos binary) and the /api/missions cache.\ntype server struct {\n\trepo     string\n\tethosBin string\n\tcache    *missionsCache\n\tcacheTTL time.Duration\n}","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"08ae622c55dc3a1f9d57ff629982f6499da6085d2bc6609c2d32172f06767bfd","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/deskd/main.go\",\"new_string\":\"// server holds the state shared by every handler: where the data comes\\n// from (repo, ethos binary) and the caches for /api/m..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:37:25.193135747Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-shell-8a310d7b0a566aee","agent_type":"worker-shell","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Done — commit 89dc301 on spike/thin-slice.\n\nFix: th…","message":"Done — commit 89dc301 on spike/thin-slice.\n\nFix: the tuple's `_child` binding is now `child`, stashed in new managed state `SidecarChild(Mutex\u003cOption\u003cCommandChild\u003e\u003e)` right after spawn. Split `.run(context)` into `.build(context)` + a separate `app.run(callback)` so there's a RunEvent handler to live in; on `RunEvent::Exit`, it takes the child out of state and calls `.kill()`, logging via eprintln! if that fails.\n\nVerification, as you flagged: can't run-verify the Tauri leg on this host (no webview libs, Rust too old — see m-2026-09-11-006's result). Did confirm via rustc parse-check: 17 unresolved-import errors (same shape/count-class as the prior two passes, +1 for the new tauri::RunEvent reference), 0 syntax errors.\n\nOne thing to flag on myself: my commit command had backticks inside a double-quoted -m message, which bash tried to interpret as command substitution — the commit still landed but the message's opening clause got silently stripped, AND because I ran a bare `git commit -m` (no pathspec, unlike my earlier commits) it swept in 4 already-staged .punt-labs/ethos/missions/*/log-*.jsonl files from the shared session's ethos audit trail (not mine, not secrets, legitimate tracked content per the ethos design — just not what I meant to commit under this message). Didn't reset/amend per the no-amend rule; flagging for visibility rather than silently leaving it. Let me know if you'd like it cleaned up differently.","recipient":"main","summary":"done: sidecar child now owned + killed on exit","to":"main","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"f0cc50faf8ea12d7ea40f891a78362c1763ad43313687e5a10525779e74aef89","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Done — commit 89dc301 on spike/thin-slice.\\n\\nFix: th…\",\"message\":\"Done — commit 89dc301 on spike/thin-slice.\\n\\nFix: the tuple's `_child` binding is now `child`, stashed in new mana..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:37:30.705415637Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/deskd/main.go","new_string":"\ts := \u0026server{\n\t\trepo:     absRepo,\n\t\tethosBin: *ethosBin,\n\t\tcache:    \u0026missionsCache{},\n\t\tidSets:   \u0026idSetsCache{},\n\t\tcacheTTL: *cacheTTL,\n\t}","old_string":"\ts := \u0026server{\n\t\trepo:     absRepo,\n\t\tethosBin: *ethosBin,\n\t\tcache:    \u0026missionsCache{},\n\t\tcacheTTL: *cacheTTL,\n\t}","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"daf9112ef65b5477b2d7a24680dbc30e19da1018998c8f62555991452ad18168","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/deskd/main.go\",\"new_string\":\"\\ts := \\u0026server{\\n\\t\\trepo:     absRepo,\\n\\t\\tethosBin: *ethosBin,\\n\\t\\tcache:    \\u0026missionsCache{},\\n\\t\\tidSets:   \\u0..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:37:33.783438188Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Accepted as-is, no cleanup: the swept-in mission …","message":"Accepted as-is, no cleanup: the swept-in mission log chunks were headed for a commit at wrap-up anyway (tracked-by-design ethos state), and a cosmetically clipped message on an unmerged spike branch isn't worth history surgery. The child-handle fix shape (managed SidecarChild + kill on RunEvent::Exit) is right and parse-clean is the best verification this host allows — the real proof runs when the operator lands the toolchain. You're done for the day; strong work throughout, особенно the portable-rust forensics.","recipient":"worker-shell","summary":"89dc301 accepted as-is; you're done","to":"worker-shell","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"1734b77e40d42ce88ba594ba2768e0fe52fbb011739722b30031a5fdd4d01b7e","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Accepted as-is, no cleanup: the swept-in mission …\",\"message\":\"Accepted as-is, no cleanup: the swept-in mission log chunks were headed for a commit at wrap-up anyway (tracked-by-design e..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:37:35.779613305Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/deskd \u0026\u0026 gofmt -l . ; gofmt -w . ; gofmt -l . \u0026\u0026 go vet ./... \u0026\u0026 go build -o /dev/null ./... \u0026\u0026 echo OK","description":"Format, vet, build after trace-only fix"},"tool_input_hash":"cbb61c22ad1fa79467e47c8f39fbb0f2c8a7262dbf12dffafed5d7b69527638d","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/deskd \\u0026\\u0026 gofmt -l . ; gofmt -w . ; gofmt -l . \\u0026\\u0026 go vet ./... \\u0026\\u0026 go build -o /dev/null ./... \\u0026\\u0026 echo OK\",\"descripti..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:37:42.699453906Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/ui/fixtures/README.md","new_string":"4. **Verdict appears at two levels with different value sets.**\n   Mission-level verdict (`find`/`list` rows) has four real values:\n   `pass | fail | escalate | abandoned`. Round-level result verdict\n   (`results[].verdict`) is three-valued — `pass | fail | escalate` —\n   `abandoned` never appears there, only as a mission-level terminal\n   state. `escalate` is not a failure at either level and is styled\n   distinctly (amber, not red).\n5. **CORRECTION (was wrong in an earlier draft of this file):**\n   `ethos mission show --json` does **not** drop `open_questions`.\n   `contract.results[].open_questions` is present and populated directly\n   on the JSON `show` output — verified live against the deskd daemon in\n   mission m-2026-09-11-011, and by re-grepping this very fixture file\n   (`grep -c open_questions show-m-2026-07-21-001.json` returns 3). The\n   original claim came from inspecting a `head -n 200` slice of the file\n   and a couple of key-extraction scripts that never checked for that\n   specific key, then \"confirming\" the false narrative by grepping the\n   raw YAML separately instead of the JSON already on disk. The\n   raw-YAML-parsing workaround this UI kit uses for\n   `m-2026-07-21-001` (`results-m-2026-07-21-001.yaml`, the `yaml`\n   package, `src/data/fixtures.ts`'s `loadOpenQuestionsByRound`) was\n   therefore unnecessary — `open_questions` should be read directly off\n   `full.results[]` like every other result field, same as\n   `apps/desk/src/components/PeekPanel.tsx` now does. Left in place here\n   for the historical record rather than fixed, since it's harmless\n   (the value it produces is correct) and not worth another commit to a\n   spike; do not copy the pattern.","old_string":"4. **Round-level verdict has four real values**, not two:\n   `pass | fail | escalate | abandoned`. `escalate` is not a failure and\n   is styled distinctly (amber, not red).\n5. **`ethos mission show --json` silently drops the `open_questions`\n   field.** It's a real, documented part of the `ethos mission result`\n   YAML schema (`ethos mission result --help` shows it in the escalate\n   example) and every round of `m-2026-07-21-001`'s raw `results.yaml`\n   has one or two entries — but the JSON `show` prints for that same\n   mission omits the field entirely. The UI reads the raw YAML directly\n   for this one mission (via the `yaml` package, `?raw` import) to\n   render the \"Open questions for the leader\" callout honestly; every\n   other mission's peek panel has no open-questions section because no\n   other mission had its raw YAML fetched, not because the field is\n   rare in the real data — grep'd, `open_questions:` appears in 28 of the\n   135 local `results.yaml` files. This CLI gap should be fixed before\n   any production read path is built on `mission show --json` alone.","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"3b2c07d0f6190c8b28ce59ade28fddb9637b33170342d735a62a774e779690c9","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/ui/fixtures/README.md\",\"new_string\":\"4. **Verdict appears at two levels with different value sets.**\\n   Mission-level verdict (`find`/`list` rows) has four..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:38:01.405487663Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/ui/fixtures/README.md","new_string":"- **`m-2026-07-21-001`** — 3-round pass, rich per-round reflection prose,\n  a captured `prompt.md`, and real structured `open_questions` on every\n  round (present directly in `show-m-2026-07-21-001.json`; see finding 5\n  for a correction to an earlier, wrong claim that it wasn't).","old_string":"- **`m-2026-07-21-001`** — 3-round pass, rich per-round reflection prose,\n  a captured `prompt.md`, and real structured `open_questions` on every\n  round (see finding 5 — pulled from the raw `results.yaml` because\n  `mission show --json` drops the field).","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"c18930f60730e0698057e1aa21494fd4400ef6b72f7d6fdbcccfa523f89b21d5","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/spike/ui/fixtures/README.md\",\"new_string\":\"- **`m-2026-07-21-001`** — 3-round pass, rich per-round reflection prose,\\n  a captured `prompt.md`, and real structu..."}
