{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:38:32.219681123Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git status --short -- spike/deskd \u0026\u0026 echo --- \u0026\u0026 git diff --stat -- spike/deskd","description":"Review changed files before commit"},"tool_input_hash":"8675aeb913bc8f37de4be249411f8981b63e3542c1e0fd3a5e740349e0a9ed53","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git status --short -- spike/deskd \\u0026\\u0026 echo --- \\u0026\\u0026 git diff --stat -- spike/deskd\",\"description\":\"Review changed files before comm..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:38:39.930404932Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nspike(deskd): stop 404ing trace-only missions\n\n30 of 155 ids exist only in the find-missions trace log -- their\nstore directories are gone, so `mission show`/`mission list` no\nlonger see them, and GET /api/missions/{id} 404d on 19% of rows.\n\nFactor the two id sets (trace log rows, ids mission list --status all\ncan still resolve) into fetchIDSets, shared by both handlers and\ncached alongside the existing /api/missions bytes cache:\n\n- GET /api/missions marks each trace-only item trace_only: true.\n- GET /api/missions/{id} for a trace-only id returns 200 with that\n  trace summary + trace_only: true, without attempting mission\n  show/log. Real 404s (unknown ids) are unaffected.\n\nVerified live against m-2026-05-21-005 (a trace-only id): 200 with\ntrace_only:true and no mission_show/mission_log calls in the log\nline; a real id still gets the full contract/log/delegations/\nartifacts detail; an unknown id still 404s.\nEOF\n)\" -- spike/deskd/cache.go spike/deskd/main.go spike/deskd/missions.go","description":"Commit the trace-only fix"},"tool_input_hash":"c0343acc5dbefa037c5a5dcc4d74b60316c3f4b8774aed783c2c5f6a945a0151","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"$(cat \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\nspike(deskd): stop 404ing trace-only missions\\n\\n30 of 155 ids exist only in the find-missions trace log --..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:38:46.554828792Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git add apps/desk/src/lib/daemon.ts apps/desk/src/lib/timeline.ts apps/desk/src/lib/grouping.ts \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\napps/desk/src: fix daemon retry, timeline honesty, and grouping signal\n\nThree review findings, all mechanical:\n\n- daemon.ts: daemonConnection() memoized a rejected promise forever —\n  one Tauri sidecar-not-ready timeout poisoned every later fetch even\n  after the sidecar came up. Clear the cache on rejection so the next\n  call retries, mirroring api.ts's detailCache delete-on-error.\n\n- timeline.ts: a row with created_at but no closed_at was labeled\n  source:'none', discarding the real created_at point and rendering\n  \"not recorded\" for a mission that DOES have a recorded timestamp —\n  an honesty defect in the opposite direction from what this UI is\n  supposed to guard against. Any row with created_at now renders it.\n\n- grouping.ts: the comment claimed there was \"no cheap way\" to tell\n  delegated from reflecting on an open mission, but deskd already sets\n  `verdict` from the last result's verdict — a free signal that a\n  result has landed. groupFor() now uses it; the comment no longer\n  overstates the gap. Also split the default switch branch out from\n  the 'open' case and noted that it swallows any unmodeled status\n  string into 'delegated' rather than pretending that's a verified\n  classification.\n\ntsc --noEmit clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 \[REDACTED:email]\u003e\nEOF\n)\" -- apps/desk/src/lib/daemon.ts apps/desk/src/lib/timeline.ts apps/desk/src/lib/grouping.ts","description":"Commit the mechanical bug fixes"},"tool_input_hash":"4e494e04986d626875fca78451adc855eb9375faab9c383d8d96aff364cef29c","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git add apps/desk/src/lib/daemon.ts apps/desk/src/lib/timeline.ts apps/desk/src/lib/grouping.ts \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"$(cat \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:38:46.840306967Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Done, commit b655eed on spike/thin-slice (spike/d…","message":"Done, commit b655eed on spike/thin-slice (spike/deskd/{cache,main,missions}.go).\n\nFactored the two id sets into fetchIDSets (find-missions rows + the mission-list id set), cached alongside the existing /api/missions bytes cache so a burst of detail requests doesn't repeat find+list per id. GET /api/missions marks each trace-only item trace_only:true; GET /api/missions/{id} for one returns 200 with that trace summary and trace_only:true, no mission show/log attempted — confirmed via the log line (find_missions=3ms mission_list=18ms, no mission_show/mission_log). Real ids and unknown ids are unaffected — verified m-2026-08-22-053 still gets the full contract/log/delegations/artifacts shape, and an unknown id still 404s.\n\nVerified live against m-2026-05-21-005 exactly as you named: confirmed first that its store dir is actually gone (`ls` fails, `mission show` errors \"no mission matching prefix\"), then got 200 + trace_only:true from deskd. Full /api/missions count matches your number: 30 of 155 trace_only.\n\ngofmt/vet clean.","recipient":"team-lead","summary":"trace-only fix done, commit b655eed","to":"team-lead","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"ce745cb0faad75a0a386173e2ca6bc4fe860b7911ff5b8a362bd80ddf65d3640","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Done, commit b655eed on spike/thin-slice (spike/d…\",\"message\":\"Done, commit b655eed on spike/thin-slice (spike/deskd/{cache,main,missions}.go).\\n\\nFactored the two id sets into fetchIDSe..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:39:01.907076779Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git add apps/desk/src/API-NOTES.md spike/ui/fixtures/README.md \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\ndocs: correct stale success_criteria and open_questions claims\n\nAPI-NOTES.md: the /api/missions gap writeup still said \"no\nsuccess_criteria at all\" after deskd's fae82d1 added the field —\nupdated the example payload and rationale to match what the API\nactually returns now (0/155 missions lack it).\n\nspike/ui/fixtures/README.md: two corrections to my own m-007 findings,\nmade now since this is the same area and the claims are simply wrong:\nfinding 5 said `mission show --json` drops `open_questions` — it\ndoesn't; verified live and by re-grepping the fixture file that's been\nsitting in this repo since m-007. Finding 4 conflated mission-level\nverdict (four values, including `abandoned`) with round-level result\nverdict (three values, no `abandoned`) — split them out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 \[REDACTED:email]\u003e\nEOF\n)\" -- apps/desk/src/API-NOTES.md spike/ui/fixtures/README.md","description":"Commit the documentation corrections"},"tool_input_hash":"10237f61c1456debdf931107b59e07dabe98e2f7b76e368184e86ebb729d7684","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git add apps/desk/src/API-NOTES.md spike/ui/fixtures/README.md \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"$(cat \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\ndocs: correct stale success_cri..."}
