{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:39:19.725082648Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"done. Two commits:\n\n6e9a671 (apps/desk/src/lib/{dae…","message":"done. Two commits:\n\n6e9a671 (apps/desk/src/lib/{daemon,timeline,grouping}.ts):\n- daemon.ts: daemonConnection() now clears the cached promise on rejection so a Tauri-not-ready timeout doesn't poison every later fetch — mirrors detailCache's delete-on-error in api.ts.\n- timeline.ts: fixed the honesty-in-the-wrong-direction bug — a row with created_at but no closed_at now renders that real point instead of being labeled source:'none' and showing \"not recorded\".\n- grouping.ts: groupFor() now uses row.verdict (set from the last result's verdict) as the free delegated/reflecting distinguisher for open missions; comment no longer overstates the gap. Split the unmodeled-status fallback out from the 'open' case with an honest note that it's an unverified catch-all, not a real classification.\n\na31a794 (docs only): API-NOTES.md's success_criteria writeup updated to match fae82d1 (0/155 missions lack it now). spike/ui/fixtures/README.md finding 5 corrected — open_questions is NOT dropped by show --json, verified live and by re-grepping the fixture file that's had it all along. Finding 4 split mission-level verdict (4 values) from round-level result verdict (3 values, no abandoned).\n\ntsc --noEmit clean both times.","recipient":"team-lead","summary":"done — daemon retry, timeline honesty, grouping, docs fixed","to":"team-lead","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"c4c3d42910cbf612fbf0292deda9e464de38aeb789065c916271b17935db09ce","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"done. Two commits:\\n\\n6e9a671 (apps/desk/src/lib/{dae…\",\"message\":\"done. Two commits:\\n\\n6e9a671 (apps/desk/src/lib/{daemon,timeline,grouping}.ts):\\n- daemon.ts: daemonConnection() now c..."}
