{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:42:23.690942498Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nspike(deskd): validate mission ids, fix session HTTP contract, degrade gracefully\n\nFive fixes from the final review batch (rune-split and identities\njson.Valid guard already covered by de362de):\n\n- missionIDPattern (^m-\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}-\\d{3}$) validated at the top\n  of missionDetailHandler, 400 on mismatch. Closes both the\n  /api/missions/--help-reaches-the-CLI-as-a-flag gap and a\n  traversal-shaped id reaching filepath.Join.\n- missionDetailHandler now parses the resolved contract and reads\n  delegations/artifacts by its mission_id, not the raw URL param.\n- sessionHandler: only the exact \"No active session.\" CLI-gap prose\n  gets the empty-roster 200. A real exec error or any other non-JSON\n  output is 5xx -- a broken bridge must not read as an idle one.\n- mergedMissions: sort.SliceStable with an id tiebreak, so 13 missions\n  sharing a created_at no longer jitter order on every cache refresh.\n- The enrichment loop skips a failed `mission show` instead of failing\n  the whole request, and reports the id in a new \"degraded\" field.\n\nBREAKING for callers: GET /api/missions is now {\"missions\": [...],\n\"degraded\": [...]} instead of a bare array.\n\nVerified live: /api/missions/--help -\u003e 400; a %2f-traversal-shaped id\n-\u003e 400; a wrapper ethos binary forcing one mission show to fail\nproduces degraded:[\"\u003cid\u003e\"] and count 154/155, with the failure logged\n(mission_show_failed(id=...)) rather than the whole request failing;\nreal ids, trace-only ids, and unknown ids all still behave correctly;\nsort order identical across repeated calls.\nEOF\n)\" -- spike/deskd/identity.go spike/deskd/missions.go","description":"Commit the final review batch"},"tool_input_hash":"b356d95a019f6afa06d4720cf3fd982828037f12ed023300529a06e4ed86e79f","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"$(cat \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\nspike(deskd): validate mission ids, fix session HTTP contract, degrade gracefully\\n\\nFive fixes from the fi..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:42:31.426304035Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-ui-85a325c3a077a9d5","agent_type":"worker-ui","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/src/components/MissionRowView.tsx","new_string":"      \u003cspan className={`mission-row-title ${derived ? '' : 'mission-row-title--faint'}`}\u003e{text}\u003c/span\u003e\n      {row.trace_only \u0026\u0026 (\n        \u003cspan className=\"mission-row-trace\" title=\"trace-log record only — full mission record no longer in the store\"\u003e\n          trace\n        \u003c/span\u003e\n      )}\n      {row.verdict \u0026\u0026 \u003cBadge variant={verdictVariant(row.verdict)}\u003e{row.verdict}\u003c/Badge\u003e}","old_string":"      \u003cspan className={`mission-row-title ${derived ? '' : 'mission-row-title--faint'}`}\u003e{text}\u003c/span\u003e\n      {row.verdict \u0026\u0026 \u003cBadge variant={verdictVariant(row.verdict)}\u003e{row.verdict}\u003c/Badge\u003e}","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"ca88a27e9c20b97194c86767349cd356fa4097d87ea81e33c7d9b8baa1ac1ddf","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/src/components/MissionRowView.tsx\",\"new_string\":\"      \\u003cspan className={`mission-row-title ${derived ? '' : 'mission-row-title--faint'}`}\\u003e{tex..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:42:33.869494378Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Done, commit fb6bf8c on spike/thin-slice (spike/d…","message":"Done, commit fb6bf8c on spike/thin-slice (spike/deskd/{identity,missions}.go).\n\n1. missionIDPattern (^m-\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}-\\d{3}$) checked at the top of missionDetailHandler, 400 on mismatch.\n2. FS reads now use the parsed contract's mission_id, not the raw URL param.\n3. sessionHandler: only exact \"No active session.\" prose gets the empty-roster 200; a real exec error or any other unexpected non-JSON output is now 5xx.\n4. sort.SliceStable + id tiebreak in mergedMissions.\n5. Enrichment loop skips-and-logs a failed mission show instead of failing the whole request; failed ids surface in a new \"degraded\" field.\n\nVerified live:\n- GET /api/missions/--help -\u003e 400 {\"error\":\"invalid mission id \\\"--help\\\", want m-YYYY-MM-DD-NNN\"}\n- A %2f-encoded traversal-shaped id -\u003e 400, never reached the CLI or filesystem.\n- Wrapper ethos binary forcing `mission show m-2026-08-01-001` to fail: /api/missions came back 200 with degraded:[\"m-2026-08-01-001\"], missions count 154/155, and the log line shows mission_show_failed(id=m-2026-08-01-001)=\u003cthe error\u003e — request didn't fail.\n- Real ids, trace-only ids, unknown ids, identities, session (real passthrough) all still behave as before.\n- Sort order identical across repeated /api/missions calls.\n\nOne thing that needs to reach worker-shell/worker-ui directly, flagging separately: item 5 required GET /api/missions to become an object ({\"missions\":[...],\"degraded\":[...]}) instead of a bare array, since a JSON array can't carry a named field. That's a breaking shape change for anyone already consuming it as an array — sending them a heads-up now.","recipient":"team-lead","summary":"final review batch done, commit fb6bf8c — one breaking change to flag","to":"team-lead","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"8e4f0e7dd8a059805972a94067093bca7cb848ad9fafa6466d747933b514260f","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Done, commit fb6bf8c on spike/thin-slice (spike/d…\",\"message\":\"Done, commit fb6bf8c on spike/thin-slice (spike/deskd/{identity,missions}.go).\\n\\n1. missionIDPattern (^m-\\\\d{4}-\\\\d{2}-\\\\d..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:42:36.654942528Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Heads up before you pull latest: GET /api/mission…","message":"Heads up before you pull latest: GET /api/missions changed shape in commit fb6bf8c (spike/thin-slice). It's now {\"missions\": [...], \"degraded\": [...]} instead of a bare array — the team lead asked for a \"degraded\" field to surface any mission whose enrichment call failed, and you can't add a named field to a JSON array. GET /api/missions/{id} is unchanged for normal/trace-only ids, but now 400s on a malformed id (was previously passed straight to the CLI). If anything on the frontend/shell side parses /api/missions as an array directly, it'll need `.missions` added. Let me know if this lands somewhere unexpected.","recipient":"worker-shell","summary":"breaking change: GET /api/missions is now an object, not an array","to":"worker-shell","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"61cc13abf22ae7e28bfc77aa570c775b9aa51950b658bce1d651ed422ab98063","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Heads up before you pull latest: GET /api/mission…\",\"message\":\"Heads up before you pull latest: GET /api/missions changed shape in commit fb6bf8c (spike/thin-slice). It's now {\\\"missions..."}
