{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:42:42.597137036Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-deskd-8cc8192e6dcc72db","agent_type":"worker-deskd","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Heads up: GET /api/missions changed shape in comm…","message":"Heads up: GET /api/missions changed shape in commit fb6bf8c on spike/thin-slice (spike/deskd/). It's now {\"missions\": [...], \"degraded\": [...]} instead of a bare array — needed a named field to surface any mission whose enrichment failed, which a JSON array can't carry. GET /api/missions/{id} is unchanged for normal/trace-only responses, but now returns 400 on a malformed id instead of passing it straight to the CLI. If your fixtures or fetch code in spike/ui treat /api/missions as an array directly, they'll need a `.missions` accessor now.","recipient":"worker-ui","summary":"breaking change: GET /api/missions is now an object, not an array","to":"worker-ui","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"fcb71a9e5a35977fdcce2ed7229a9c9e147021fbe49b4ab4a8f7779c4658b1dd","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Heads up: GET /api/missions changed shape in comm…\",\"message\":\"Heads up: GET /api/missions changed shape in commit fb6bf8c on spike/thin-slice (spike/deskd/). It's now {\\\"missions\\\": [....."}
