{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:42:47.2260465Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Heads-up folded into your remaining batch (worker…","message":"Heads-up folded into your remaining batch (worker-deskd may have pinged you too): GET /api/missions changed shape in fb6bf8c — now {\"missions\":[...],\"degraded\":[\"\u003cid\u003e\",...]} instead of a bare array (needed to carry the degraded-enrichment field). Adapt api.ts/types.ts to the envelope, and render degraded ids somewhere honest but quiet (e.g. a one-line notice above the list: \"N missions could not be fully loaded\"). That plus your remaining three items (trace-only peek state, spike/ui yaml-workaround removal, README 104-vs-125 count) completes your batch — verify against the rebuilt daemon, reply done with commits.","recipient":"worker-ui","summary":"API shape change: adapt client in your batch","to":"worker-ui","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"0e0b28a17df4355f784a2e7184ace144bfabbb81f508fe34462130339f18facd","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Heads-up folded into your remaining batch (worker…\",\"message\":\"Heads-up folded into your remaining batch (worker-deskd may have pinged you too): GET /api/missions changed shape in fb6bf8..."}
