{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:52:28.228198001Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"git -C ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk commit -m \"chore(ethos): mission records for the thin-slice spike\n\nFour missions, all closed pass round 1: m-005 deskd bridge daemon\n(bwk/rsc), m-006 Tauri shell + shot rig (adb/kth), m-007 fixture-driven\nMissions UI kit (edt/dna), m-011 live integration (edt/dna).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 \[REDACTED:email]\u003e\"","description":"Commit mission records"},"tool_input_hash":"562e424942398fff9257e0341422ce511c5d31fff6f3e31a764fffcc58e7f99a","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"git -C ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk commit -m \\\"chore(ethos): mission records for the thin-slice spike\\n\\nFour missions, all closed pass round 1: m-005 deskd bridge daemon\\n(bwk/rsc), m-006 Tau..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T05:52:56.493543177Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/PLAN.md","new_string":"### Spike result — thin slice, 2026-09-11 (branch `spike/thin-slice`, unmerged)\n\nOne-day end-to-end slice: this repo's sibling ethos store (155 missions) →\n`spike/deskd` Go bridge daemon (shells the `ethos --json` CLI) → the\nLinear-pattern Missions UI in `apps/desk` → verified by leader-run\n`make shot` (real PNG, real data, read back by the agent). Four ethos\nmissions, all closed pass round 1 (m-2026-09-11-005/-006/-007/-011,\nrecords committed). Three local review agents ran; every finding fixed\nsame-day or accepted-and-documented. **Two of three legs proven** —\ndaemon↔ethos and browser-UI↔daemon; the native Tauri leg compiles-blocked\non host toolchain (below), its Rust code parse-checked only.\n\n**Exit-question verdicts:**\n\n1. *CLI-with-pixels invariant* — **held, with a measured residue**: the UI\n   needed only 4 endpoints over CLI output plus FS reads for exactly the\n   gaps the research predicted (prompt.md, artifacts, delegation\n   enumeration). New gap found live: no title-shaped field exists;\n   `success_criteria[0]` is a workable headline (landed daemon-side).\n2. *Real data vs the design* — **design held; data taught**: trace log is\n   missing 51 of 155 missions (not only open ones — closed/failed/\n   abandoned/escalated too), 30 of 155 are trace-only ghosts whose store\n   dirs are gone (now honest `trace_only` records, not 404s), round-level\n   verdicts are three-valued vs four at mission level, duplicate trace\n   line for one id. Attribution honesty generalized into a UI principle.\n3. *Exec-per-request latency* — **daemon-with-cache wins**: cold\n   `/api/missions` 314 ms (dominated by 51-id enrich fan-out, ~5 ms each),\n   warm 0–1 ms; detail 17 ms cold. Verdict for S2-proper: keep the\n   sidecar daemon; cold path parallelizes trivially; zero-spinner bar is\n   met warm and missable cold.\n4. *Tauri sidecar on this machine* — **blocked, precisely diagnosed**: no\n   host Rust at all; apt tops out at 1.75 vs the ~1.85 (`edition2024`)\n   Tauri 2's tree needs; webkit dev libs absent. Operator installs\n   (rustup + apt list) convert this to a ~10-minute `make dev`. Sidecar\n   code (spawn, stdout handshake, managed child, kill-on-exit) is written\n   and parse-clean.\n5. *Agent visual loop* — **decisive**: caught a clipped-layout defect on\n   first use (mockup phase), a wrong-diagnosis screenshot (rig waited on\n   `load`, not data — fixed with wait-for-selector + honest `-fallback.png`\n   artifacts), and drove 4+ UI iteration rounds. Screenshot evidence now\n   lives in mission results.\n\n**Ethos CLI bugs found (file upstream):** `session --json` emits prose\n\"No active session.\" with exit 0; `mission list` defaults to open-only\n(reads as empty store); `find missions` vs `mission list` disagree on the\nid field name (`id` vs `mission_id`); trace log carries a duplicate line\n(m-2026-07-26-013); `mission dispatch --write-set` repeated flags override\ninstead of append (leader had to hand-amend a contract; also\n`mission result` hard-rejects out-of-write-set files, so the quirk\nblocks result submission). One false alarm corrected on the record:\n`mission show --json` does NOT drop `open_questions` (m-007's claim,\ndisproven in m-011).\n\n**Ops findings (multi-agent on one host):** `ethos` session-lock\ncontention makes daemon startup ~50% flaky under concurrent agents\n(mitigated: 30 s poll budget); vite EMFILE under load; leaked dev-server\nprocesses squat port 1420 (strictPort) and can serve a stale app to the\nshot rig — kill before runs. Process notes: one worker ran `git stash`/\n`pop` in the shared tree (lossless, self-reported, verified); leader\nedited two contract fields by hand (write-set amendment) due to the\ndispatch flag bug.\n\n**Next:** operator runs the two installs → `make dev` native-window\nproof (completes leg 3) → S1 blame spike is the next new risk to retire.\n\n## 10. Phases by increasing confidence","old_string":"## 10. Phases by increasing confidence","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"f328804a1ae196505427f9270bccb4abc00d233ebe60ca84ddec5244a329063c","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/PLAN.md\",\"new_string\":\"### Spike result — thin slice, 2026-09-11 (branch `spike/thin-slice`, unmerged)\\n\\nOne-day end-to-end slice: this repo's sibling ethos st..."}
