{"ts":"2026-09-11T12:42:40.88610046Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"---\nname: desk-native-not-browser\ndescription: Desk is a native Tauri desktop app — browser mode is a test path, never the product to demo\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nThe desk GUI (Punt Labs workspace, ethos v1 module) is a **native Tauri\ndesktop app** — that is the founding premise (\"build this in Tauri modelled\noff Block\"; Lux rejected for UI-framework robustness; \"a GUI is what makes\nethos real\"). The operator reacted strongly (2026-09-11) when offered\nbrowser mode as the way to \"run it interactively.\"\n\n**Why:** The browser path (vite + VITE_DESKD_URL) exists ONLY for the\nPlaywright test tier and CI. Handing the operator a browser tab presents\nthe test harness as the product and undercuts the entire native-app thesis.\n\n**How to apply:** When the operator asks to run/demo desk, the answer is\nthe native window (`make dev`) — and if the host toolchain blocks it\n(rustup ≥1.85 + webkit2gtk dev libs), say so and drive the unblock; never\nsubstitute browser mode for a demo unless the operator explicitly asks for\nit. Browser mode remains fine for agents' screenshot loops and CI.\n","file_path":"~/.claude/projects/-home-jfreeman-Coding-punt-labs-ethos/memory/desk-native-not-browser.md"},"tool_input_hash":"d43059ef336c7ceb324ac91ffb79ac3839d106d0edcd4f4d6b0c34929488d61b","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"---\\nname: desk-native-not-browser\\ndescription: Desk is a native Tauri desktop app — browser mode is a test path, never the product to demo\\nmetadata:\\n  type: feedback\\n---\\n\\nThe desk..."}
