{"ts":"2026-09-11T12:44:29.868876239Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 ethos mission correct m-2026-09-11-006 --kind factual --claim \"Result verdict pass implied the Tauri shell deliverable was verified\" --corrected \"The shell implementation is complete but has never compiled or executed - no Rust \u003e=1.85 toolchain and no webkit dev libs exist on this host. Verified was only the adjacent shot rig and daemon. Accurate status: implemented, verification blocked on host toolchain; the leader should have escalated the operator-resolvable blocker at hour 0 instead of closing pass. Leader error, not worker error - the worker documented the blockers prominently and accurately.\" --evidence \"cargo build or tauri dev ever executed=fail\" --evidence \"rustc parse-check only=pass\" --evidence \"make shot browser-path PNG=pass\"","description":"File factual correction against m-006's pass verdict"},"tool_input_hash":"c50279de1e29cc96e440dbf350ae53e89baf1cbf97f6620e7d412a54ba66eb3e","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 ethos mission correct m-2026-09-11-006 --kind factual --claim \\\"Result verdict pass implied the Tauri shell deliverable was verified\\\" --corrected \\..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T12:44:39.452491876Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"---\nname: verification-requires-running\ndescription: Never claim verified/pass for code that has never executed; escalate operator-resolvable blockers immediately\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nDuring the desk thin-slice spike (2026-09-11), the leader closed mission\nm-2026-09-11-006 (Tauri shell) as `pass` although the shell had never\ncompiled, let alone run — host lacked Rust ≥1.85 and webkit dev libs. The\noperator's reaction: \"How can you verify software without ever running it?\"\nA factual correction was filed against the mission (DES-072 mechanism).\n\n**Why:** Phase 3 of the org workflow (\"the feature was actually run,\ndriven through its real entry point\") is absolute. Parse-checks, lint,\nand adjacent-path evidence (browser rig, curl) verify only what they\ntouch. Code that never executed is unverified, whatever else is green.\nRelated: [[desk-native-not-browser]], [[bias-to-real-work]].\n\n**How to apply:**\n1. A mission whose deliverable never executed cannot close `pass` —\n   verdict is escalate/blocked, and the record says exactly what did and\n   did not run.\n2. When a blocker is operator-resolvable (sudo installs, logins,\n   toolchains), STOP and ask the operator at the moment it's discovered —\n   don't engineer around it for hours and let the gap reach the report.\n3. In any status/report, separate \"ran and observed\" from\n   \"written and believed\" explicitly, every time.\n","file_path":"~/.claude/projects/-home-jfreeman-Coding-punt-labs-ethos/memory/verification-requires-running.md"},"tool_input_hash":"4d87ecd4829c15382c1c86ebc0d39918a62c9612a52c2e9d163db3584e87cdb7","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"---\\nname: verification-requires-running\\ndescription: Never claim verified/pass for code that has never executed; escalate operator-resolvable blockers immediately\\nmetadata:\\n  type: fee..."}
