{"ts":"2026-09-11T13:12:23.319069564Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"---\nname: no-freelance-design\ndescription: Do not freelance UI design — copy named references literally; design decisions belong to the operator's UX workshop\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nOn the desk thin slice (2026-09-11), the operator judged the shipped UI\n\"the same as the earlier cognitive overload design\" and said \"I told you\nnot to freelance on the design.\" The leader had made his own v0 mockup the\nvisual spec in mission contracts, skipping the UX workshop the operator had\nalready scheduled, and labeled the result \"Linear patterns\" while it was\nactually an interpretation (6 data elements per row; 5 stacked peek\nsections — vs real Linear's dot + title + 1-2 quiet chips).\n\n**Why:** \"Follow established patterns\" means copy the reference literally\nand let the operator rule on deltas — not produce an original design that\ncites references. Density that reads fine in a mockup becomes cognitive\noverload as a working app. Related: [[desk-native-not-browser]],\n[[bias-to-real-work]].\n\n**How to apply:**\n1. Design authority = the operator, exercised through the UX workshop;\n   until a workshop ruling exists, screens clone a named reference\n   screen-for-screen (Linear for lists/detail, GitHub for blame bands).\n2. When building, present deltas from the reference as decisions\n   (\"Linear does X, we do Y — adopt X?\"), never as silently shipped taste.\n3. Never promote a self-made mockup into a contract's \"visual spec\"\n   without the operator ratifying that mockup explicitly.\n","file_path":"~/.claude/projects/-home-jfreeman-Coding-punt-labs-ethos/memory/no-freelance-design.md"},"tool_input_hash":"8bd9563d7f0ded980670178acc7bd04446ced12f591c43352bebd2916305e240","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"---\\nname: no-freelance-design\\ndescription: Do not freelance UI design — copy named references literally; design decisions belong to the operator's UX workshop\\nmetadata:\\n  type: feedb..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T13:12:42.474086688Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/.claude/projects/-home-jfreeman-Coding-punt-labs-ethos/memory/no-freelance-design.md","new_string":"The operator's sharpening: \"You are not looking at linear, notion, or any\nother modern tooling\" — one marketing-page screenshot is not reference\nstudy. Actual product screens of modern tools must be in front of whoever\ndesigns, before and during the work.\n\n**How to apply:**","old_string":"**How to apply:**","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"fe6eb8f13c6ec95ba42a93514a6d85772ec1c6295b38fff0b78de1cfc4ffec45","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.claude/projects/-home-jfreeman-Coding-punt-labs-ethos/memory/no-freelance-design.md\",\"new_string\":\"The operator's sharpening: \\\"You are not looking at linear, notion, or any\\nother mo..."}
