{"ts":"2026-09-11T13:19:26.199078866Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"# UX teardown — desk vs real modern tooling (2026-09-11)\n\nInput for the operator's UX workshop. Every delta below is a decision for\nthe operator; nothing ships unruled. Reference captures (not committed —\nother companies' product shots) live in `ethos/.tmp/ux-refs/`:\n`linear-docs-concepts.png` (real issues list), `linear-home.png` (real\nissue detail + properties rail), `linear-docs-issue.png` (composer),\n`notion-viewport.png` (board school), `github-blame.png` (blame bands),\n`berd-readme-full.png`. Ours: `desk/apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png`.\n\n## What the references actually do\n\n**Linear issues list** (docs capture, real app):\n\n- Row = tiny priority glyph · status circle · **muted small id** · title in\n  **plain weight** · right side: 0–3 tiny label chips · muted date · small\n  avatar. One line, ~32 px. Nothing bold. Most rows carry almost nothing on\n  the right.\n- Chrome: view tabs as pills (All / Active / Backlog / custom), a `Filter`\n  button left, a `Display` button right, group headers with counts.\n- Color: label dots and priority glyphs only. No colored status text.\n\n**Linear issue detail** (homepage capture, real app): ONE dominant element\n(title), description prose under it, then an Activity feed (compact,\nnewest few). **All metadata lives in a right properties rail** — small\nrows: Status, Priority, Assignee, Cycle, Labels — never inline sections in\nthe body. Composer (docs): title → description → properties as small pills\nat the *bottom*.\n\n**Notion** (product capture): the opposite school — soft color group\npills, white cards, friendly. Named here so the school choice is explicit,\nnot accidental.\n\n**GitHub blame**: age heat-strip; attribution in commit-spanning *bands*,\nnot per-line labels.\n\n## What we shipped (root.png) vs the reference\n\nOur row: status glyph + mono id + **criteria-sentence headline** + colored\n`pass` chip + confidence number + date + avatar — 6–7 elements of equal\nweight. Our peek panel: big bold title (same criteria sentence again) +\nstatus chips + five stacked expanded sections (Ask / Came back / Criteria\n/ Timeline / Mechanics). This is an original design citing Linear, not\nLinear. Operator verdict: cognitive overload, same as the mockup.\n\n## Delta decisions (rule each: adopt / keep ours / other)\n\n| # | Reference does | We do | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| D1 | Short human title, plain weight | Full first success criterion (clause-length) | Trim to ≤ ~60 chars at a word boundary; plain weight; full criterion only in detail |\n| D2 | ≤ 5 quiet row elements, whitespace dominant | 6–7 equal-weight elements | Drop verdict chip + confidence from rows (status glyph already encodes outcome); date + avatar go muted |\n| D3 | Detail = title + description + activity; metadata in right properties rail | Five stacked sections | Rebuild peek as Linear anatomy: \"the ask\" is the description; \"what came back\" is the newest activity entry; worker/evaluator/verdict/rounds/ticket become a properties rail; Mechanics stays a collapsed disclosure |\n| D4 | `Filter` + `Display` buttons, pill view tabs | Text toggle \"List · Board · Lanes\", lone search box | Adopt Linear chrome (stubs acceptable in spike) |\n| D5 | Color = dots/glyphs only | Colored verdict chips in every closed row | Verdict color only in the properties rail and status glyph |\n| D6 | 13 px base, ~32 px rows, detail title ~16 px medium | 36 px rows, 20 px bold panel title | Adopt Linear scale |\n| D7 | School: Linear monochrome-pro vs Notion soft-color | Near-black monochrome | Confirm Linear school explicitly (assumed from prior ruling) |\n| D8 | Search: sidebar icon + ⌘K, no persistent wide box | Persistent wide search box | Icon + ⌘K; retire the box |\n| D9 | Blame: commit-spanning bands + age strip | (not yet built) | Bind for the future Blame screen now |\n\n## Process rulings already in force\n\nDesign authority is the operator via this workshop; screens clone named\nreference screens until ruled otherwise; deltas are presented, never\nsilently shipped (memory: no-freelance-design).\n","file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/docs/ux-teardown-2026-09-11.md"},"tool_input_hash":"29465c031d88c1e44160155063f30c342e243e5df10fc376643c8865d593c9ca","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"# UX teardown — desk vs real modern tooling (2026-09-11)\\n\\nInput for the operator's UX workshop. Every delta below is a decision for\\nthe operator; nothing ships unruled. Reference capt..."}
