{"ts":"2026-09-11T13:43:05.575533353Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"convert ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png -crop 740x290+230+140 +repage -resize 200% ours-rows-crop.png \u0026\u0026 convert linear-docs-concepts.png -crop 420x180+620+365 +repage -resize 350% linear-rows-crop.png \u0026\u0026 identify ours-rows-crop.png linear-rows-crop.png","description":"Crop row regions from ours and Linear at readable scale"},"tool_input_hash":"429ac904502031b6fce6811d421336d01d12d6bd421027c6b9bb1c7a9fac87ba","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"convert ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png -crop 740x290+230+140 +repage -resize 200% ours-rows-crop.png \\u0026\\u0026 convert linear-docs-concepts.png -crop 420x180+620+..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T13:43:48.532916665Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/docs/ux-teardown-2026-09-11.md","new_string":"## Density analysis (same-scale row crops: `ours-rows-crop.png` vs `linear-rows-crop.png`)\n\nLinear's row density is **variable**: a heavy row (6 chips) sits next to a\nnear-empty one; metadata renders only where it differentiates, and exactly\none element per row is white (the title) — everything else is 2–3\nluminance steps down, chips ghost-outlined. Ours is **uniform-maximal**:\nevery row stamps glyph + 13-char id + title + bright verdict chip + date +\navatar even when the values are identical down the column (8× `pass`, 8×\n`Aug 22`, 8× `BK` in one screen = zero information transmitted). Our\ncriteria-fragment titles truncate mid-word on nearly every row; Linear's\nshort titles rarely truncate.\n\n| # | Reference does | We do | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| D10 | Metadata only where it discriminates | Same chips/date/avatar stamped per row | Suppress a row value when constant within the visible group (worker, date, verdict); the group header or rail can carry it once |\n| D11 | 7-char ids (`ENG-139`) | 13-char ids with constant prefix | Elide the shared prefix within a group (`…-053`); full id on hover/detail |\n| D12 | One white element per row; the rest stepped down | Title, id, chip near-equal brightness | Adopt a one-bright-element luminance rule |\n\n## Process rulings already in force","old_string":"## Process rulings already in force","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"45970b8d09fb0769a2fc1fc503b59b9aea80f2367706250c6dfb69e4b01567b7","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/docs/ux-teardown-2026-09-11.md\",\"new_string\":\"## Density analysis (same-scale row crops: `ours-rows-crop.png` vs `linear-rows-crop.png`)\\n\\nLinear's row density i..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T13:43:55.640452563Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"\u003crepo\u003e/.tmp/ux-refs/teardown.html","new_string":"\u003ch2\u003eDensity — same-scale row crops\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp class=\"cap\"\u003eOurs: uniform-maximal — every row stamps all six elements at full brightness even when identical down the column (8× pass, 8× Aug 22, 8× BK = zero information). Linear: variable — heavy rows next to near-empty ones, metadata only where it differentiates, exactly one white element per row. → D10 D11 D12\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"pair\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"tag\"\u003eOurs\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg src=\"ours-rows-crop.png\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cdiv\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"tag\"\u003eLinear\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg src=\"linear-rows-crop.png\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch2\u003eSide by side — list anatomy\u003c/h2\u003e","old_string":"\u003ch2\u003eSide by side — list anatomy\u003c/h2\u003e","replace_all":false},"tool_input_hash":"3a51355ae4155f189da27369d0058cfd1f84d102d7f7ca2c86a9032ef0068f7a","tool_input_preview":"{\"file_path\":\"\\u003crepo\\u003e/.tmp/ux-refs/teardown.html\",\"new_string\":\"\\u003ch2\\u003eDensity — same-scale row crops\\u003c/h2\\u003e\\n\\u003cp class=\\\"cap\\\"\\u003eOurs: uniform-maximal — every row s..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-11T13:44:04.364054815Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport base64, re, pathlib\nhtml = pathlib.Path('teardown.html').read_text()\ndef embed(m):\n    src = m.group(1)\n    p = pathlib.Path(src.replace('file://','')) if src.startswith('file://') else pathlib.Path(src)\n    data = base64.b64encode(p.read_bytes()).decode()\n    return f'src=\\\"data:image/png;base64,{data}\\\"'\nhtml = re.sub(r'src=\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"', embed, html)\npathlib.Path('teardown-embedded.html').write_text(html)\nprint('ok', len(html)//1024, 'KB')\n\" \u0026\u0026 cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 npx --yes markdownlint-cli2 docs/ux-teardown-2026-09-11.md \u0026\u0026 git add docs/ux-teardown-2026-09-11.md \u0026\u0026 git commit -q -m \"docs(ux): density analysis — uniform-maximal vs Linear's variable density; D10-D12\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 \[REDACTED:email]\u003e\" \u0026\u0026 echo committed","description":"Re-embed teardown page; lint and commit density analysis"},"tool_input_hash":"92e85fa5f4121c5369f3912ad3be4def248f2fe7c6756d3e470f1ade430210ea","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport base64, re, pathlib\\nhtml = pathlib.Path('teardown.html').read_text()\\ndef embed(m):\\n    src = m.group(1)\\n    p = pathlib.Path(src.replace('file://','')) if src.sta..."}
