{"ts":"2026-09-11T14:20:28.770418378Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Rebuild Missions UI to D1-D12","name":"worker-redesign","prompt":"You are the worker on ethos mission m-2026-09-11-021. cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice — verify, never switch), run `ethos mission show m-2026-09-11-021`, and read `docs/ux-teardown-2026-09-11.md` end-to-end — it contains the operator's ruling: deltas D1–D12 all adopted. You built this screen (missions m-007/m-011); now rebuild it to the ruling. Pixels only: everything stays inside apps/desk/src/**; no daemon, config, or src-tauri changes.\n\nReference images to study FIRST (Read each PNG before coding): \u003crepo\u003e/.tmp/ux-refs/linear-docs-concepts.png (real Linear list), linear-detail-crop.png (real Linear issue detail, enlarged), linear-rows-crop.png vs ours-rows-crop.png (the density comparison that drove D10–D12). Clone the reference; do not reinterpret it.\n\nDelta specs (D-numbers from the teardown doc):\n- D1: row headline = success_criteria[0] trimmed to ≤60 chars at a word boundary, PLAIN weight (400–450), single line; full criterion lives only in the peek.\n- D2: rows LOSE the verdict chip and confidence number. The status glyph alone encodes outcome. Date muted; avatar 16–18px.\n- D6: 13px base type; 32px row height; peek title 16px medium (not 20 bold).\n- D10 (variable density): within each visible group, compute which of {verdict, date, avatar/worker} are CONSTANT across the group's rows; render a constant value ONCE in the group header (e.g. \"Closed 129 · all pass · Aug 22 · BK\") and OMIT it from every row. A value renders per-row only when it varies. This is the core fix — eight identical chips is zero information.\n- D11: elide the constant id prefix within a group: display the shortest differentiating tail (e.g. \"…053\" or \"08-22-053\" when days vary); full id via title attr and in the peek header.\n- D12: one bright element per row — the headline at full text color; id, date, avatar, everything else 2–3 luminance steps down (use your muted/faint tokens).\n- D3 (peek anatomy, clone linear-detail-crop.png adapted to the 430px panel): (1) header — full mono id small+muted, then title 16px medium; (2) a Linear-style compact properties block: one quiet row each (small icon/glyph + value) for status, worker → evaluator, round n of m, ticket, write-set count — muted, tight; (3) \"the ask\" as plain description PROSE (no boxed card, no provenance-chip header line — just a small muted \"Ask · d-…-129\" caption above the text); (4) Activity: newest result as a compact entry (author, verdict glyph, confidence muted, prose), older rounds and timeline events collapsed under one \"Show earlier activity\" disclosure; (5) Mechanics stays a collapsed \u003cdetails\u003e at the bottom. Criteria render as plain muted bullets inside the description area after the ask.\n- D4: top chrome — view switcher becomes Linear-style pills (List active; Board, Lanes as disabled stubs); add ghost \"Filter\" and \"Display\" buttons (non-functional stubs are fine, style them right).\n- D5: color discipline — colored pixels allowed ONLY: status glyphs, the verdict glyph in properties/activity, label-dot-like accents. No colored text chips anywhere.\n- D7: keep the near-black Linear school theme.\n- D8: retire the wide persistent search box; a search icon + \"/\" or ⌘K hint that expands to an input on focus.\n\nLoop discipline: after each meaningful change run `make shot SCREEN=/` (retry on the known daemon-handshake flake; also `rm`-check for a stale vite on 1420 and kill YOUR OWN leaked ones only), READ the PNG, compare against linear-docs-concepts.png / linear-detail-crop.png, fix, repeat. Minimum 3 look-iterate cycles. Final evidence: at least list + peek screenshots saved under apps/desk/.tmp/shots/ and referenced in your result.\n\ntsc --noEmit clean; commit per logical step on spike/thin-slice; submit `ethos mission result` (round 1, author edt) with verdict, screenshots, and any spec ambiguities you had to resolve (note them explicitly — do NOT silently invent; if a delta is ambiguous, pick the closest-to-reference option and flag it). Report back the same.","subagent_type":"edt"},"tool_input_hash":"0b2190539e85e220863ae99d722ba10f7a554eac934a1b7e7a71329a6310335a","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"Rebuild Missions UI to D1-D12\",\"name\":\"worker-redesign\",\"prompt\":\"You are the worker on ethos mission m-2026-09-11-021. cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice — verify, ..."}
