{"ts":"2026-09-11T14:37:37.757410456Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"mission: m-2026-09-11-021\nround: 1\nauthor: edt\nverdict: pass\nconfidence: 0.85\nfiles_changed:\n  - path: apps/desk/src/App.css\n    added: 201\n    removed: 114\n  - path: apps/desk/src/components/Badge.tsx\n    added: 0\n    removed: 7\n  - path: apps/desk/src/components/GroupHeader.tsx\n    added: 13\n    removed: 1\n  - path: apps/desk/src/components/MissionRowView.tsx\n    added: 17\n    removed: 8\n  - path: apps/desk/src/components/MissionsScreen.tsx\n    added: 39\n    removed: 20\n  - path: apps/desk/src/components/PeekPanel.tsx\n    added: 200\n    removed: 125\n  - path: apps/desk/src/lib/density.ts\n    added: 75\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src/lib/format.ts\n    added: 85\n    removed: 27\nevidence:\n  - name: tsc --noEmit clean (apps/desk)\n    status: pass\n  - name: make shot SCREEN=/ — list+peek screenshot (apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png)\n    status: pass\n  - name: D10/D11 verified live via search-filtered group (\"CLOSED 10 · all pass\", \"FAILED 3 · DM\", \"ESCALATED 1 · all escalate · Aug 21 · DM\" with per-row date/avatar correctly suppressed) — apps/desk/.tmp/shots/review-density-filtered.png\n    status: pass\n  - name: Activity \"Show earlier activity\" disclosure verified on a 3-round mission (m-2026-07-21-001) — apps/desk/.tmp/shots/review-earlier-expanded.png\n    status: pass\nopen_questions:\n  - \"D10 ambiguity: took 'group' literally as the whole status bucket (Delegated/Reflecting/Closed/Failed/Escalated/Abandoned), matching the ruling's own example ('Closed 129 · all pass · Aug 22 · BK'). On the live 155-mission dataset the Closed bucket alone spans 19 dates and 10 workers, so literal whole-group-constant almost never fires there (verified via the API: 128/129 pass but 2 distinct verdicts, 12 workers, 19 dates) — the mechanism is correct and I verified it firing exactly as designed on smaller/filtered groups (FAILED 3, ESCALATED 1, and any search-narrowed Closed set), but it delivers little visible density reduction on the unfiltered Closed bucket specifically, since real production data rarely holds one constant value across 129 rows. I did not invent a finer sub-grouping (e.g. by day) to force more suppressions, since that would add a UI concept (sub-headers) the ruling didn't authorize — flagging for a ruling if the leader wants that follow-up.\"\n  - \"D3 ambiguity: when a mission has zero results (row.status !== 'open', no delegation ever resulted in a round), the spec's 'older rounds + timeline collapsed under one disclosure' has nothing to anchor the disclosure to. Resolved by showing the timeline directly (uncollapsed) in that case instead of nesting a single-item disclosure with nothing to collapse — closest-to-reference option rather than losing the real created/closed timestamps.\"\n  - \"D3 ambiguity: open_questions inside an activity entry keeps its warn-colored callout box (unchanged from before). This isn't strictly a 'text chip' under D5's letter, but it is a colored background — flagging it as the one surviving non-glyph color usage, kept because it's a load-bearing 'needs a decision' signal, not decoration.\"\n  - \"Confirmed (not an ambiguity, but worth recording): make shot's teardown trap does not reliably kill its own vite on success — I found and killed two of my own leaked vite processes on port 1420 across this session (verified via each process's VITE_DESKD_URL env matching a deskd port I had just started) before they'd have blocked a teammate's next make shot. tools/shot/shot.sh is outside this mission's write set so I didn't fix it, but the leader may want a bead for it.\"\nprose: |\n  Rebuilt the Missions screen to D1-D12 per docs/ux-teardown-2026-09-11.md's ruling. Pixels only, all inside apps/desk/src/**.\n\n  Data layer (lib/format.ts, new lib/density.ts): rowHeadline now trims to \u003c=60 chars at a word boundary (D1); detailHeadline shows the full untruncated criterion in the peek. density.ts computes per-group constants (verdict/date/worker) for D10 and the group-level id-prefix elision for D11.\n\n  Row/group (MissionRowView, GroupHeader, MissionsScreen): dropped the verdict chip + confidence entirely, the status glyph alone encodes outcome (D2); a row only shows date/avatar when they vary within the group, otherwise the group header carries the constant once (\"Closed 129 · all pass · Aug 22 · BK\") (D10); ids collapse to the shortest differentiating tail within the group, full id on hover (D11); 32px rows, plain-weight bright title as the one colored/bright element, everything else stepped down (D6/D12).\n\n  Chrome: ghost Filter/Display stub buttons flanking Linear-style view pills; search retired its persistent box for an icon+\"/\" trigger that expands to an input on focus (D4/D8).\n\n  Peek (PeekPanel): rebuilt to Linear anatomy — mono id + 16px/500 title, a quiet properties rail (status, worker-\u003eevaluator, round, ticket, write-set count, one row each, no colored chips), \"the ask\" as plain description prose with a small muted caption (no box, no provenance-chip header) and criteria as muted bullets right after it, and an Activity feed (newest result compact with only the verdict glyph colored, older rounds + timeline collapsed under one \"Show earlier activity\" disclosure) (D3/D5). Removed Badge.tsx — dead code once every colored verdict/status chip in both the row and the peek was replaced by a glyph or plain text.\n\n  Verified live (not just via make shot's default view): filtered the list to a single worker/mission via the new search trigger and confirmed D10 fires correctly on genuinely-constant groups (FAILED 3 -\u003e \"DM\" once in the header, no per-row avatar; ESCALATED 1 -\u003e \"all escalate · Aug 21 · DM\" in the header, the one row below shows only glyph+id+title), and confirmed the Activity \"Show earlier activity\" disclosure expands a 3-round mission's older rounds correctly. Screenshots: apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png (make shot, list+peek), review-density-filtered.png, review-earlier-expanded.png (ad hoc Playwright verification, not from make shot since it has no interaction support).\n\n  Two commits on spike/thin-slice: ca67429 (data layer + row/group/peek components) and 81f49fe (CSS for chrome/rows/peek). tsc --noEmit is clean after each.\n","file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/missions/m-2026-09-11-021-result.yaml"},"tool_input_hash":"b976db79e985e86ac893e04dbfc866559cf59bd4b99f3ed3f7742485ab56ac94","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"mission: m-2026-09-11-021\\nround: 1\\nauthor: edt\\nverdict: pass\\nconfidence: 0.85\\nfiles_changed:\\n  - path: apps/desk/src/App.css\\n    added: 201\\n    removed: 114\\n  - path: apps/desk/sr..."}
