{"ts":"2026-09-11T14:38:45.08734172Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Mission m-2026-09-11-021 done. Rebuilt the Missio…","message":"Mission m-2026-09-11-021 done. Rebuilt the Missions screen (apps/desk/src/**, pixels only) to D1-D12 per docs/ux-teardown-2026-09-11.md. Round 1 result submitted: verdict=pass, confidence=0.85.\n\nTwo commits on spike/thin-slice:\n- ca67429 — data layer + row/group/peek component rebuild (lib/format.ts, new lib/density.ts, MissionRowView, GroupHeader, MissionsScreen, PeekPanel; removed Badge.tsx as dead code)\n- 81f49fe — CSS for chrome/rows/peek (32px rows, 16px/500 peek title, ghost Filter/Display buttons, search trigger, properties rail, activity feed)\n\ntsc --noEmit clean after each commit. Did 3+ look-iterate cycles, including ad hoc interactive Playwright verification beyond make shot's static default view (make shot has no click/search interaction).\n\nScreenshots (apps/desk/.tmp/shots/):\n- root.png — make shot SCREEN=/, list+peek together (default view: Closed group, 129 rows spanning many dates/workers)\n- review-density-filtered.png — search-filtered to prove D10 fires on real constant groups: \"FAILED 3 · DM\" (worker suppressed per-row), \"ESCALATED 1 · all escalate · Aug 21 · DM\" (date+worker suppressed on the one row below)\n- review-earlier-expanded.png — \"Show earlier activity\" disclosure expanded on a 3-round mission\n\nThree ambiguities I resolved rather than silently inventing, flagged in the result's open_questions (also in results.yaml, not yet committed since .punt-labs/ethos/missions/** is outside my write-set):\n\n1. D10 \"group\" = the literal whole status bucket, matching the ruling's own example. On the live 155-mission dataset the Closed bucket (129 rows) spans 19 dates/10 workers, so it almost never hits 100%-constant — verified via the API this isn't a bug, real data just has more variety than the ruling's example assumed. The mechanism does work correctly (verified above on smaller/filtered groups). I did not invent day-level sub-grouping to force more suppressions since that's a new UI concept the ruling didn't authorize — worth a ruling if you want that follow-up.\n2. D3: when a mission has zero results, there's nothing to anchor \"newest result + collapsed older\" to. I show the raw timeline directly instead of nesting a single-item disclosure with nothing to collapse.\n3. D3/D5: open_questions inside an activity entry keeps its warn-colored callout box — not literally a text chip, but the one surviving non-glyph color. Kept it since it's a \"needs a decision\" signal, not decoration.\n\nAlso found and killed two of my own leaked `make shot` vite processes on port 1420 across the session (each verified via its VITE_DESKD_URL env before killing, per the loop discipline note). tools/shot/shot.sh's teardown trap doesn't reliably fire on success — outside my write-set to fix, but worth a bead.\n\nFull result: `ethos mission show m-2026-09-11-021` / `ethos mission results m-2026-09-11-021`.","recipient":"main","summary":"m-2026-09-11-021 done — Missions screen rebuilt to D1-D12, result submitted pass","to":"main","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"6a8d302b2c693fb8de6fb76c1c5c11dc13de91804332fc3b9dd112d8e837401f","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Mission m-2026-09-11-021 done. Rebuilt the Missio…\",\"message\":\"Mission m-2026-09-11-021 done. Rebuilt the Missions screen (apps/desk/src/**, pixels only) to D1-D12 per docs/ux-teardown-2..."}
