{"ts":"2026-09-12T01:38:26.743118915Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"New mission m-2026-09-12-001 — cd ~/…","message":"New mission m-2026-09-12-001 — cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice), `ethos mission show m-2026-09-12-001`. This replaces the peek-panel layout you built: the operator rejected it (390px detail gutter, titles truncating into 800px of dead row space).\n\nClone Linear's actual navigation model, literally, from the references you already have:\n1. REMOVE the permanent side panel. List view is FULL WIDTH. Click/Enter on a row navigates to a full detail view; Esc or breadcrumb (\"Missions / m-…-016\") returns to the list with scroll+selection preserved.\n2. Detail view = linear-detail-crop.png at full size: centered prose column (max-width 720-760px) with title (2-line cap + expand), the ask as description (~6-line excerpt + \"show full\"), activity entries ONE line collapsed (author + verdict glyph + first sentence, click to expand), evidence collapsed past 4 items; properties rail fixed ~280px on the RIGHT (status, worker→evaluator, round, ticket, write-set), Mechanics \u003cdetails\u003e at rail bottom.\n3. Row title flexes: `flex:1; min-width:0` with ellipsis ONLY on true overflow — kill the fixed title width. Meta (date, avatar) right-aligned, gap tight.\n4. Headline precedence: contract.context if the API provides it, else ticket, else trimmed criterion; when two visible rows collide exactly, append \" · \u003cticket-or-id-tail\u003e\". (If context isn't in the list payload, use ticket-else-criterion and note the daemon gap in your result — do NOT touch the daemon.)\n5. Show the WORKER delegation's prompt in the ask (records carry agent_type; the evaluator prompt starting \"You are the pinned evaluator\" must never render as the ask — label the section \"Ask · \u003cworker handle\u003e\").\n6. Normalize YAML literal-block newlines: join single \\n within paragraphs, keep \\n\\n as breaks, preserve list lines starting with -, *, digits, or ✓.\n7. Default list scope: \"Recent\" = missions with activity in the last 14 days, grouped by day (e.g. \"Sep 11 · 6\"); an \"All\" pill loads the full store grouped by status as now.\nLoop: after each step `make shot SCREEN=/` (retry flake), READ the PNG NEXT TO linear-docs-concepts.png / linear-detail-crop.png in the same look, fix, repeat — grade against the reference, never in isolation. Also capture the detail route (make shot with the mission route or Playwright click). tsc clean, commit per step, `ethos mission result` with screenshots + flagged ambiguities. Report back.","recipient":"worker-redesign","summary":"New mission: layout rebuild to Linear, literal","to":"worker-redesign","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"b8ee87444f6dd38d37d06b3b5f5077a170e05930f2f1653e54f732019889f403","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"New mission m-2026-09-12-001 — cd ~/…\",\"message\":\"New mission m-2026-09-12-001 — cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk (branch spike/thin-slice), `ethos mission show m-2026-09-12-001`. This rep..."}
