{"ts":"2026-09-12T01:52:10.92021329Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nmissions ux: replace peek panel with Linear's full-detail navigation model\n\nOperator rejected the permanent 430px peek panel (dead row space, titles\ntruncating early). Clone Linear literally instead:\n\n- List is full width. Selecting a row (click, or Enter on the\n  keyboard-highlighted row) pushes /missions/\u003cid\u003e and renders a full\n  MissionDetailView; Esc or the breadcrumb (\"Missions / m-...\") returns\n  to the list with scroll position + selection preserved. Plain\n  history.pushState/popstate — no router dependency, and it makes\n  `make shot SCREEN=/missions/\u003cid\u003e` work for detail-route evidence.\n- MissionDetailView: centered ~760px prose column (title 2-line clamp +\n  expand, ask ~6-line clamp + expand, one-line collapsed activity\n  entries that expand to full prose/evidence-past-4/open-questions) with\n  a fixed 280px properties rail on the right; Mechanics stays a\n  collapsed \u003cdetails\u003e at the rail's bottom.\n- Headline precedence changes to context \u003e ticket \u003e trimmed criterion\n  (types.ts models `context` even though it's confirmed absent from the\n  live list payload — daemon gap, not touched) with a collision\n  discriminator (\" · \u003cticket-or-id-tail\u003e\") when two visible rows resolve\n  to the same text. Row/detail titles no longer pre-truncate in JS —\n  CSS ellipsis/line-clamp does the clipping against the row's real\n  width instead of a fixed 60-char budget.\n- \"The ask\" now shows the WORKER's delegation prompt specifically\n  (lib/delegation.ts): deskd's delegation records carry no agent_type\n  field (probed live — id+prompt_excerpt only), so the evaluator's\n  prompt is excluded by its own conventional \"You are the pinned\n  evaluator\" prefix rather than a real classification.\n- lib/prose.ts normalizes YAML literal-block text: joins wrapped single\n  newlines into real paragraphs, keeps blank-line paragraph breaks, and\n  preserves list/checklist lines (-, *, digit., ✓, ✕) verbatim.\n- Default list scope is \"Recent\" (activity in the last 14 days, grouped\n  by day, e.g. \"Sep 11 · 6\"); \"All\" is the previous status-grouped view,\n  now behind a pill.\nEOF\n)\""},"tool_input_hash":"bcf64431f10fa08dedf2e9ab48c94e55c9d3d0be08e23d4006737da90c5f647b","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -m \\\"$(cat \\u003c\\u003c'EOF'\\nmissions ux: replace peek panel with Linear's full-detail navigation model\\n\\nOperator rejected the permane..."}
