{"ts":"2026-09-12T02:05:43.391380061Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"mission: m-2026-09-12-001\nround: 1\nauthor: edt\nverdict: pass\nconfidence: 0.85\nfiles_changed:\n  - path: apps/desk/src/App.css\n    added: 193\n    removed: 98\n  - path: apps/desk/src/components/GroupHeader.tsx\n    added: 1\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src/components/MissionDetailView.tsx\n    added: 414\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src/components/MissionRowView.tsx\n    added: 16\n    removed: 10\n  - path: apps/desk/src/components/MissionsScreen.tsx\n    added: 144\n    removed: 39\n  - path: apps/desk/src/components/PeekPanel.tsx\n    added: 0\n    removed: 308\n  - path: apps/desk/src/components/Prose.tsx\n    added: 23\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src/lib/delegation.ts\n    added: 27\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src/lib/format.ts\n    added: 66\n    removed: 55\n  - path: apps/desk/src/lib/grouping.ts\n    added: 31\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src/lib/prose.ts\n    added: 48\n    removed: 0\n  - path: apps/desk/src/types.ts\n    added: 12\n    removed: 0\nevidence:\n  - name: tsc --noEmit clean (apps/desk)\n    status: pass\n  - name: make shot SCREEN=/ — full-width list, Recent scope (apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png)\n    status: pass\n  - name: make shot SCREEN=/missions/\u003cid\u003e — direct URL deep-link renders the full detail route (fallback screenshot, pathname routing confirmed working; caught mid-fetch \"loading...\" due to shot.sh's own documented row-less-screen limitation, see open_questions) (apps/desk/.tmp/shots/missions_m-2026-08-09-024-fallback.png)\n    status: pass\n  - name: ad hoc Playwright — fully-loaded detail view, title 2-line clamp + \"Show full title\", ask 6-line clamp + \"Show full\", worker-only Ask caption, YAML-literal-block prose normalized into real paragraphs with list lines preserved (apps/desk/.tmp/shots/detail-loaded.png)\n    status: pass\n  - name: ad hoc Playwright — activity one-line collapse/expand, evidence collapsed past 4 with \"+N more\" toggle, on a 17-evidence-item mission (verified interactively, screenshots not retained in final evidence set — described in prose below)\n    status: pass\n  - name: ad hoc Playwright — headline collision discriminator fires only on rows sharing a ticket that are BOTH visible in the active scope (e.g. \"ethos-268t · 053\"/\"· 052\"/etc. under All scope); verified the reverse case live via the API and fixed a real bug where it fired on an isolated visible row colliding with an off-screen one (apps/desk/.tmp/shots/list-all-scope.png)\n    status: pass\n  - name: ad hoc Playwright — Esc and browser back/forward (popstate) both correctly toggle between /  and /missions/\u003cid\u003e, and list scroll position + row selection are restored exactly across a detail round-trip (measured scrollTop before/after: 400/400)\n    status: pass\nopen_questions:\n  - \"D-2026-09-12 ambiguity: the mission said delegation records 'carry agent_type' to distinguish the worker's prompt from the evaluator's. Probed live against a 3-delegation mission (m-2026-07-21-001): deskd's /api/missions/{id} delegation records are {id, prompt_excerpt} only, no agent_type field anywhere. Resolved via the literal signal the mission also gave me: exclude any delegation whose prompt_excerpt starts with 'You are the pinned evaluator' (lib/delegation.ts), picking the first remaining one as the worker's ask. This is a text-prefix heuristic, not a real classification — it would misfire on a differently-worded evaluator prompt template. Flagging since 'carries agent_type' as stated doesn't match what the API returns today.\"\n  - \"D-2026-09-12 ambiguity: title font-size. The teardown's D6 ruling (16px/500, calibrated for the retired 430px peek gutter) is still in force per 'rulings still apply', but this mission also says 'Detail view = linear-detail-crop.png at full size'. I read the two as compatible by superseding D6 for this one sub-detail — the title now renders at 22px/600 (larger, matching the real detail-page reference) while D6's underlying intent (no giant blaring headline given our 'title' is really success_criteria[0] and can be a full paragraph) is preserved via the mandated 2-line clamp. Flagging the font-size number as my judgment call, not a literal instruction.\"\n  - \"Data observation, not a bug: 'Recent' (last 14 days) is nearly empty against the live ethos repo dataset today — verified via the API that only 1 of 155 missions has activity (closed_at/created_at) within 14 days of the actual host clock (2026-09-11/12); the bulk of recorded activity clusters around Aug 22 and earlier, 3+ weeks out. The feature is implemented and verified correct (tested by widening the window and by using the 'All' pill), it's just that this specific demo dataset has a multi-week gap right before 'now'. Same category of finding as D10's group-density note from m-2026-09-11-021: real data doesn't match the density the ruling's own example assumed.\"\n  - \"Found and fixed during this round (not left for a defect cycle): the collision discriminator was originally scoped to the whole search-filtered set rather than what's actually rendered under the active scope (Recent's day-groups or All's status-groups). Caught live: m-2026-05-07-001 and m-2026-05-07-002 share ticket 'xboing-c-ktp'; -002 sits outside the 14-day window, so the isolated -001 row was getting a spurious '· 001' suffix for a collision the user can't see. Fixed in the second commit (bf729bb) — headlines/flatIds now derive from the actual on-screen row set.\"\n  - \"Minor pre-existing redundancy, not introduced this round and not asked to be fixed: when a mission has no context/ticket, the title (= success_criteria[0]) is also the FIRST bullet in the criteria list below it, so that text appears twice on the page. Same behavior existed in the retired peek panel design. Noting it rather than silently changing scope.\"\nprose: |\n  Replaced the permanent 430px peek panel (rejected by the operator: dead\n  row space, titles truncating early) with Linear's actual navigation\n  model, cloned literally from linear-detail-crop.png and\n  linear-rows-crop.png.\n\n  Routing (MissionsScreen.tsx): plain history.pushState/popstate between\n  \"/\" and \"/missions/\u003cid\u003e\" — no router dependency (package.json is\n  outside the write set anyway), and it means make shot SCREEN=/missions/\u003cid\u003e\n  renders the real detail route directly. List scroll position and row\n  selection are saved before navigating away and restored on return;\n  verified both survive a full navigate-out/navigate-back round trip.\n\n  MissionDetailView.tsx (new, replaces PeekPanel.tsx): centered ~760px\n  prose column — title with a real 2-line CSS clamp + \"Show full title\"\n  (only rendered when the title actually overflows two lines, measured\n  via scrollHeight vs clientHeight, never a dead-end button), \"the ask\"\n  as a ~6-line clamped excerpt + \"Show full\", one-line collapsed activity\n  entries (author + verdict glyph + first sentence) that expand to full\n  prose + evidence (collapsed past 4, \"+N more\") + open questions — plus\n  a fixed 280px properties rail on the right (status, worker-\u003eevaluator,\n  round, ticket, write-set count) with Mechanics as a collapsed \u003cdetails\u003e\n  at the rail's bottom.\n\n  Headline precedence changes to context \u003e ticket \u003e trimmed criterion\n  (lib/format.ts), with a collision discriminator when two rows visible\n  under the SAME active scope resolve to identical text. Row and detail\n  titles no longer pre-truncate in JS at a fixed character budget — CSS\n  ellipsis (row) and line-clamp (detail) clip against the row's real\n  available width instead, which is the actual fix for the operator's\n  \"titles truncating into dead row space\" complaint.\n\n  \"The ask\" now shows the WORKER's delegation specifically\n  (lib/delegation.ts) rather than whichever delegation happened to be\n  first, since deskd's delegation records carry no agent_type field\n  (probed live) — the evaluator's conventional prompt prefix is the\n  actual signal used, per the ambiguity noted above.\n\n  lib/prose.ts normalizes YAML literal-block text into real paragraphs:\n  wrapped single newlines join into one line, blank-line breaks are kept\n  as paragraph breaks, and list/checklist lines (-, *, digit., ✓, ✕) are\n  preserved verbatim rather than getting merged into surrounding prose.\n  Verified live on a mission whose result prose mixes plain paragraphs\n  with an inline checklist — both render correctly.\n\n  Default list scope is \"Recent\" (14-day activity window, grouped by\n  day); \"All\" is the previous status-grouped view behind a pill.\n\n  Two commits on spike/thin-slice (42be816, bf729bb — the second fixes a\n  real bug I found during my own verification pass, see open_questions).\n  tsc --noEmit clean after each. 3+ look-iterate cycles against the\n  Linear references, plus interactive Playwright verification beyond\n  what make shot alone can drive (search, scope pills, row clicks,\n  keyboard Escape, browser back/forward) since make shot has no\n  interaction support.\n","file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/.tmp/missions/m-2026-09-12-001-result.yaml"},"tool_input_hash":"c04f6c79e3d324667f56c463b0fe5623f7dc10602f0878605b116a6aa24ca9e2","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"mission: m-2026-09-12-001\\nround: 1\\nauthor: edt\\nverdict: pass\\nconfidence: 0.85\\nfiles_changed:\\n  - path: apps/desk/src/App.css\\n    added: 193\\n    removed: 98\\n  - path: apps/desk/src..."}
