{"ts":"2026-09-12T02:06:42.477925459Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Mission m-2026-09-12-001 done. Replaced the rejec…","message":"Mission m-2026-09-12-001 done. Replaced the rejected permanent peek panel with Linear's actual navigation model (apps/desk/src/** only). Round 1 result submitted: verdict=pass, confidence=0.85.\n\nTwo commits on spike/thin-slice:\n- 42be816 — routing (history.pushState/popstate between / and /missions/\u003cid\u003e, no router dependency) + new MissionDetailView.tsx (centered ~760px prose, 2-line title clamp, 6-line ask clamp, one-line collapsed activity entries, evidence collapsed past 4, fixed 280px properties rail) + headline precedence rewrite (context\u003eticket\u003ecriterion, JS truncation removed in favor of CSS ellipsis/clamp) + lib/prose.ts (YAML literal-block normalization) + lib/delegation.ts (worker-vs-evaluator prompt heuristic); removed PeekPanel.tsx\n- bf729bb — real bug fix found during my own verification: the headline collision discriminator was scoped to the whole filtered set instead of what's actually on screen, so an isolated visible row could get a spurious \"· NNN\" suffix from a collision with an off-screen row. Fixed to scope against the active scope's rendered rows.\n\ntsc --noEmit clean after each. Since make shot has no interaction support, I did most verification via ad hoc Playwright (documented in the result, not committed): confirmed title/ask clamp+expand only appear when content actually overflows (measured via scrollHeight, never a dead-end button), activity expand + evidence-past-4 collapse, All-scope collision discriminators firing correctly on real ticket collisions, and — importantly — scroll position + row selection surviving a full detail round-trip (measured scrollTop 400→400) via both breadcrumb and Escape, plus browser back/forward.\n\nScreenshots in apps/desk/.tmp/shots/: root.png (Recent scope, make shot), list-all-scope.png, detail-loaded.png (fully-loaded detail, ad hoc), missions_m-2026-08-09-024-fallback.png (proves the /missions/\u003cid\u003e URL route itself works via make shot — caught mid-fetch since shot.sh's row-less-screen fallback has no additional wait, a known tool limitation I didn't touch).\n\nAmbiguities flagged in the result (also sending the gist here since they're worth your attention):\n1. The mission said delegation records \"carry agent_type\" — probed live, they don't (id+prompt_excerpt only). Used the literal fallback signal you also gave me: exclude prompts starting \"You are the pinned evaluator\". Text-heuristic, not a real classification.\n2. Title font-size: D6 (16px/500) is still-in-force per the ruling, but this mission also said \"linear-detail-crop.png at full size\" — I read those as compatible by sizing the detail title larger (22px/600, matching the real reference) while keeping D6's intent alive via the mandated 2-line clamp. Flagging the number as my judgment call.\n3. Data observation: \"Recent\" (14 days) is nearly empty against live data — only 1/155 missions has activity in the real last 14 days (verified via API against the actual host clock). Feature works correctly, this dataset just has a multi-week gap right before \"now\" — same shape of finding as last round's D10 note.\n\nFull result: `ethos mission show m-2026-09-12-001` / `ethos mission results m-2026-09-12-001`.","recipient":"main","summary":"m-2026-09-12-001 done — peek panel replaced with Linear's full-detail nav","to":"main","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"73ae8875aa97593af6872e145015bd2d22298f8ce0477a83608c38de0fbc053f","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Mission m-2026-09-12-001 done. Replaced the rejec…\",\"message\":\"Mission m-2026-09-12-001 done. Replaced the rejected permanent peek panel with Linear's actual navigation model (apps/desk/..."}
