{"ts":"2026-09-12T02:18:07.404323011Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git add apps/desk/src/App.css apps/desk/src/components/MissionDetailView.tsx apps/desk/src/components/MissionRowView.tsx apps/desk/src/lib/format.ts apps/desk/src/lib/prose.ts \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nmissions ux: collapse disclosure to two levels + L3 audit, pixel fidelity\n\nOperator amendment to m-2026-09-12-001: \u003e2 disclosure levels loses users\n(NN/g). Restructures the detail view and applies measured pixel values\ninstead of taste-based approximations.\n\n- L1 (row): status glyph, title, muted date, avatar — nothing else. The\n  trace-log marker moved off the row (into its title tooltip + the\n  detail rail's status line) rather than being a fifth element.\n- L2 (detail, above the fold): title (2-line clamp), Ask excerpt\n  (6-line clamp), \"Latest outcome\" — one static excerpt (author,\n  verdict glyph, 3-line clamped prose via the new lib/prose.ts\n  firstParagraph), properties rail. No per-round expand/collapse at this\n  level anymore.\n- ONE door, \"Full record — rounds, evidence, timeline, mechanics\",\n  replaces three previously-separate collapsibles (per-round activity\n  disclosure, standalone rail Mechanics, an implicit timeline spot).\n  Opens success criteria + every round's full prose (narrative, stays\n  flat per the ruling) in place.\n- L3 (operator's carve-out inside Full Record): evidence tables,\n  timeline, and contract mechanics (hashes, delegation ids, write-set\n  paths) — audit-type detail — get their own \u003cdetails\u003e nested inside the\n  door. Narrative content never drops to L3.\n\nPixel fidelity, measured against the reference PNGs rather than eyeballed:\n- Row height 32px -\u003e 39px: linear-rows-crop.png's vertical luminance\n  autocorrelates to a 78px period (consistent across 6/8 sampled\n  columns); the same technique against the same-scale ours-rows-crop.png\n  measured 72px for our then-36px rows, giving a 2.0px-per-CSS-px scale\n  -\u003e 78/2.0 = 39px.\n- List/detail background -\u003e --elevated (#131418): linear-detail-crop.png\n  samples ~rgb(18-23,19-23,20-24) uniformly across its frame (no sidebar\n  in crop) — a few rgb units from --elevated, ~15-20 units from the\n  --ground the panes previously inherited. Row hover bumped to\n  --elevated-2 to stay distinct against the lighter base.\n- Detail rail 280px -\u003e 300px: a rough visual proportion read (Linear has\n  no border/bg seam to auto-detect the rail boundary against), flagged\n  in-code as a judgment call, not measured with the same rigor as row\n  height.\n- Title font-size and gap rhythm: attempted glyph-height extraction from\n  linear-detail-crop.png but couldn't get a clean apples-to-apples\n  measurement (title string has no descenders, the body sample line\n  does, and the two lines' ink spans weren't separable in the profile) —\n  left unchanged rather than force an unreliable number.\nEOF\n)\""},"tool_input_hash":"4b6744b1e412dccf68b83d466c53e36c0a02a4d303718a9d0fd90b7f344224a2","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git add apps/desk/src/App.css apps/desk/src/components/MissionDetailView.tsx apps/desk/src/components/MissionRowView.tsx apps/desk/src/lib/format.ts..."}
