{"ts":"2026-09-12T02:24:58.621250083Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Amendment work for m-2026-09-12-001 done, on top …","message":"Amendment work for m-2026-09-12-001 done, on top of round 1 (already recorded pass). Mission is still showing \"round 1 of 2\" with no reflect/advance event yet, so I did NOT call `ethos mission result` again (round 1's result is already recorded and append-only) — that's a mission-mechanics step for you, not me. Let me know if you want a round-2 result submitted once you've reflected/advanced it.\n\nThree commits on spike/thin-slice (all apps/desk/src/**, tsc clean after each):\n\n1. `2d477c7` — collapsed disclosure to exactly two levels per the NN/g amendment:\n   - L1 (row): status glyph · title · muted date · avatar, nothing else — moved the trace-log marker off the row (into its title tooltip + the detail rail) rather than keeping it as a 5th element.\n   - L2 (detail, above the fold): title (2-line clamp), Ask excerpt (6-line clamp), \"Latest outcome\" — one static excerpt (author, verdict glyph, 3-line-clamped first paragraph via a new `firstParagraph` helper in lib/prose.ts), properties rail. Deleted the per-round expand/collapse and \"Show earlier activity\" from this level entirely.\n   - ONE door, \"Full record — rounds, evidence, timeline, mechanics\", replacing the three previously-separate collapsibles. Opens success criteria + every round's full prose in place.\n   - Per your second message's ruling: audit-type content (evidence tables, timeline, mechanics — hashes/delegation ids/write-set paths) gets its own L3 `\u003cdetails\u003e` nested inside the door; narrative (round prose) stays flat at the door's own level.\n\n2. `bf729bb` (from before the amendment, already reported) — unrelated collision-discriminator scoping fix.\n\n3. `0b63a60` — found and fixed during my own screenshot review: the ask-clamp's fade-to-background gradient still targeted `--ground`, which was correct before this round's pixel-fidelity pass but rendered as a visible hard-edged bar once the surrounding pane switched to the lighter `--elevated`.\n\nPixel fidelity — measured, not eyeballed, where I could get a clean signal:\n- Row height 32px→39px: autocorrelated linear-rows-crop.png's vertical luminance (78px period, consistent across 6/8 sampled columns), cross-scaled through the same-scale ours-rows-crop.png pair (measured 72px there for our then-36px rows → 2.0px/CSS-px) → 78/2.0 = 39px.\n- List/detail background → `--elevated` (#131418): linear-detail-crop.png samples ~rgb(18-23,19-23,20-24) uniformly (verified no sidebar in frame) — a few rgb units from `--elevated`, ~15-20 from the `--ground` these panes previously inherited. Row hover bumped to `--elevated-2` to stay distinct.\n- Detail rail 280px→300px: flagged in-code as a judgment call, not a hard measurement — Linear's rail has no border/bg seam to auto-detect against, only text extent, so I didn't run it through the same autocorrelation rigor.\n- Title font-size and gap rhythm: I tried extracting glyph cap-height from linear-detail-crop.png but couldn't get a clean apples-to-apples read (the title string has no descenders, my body-text sample did, and the two ink-spans weren't cleanly separable) — left title size unchanged rather than force an unreliable number. Flagging this rather than pretending false precision.\n\nDensity budget: counted directly from a full-page screenshot at 1280x900 — the default L2 view (title + ask + latest outcome + Full Record door) renders in well under 30 lines with room to spare; the page doesn't even need to scroll on a 900px viewport. Screenshots: apps/desk/.tmp/shots/root.png (make shot, Recent scope), missions_m-2026-08-09-024-fallback.png (make shot on the detail route — mid-fetch due to shot.sh's known row-less-screen limitation, not a code issue), detail-l2-loaded.png and detail-full-record-open.png (ad hoc Playwright, fully loaded, confirms the L3 evidence/timeline/mechanics blocks all work independently).","recipient":"main","summary":"m-2026-09-12-001 amendment done — 2-level disclosure + pixel fidelity","to":"main","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"aace147fc05418fc7235aa96550201fb0c753be4765cbc3c566ae6429524c464","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Amendment work for m-2026-09-12-001 done, on top …\",\"message\":\"Amendment work for m-2026-09-12-001 done, on top of round 1 (already recorded pass). Mission is still showing \\\"round 1 of ..."}
