{"ts":"2026-09-12T02:30:03.871508695Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Checked before doing new work: the amendment IS a…","message":"Checked before doing new work: the amendment IS already in the current committed code (commit 2d477c7, plus a follow-up CSS fix in 0b63a60). I think what you reviewed was my very first `detail-loaded.png` from before either amendment message arrived — that one genuinely did have the flat criteria dump + per-round activity list you're describing, and I reused that same filename later without realizing it could get confused with the corrected version. Sorry for the ambiguity — verified three independent ways just now, all against the current HEAD:\n\n1. **Code inspection**: `grep -n \"Mechanics\\|audit-block\\|rail-property\" apps/desk/src/components/MissionDetailView.tsx` — the `\u003caside className=\"detail-rail\"\u003e` block contains only `.rail-property` rows, zero `\u003cdetails\u003e`. Mechanics exists exactly once, nested inside `full-record-body` as an `.audit-block`. One door on the page, confirmed structurally, not just visually.\n\n2. **Fresh screenshot**, regenerated just now from HEAD and saved as `apps/desk/.tmp/shots/detail-loaded.png` (same filename you referenced, now showing the corrected state): title (clamped) → Ask excerpt (clamped, \"Show full\") → LATEST OUTCOME (bwk, ✓, round 2, 2-line excerpt) → \"▸ FULL RECORD — ROUNDS, EVIDENCE, TIMELINE, MECHANICS\" (collapsed). No criteria, no round list, nothing else renders by default.\n\n3. **Measured line count** (not eyeballed — Playwright script summing `Math.round(el.scrollHeight / lineHeight)` across every text-bearing element in `.detail-prose` while Full Record stays collapsed): **16 lines total** (title 2, ask paragraphs 3+2+1=6, outcome excerpt 2, plus 6 single-line UI bits — two \"Show full\" links, the Ask caption, the \"Latest outcome\" label, the outcome meta row, the Full Record toggle line). Comfortably under the 30-line gate with room to spare — the page doesn't scroll on a 900px viewport.\n\nOpening Full Record shows criteria + every round's full prose + the L3 audit blocks (Evidence/Timeline/Mechanics as independent `\u003cdetails\u003e`) exactly per your ruling — already verified interactively last round (screenshots `l3-evidence-open.png`/`l3-mechanics-open.png` from that session, not currently in the shots dir but reproducible).\n\n**Pixel sampling — actual (linear-detail-crop.png) vs. applied**, honest about confidence:\n- **Background**: measured ~rgb(18-23,19-23,20-24) at 3 points, uniform, no sidebar in frame → applied `--elevated` #131418 (rgb 19,20,24). High confidence, near-exact.\n- **Row height**: linear-rows-crop.png autocorrelates to a 78px period (6/8 sampled columns agree) → cross-scaled via the same-scale ours-rows-crop.png pair (72px measured there for our then-36px rows → 2.0px/CSS-px) → 78/2.0 = 39px, applied exactly. High confidence.\n- **Title size**: measured title ink-height (ascender-to-baseline, descender-free string) = 38px in that image's own pixel space, but I have no independently-scaled reference element in that SAME crop to convert 38px into a real CSS px number (unlike the row-height pair, there's no \"ours\" comparison at matching scale for this specific screenshot). Left at 22px/600 (unchanged from last round, still a judgment call) rather than force a number from an incomplete scale chain. Flagging this gap explicitly rather than papering over it.\n- **Rail width**: applied 300px (≈28% of the 1056px available width). Rough visual read of the reference put its rail at ~32% of frame width, but Linear's rail has no border/bg seam to auto-detect against, only text extent — so this was eyeballed, not measured with the same rigor as row height.\n\n**Procedural note**: `ethos mission show m-2026-09-12-001` currently reports `Status: closed` (closed 2026-09-11 19:25 PDT). I can't submit another `ethos mission result` against a closed mission — that's a reopen/new-mission decision on your end, not mine to force. The work itself is done and committed on `spike/thin-slice` (`2d477c7`, `0b63a60`); let me know if you want it tracked as a new mission/round now that it's verified correct, or if this message is sufficient confirmation to consider it settled.","recipient":"main","summary":"m-2026-09-12-001 already has the amendment — likely a stale screenshot","to":"main","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"00666b14dab9e4f148a3d25ec26a2c24c41f8a2adf23f0f7d30b04f57000d344","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Checked before doing new work: the amendment IS a…\",\"message\":\"Checked before doing new work: the amendment IS already in the current committed code (commit 2d477c7, plus a follow-up CSS..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-12T02:30:14.821474181Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Settled, no reopen needed: my \"round 2 missing\" c…","message":"Settled, no reopen needed: my \"round 2 missing\" call was against your stale same-filename screenshot — my fault-adjacent confusion, and your triple verification (structural grep, fresh shot, 16 measured lines) closes it cleanly. The mission closed pass on the corrected state I re-reviewed (detail-l2-loaded.png), so the record is accurate. The pixel-sampling writeup with explicit confidence levels is exactly the standard we want — the flagged title-size gap goes to the operator's next design pass rather than being papered over. Done for now; strong round.","recipient":"worker-redesign","summary":"Settled — no reopen; well handled","to":"worker-redesign","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"c53e74f23fd6393ec94b3c456c1e3ba9fc06a1a2dc3f138d05452f9f3480ff88","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Settled, no reopen needed: my \\\"round 2 missing\\\" c…\",\"message\":\"Settled, no reopen needed: my \\\"round 2 missing\\\" call was against your stale same-filename screenshot — my fault-adjac..."}
