{"ts":"2026-09-12T13:11:40.386942269Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git add apps/desk/src/App.css apps/desk/src/components/MissionDetailView.tsx apps/desk/src/components/MissionsScreen.tsx apps/desk/src/lib/grouping.ts \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nfix: default to All scope, day-bucket timezone bug, empty-state, rail gulf\n\nFour mechanical fixes from live use of the Missions screen, apps/desk/src/**:\n\n1. Default list scope changes Recent -\u003e All: against the real store,\n   Recent's adaptive window still landed on a single row (activity has\n   multi-week gaps). Recent also becomes genuinely adaptive — the most\n   recent 30 missions by activity grouped by day, not a fixed 14-day\n   cutoff that can go empty — but the default is All either way.\n\n2. Fixed a real timezone bug: group headers reconstructed a synthetic\n   `${key}T00:00:00Z` string and formatted it in local time, which in\n   any zone behind UTC (PDT, etc.) always reads as the PREVIOUS local\n   day regardless of the bucket's actual date — hence \"SEP 1\" headers\n   over \"Sep 2\" rows. Bucketing now keys off local calendar-day parts\n   (lib/grouping.ts localDayKey), and the header label is formatted from\n   one of the bucket's own real row timestamps through the same\n   formatDate() the row itself uses — one code path, not two.\n\n3. Empty-state consolidation: a mission with neither a delegation nor a\n   result (abandoned before any work started) used to render two\n   separate dashed \"not recorded\" boxes as its whole L2 body. One\n   compact line replaces both (\"Abandoned before any delegation — no ask\n   or results recorded\"), with success criteria shown by default in this\n   one case, since otherwise there's nothing else on the page.\n\n4. Rail adjacency: .detail-main previously had its own flex:1 region and\n   centered the prose column inside it, independent of the rail, which\n   stayed pinned to .detail-body's far edge — the gap between them grew\n   with window width. .detail-body now centers prose+gap+rail as one\n   fixed-width block (neither child flexes), so the rail sits a constant\n   28px from the prose at any window size, matching\n   linear-detail-crop.png's adjacent layout.\nEOF\n)\""},"tool_input_hash":"a343c0b0d46dc4722bd3c73d2161a61595af77705b0a8ac4351d74143eb4ae7b","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git add apps/desk/src/App.css apps/desk/src/components/MissionDetailView.tsx apps/desk/src/components/MissionsScreen.tsx apps/desk/src/lib/grouping...."}
