{"ts":"2026-09-12T13:14:24.99913393Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git status --short apps/desk/dist apps/desk/src 2\u003e\u00261; cat apps/desk/.gitignore 2\u003e/dev/null | grep -i dist"},"tool_input_hash":"409aabc734d431a8565e53704ce5c38b32dfc0920fc8867b360e3944d962697e","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git status --short apps/desk/dist apps/desk/src 2\\u003e\\u00261; cat apps/desk/.gitignore 2\\u003e/dev/null | grep -i dist\"}"}
{"ts":"2026-09-12T13:14:31.687640873Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk \u0026\u0026 npx tsc --noEmit 2\u003e\u00261; cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 git status --short apps/desk/src/ \u0026\u0026 git log --oneline -3"},"tool_input_hash":"ba8fc250087f6c9dbbb69d9408bc52a45a0128431364e041af08cba2d58c588a","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/apps/desk \\u0026\\u0026 npx tsc --noEmit 2\\u003e\\u00261; cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 git status --short apps/desk/src/ \\u0026\\u0026 git log --oneline ..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-12T13:14:47.550787499Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","agent_id":"aworker-redesign-f17c7e06facedc5b","agent_type":"worker-redesign","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"All four fixes done on spike/thin-slice, commit `…","message":"All four fixes done on spike/thin-slice, commit `07fb60f`, apps/desk/src/** only, tsc clean.\n\n1. **Default scope → All.** Also made Recent genuinely adaptive per your \"better\" suggestion: it's now the most-recent-30-missions-by-activity grouped by day (lib/grouping.ts), not a fixed 14-day window that can go empty — but default stays All either way, one click to Recent.\n\n2. **Timezone bug fixed.** Root cause: the day-group header reconstructed a synthetic `${key}T00:00:00Z` string and formatted it in local time — in any zone behind UTC (PDT here) that ALWAYS reads as the previous local day, regardless of the bucket's real date, so headers permanently lagged their own rows by one day. Fixed by bucketing on local calendar-day parts and formatting the header from one of the bucket's own real row timestamps through the exact same `formatDate()` the row uses — one code path now, not two. Verified: m-2026-05-07-001's header now reads \"SEP 2\" matching its own row and the group's \"Sep 2\" constant, where before it read \"SEP 1.\"\n\n3. **Empty-state consolidated.** m-2026-05-07-001 (abandoned, no delegation, no result) now shows one line — \"not recorded — abandoned before any delegation — no ask or results recorded\" — with its 6 success criteria visible by default underneath (the one case where criteria earn default visibility). Verified via screenshot.\n\n4. **Rail adjacency fixed.** Root cause: `.detail-main` had its own `flex:1` region and centered the prose *inside* that region, independent of the rail, which stayed pinned to the window edge — gap grew with window width. Now `.detail-body` centers prose+28px-gap+rail as one fixed-width block (neither child flexes), so the rail sits a constant distance from the prose at any size. Verified at 1920px wide: the whole block sits together, centered in the available space, no gulf.\n\n**Verification note**: port 1420 was occupied by what looked like your own live-use session (a bare vite process with no `VITE_DESKD_URL` env, unlike my usual review instances) when I went to screenshot-iterate, so I didn't touch it — instead built a production bundle (`tsc \u0026\u0026 vite build`) and ran `vite preview` on 4173 against a separate deskd instance for verification, then tore that down when done. Didn't run the official `make shot` this round since it's hardcoded to port 1420 (vite.config.ts sets `strictPort`); happy to grab that evidence once your session is free if you want it, but all four fixes are confirmed working via the preview-build screenshots in the meantime.","recipient":"main","summary":"All four live-use fixes done and verified — commit 07fb60f","to":"main","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"d75b429b3fd4cff1b95506b4e10378bf9a584e352b777250e5b22d666ddb07fc","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"All four fixes done on spike/thin-slice, commit `…\",\"message\":\"All four fixes done on spike/thin-slice, commit `07fb60f`, apps/desk/src/** only, tsc clean.\\n\\n1. **Default scope → All...."}
{"ts":"2026-09-13T14:38:19.166063243Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"# Ethos data-standard revisions surfaced by the desk UI (2026-09-13)\n\nOperator conclusion after live use of the thin slice: \"the standard for\nethos data will have to be revised to make it more human friendly.\" This\nis the input list for that revision — every item was hit concretely while\nbuilding and using the Missions screen. Target: a design round in the\nethos repo (future DES).\n\n## Contract / record changes\n\n1. **`title` (new, required)** — a ≤70-char human phrase, written by the\n   leader at dispatch the way a Linear issue title is written. The single\n   highest-leverage change: without it, every list surface falls back to\n   criteria boilerplate (\"make check passes\" ×4, \"Mission close ceremony…\"\n   ×6 — measured on the live store).\n2. **`context` promoted** — today optional and missing on most missions;\n   it is the only existing human-sentence field. Require it (or fold its\n   role into `title` + a `description`).\n3. **Criteria hygiene for pipeline stages** — templated stage criteria\n   duplicate verbatim across dozens of missions; stage templates should\n   interpolate the feature/target into the criterion text so records stay\n   distinguishable.\n4. **Delegation records carry a role** — `role: worker | evaluator |\n   verifier` on `record.yaml`. The UI currently classifies prompts by\n   matching the literal string \"You are the pinned evaluator\" — a\n   heuristic where a schema field belongs.\n5. **Result prose contract** — `prose` opens with a 1–2 sentence human\n   summary paragraph (the excerpt surfaces it); detail follows. Same for\n   reflection prose. Bounded `open_questions` items.\n6. **Trace-log completeness** — `missions.jsonl` appends on *every*\n   terminal status (failed/abandoned/escalated too, and ideally create),\n   not only successful close: measured 104 unique trace ids vs 155 real\n   missions, and 30 ghost entries whose dirs are gone. Plus: fix the\n   `id` vs `mission_id` field-name split between find/list surfaces.\n7. **CLI JSON contracts** — `session --json` must emit JSON (today: prose\n   \"No active session.\" exit 0); `--json` should never emit prose on any\n   path.\n\n## Why this matters beyond desk\n\nThese records are read by humans in every surface — `ethos mission show`,\nthe web UI, PR reviews of committed mission records — not just by desk.\nHuman-friendly records make the audit trail legible everywhere; desk just\nmade the cost of machine-first records visible and measurable.\n","file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/docs/ethos-data-standard-findings.md"},"tool_input_hash":"63e56e6b727976daa959a5e59f5223c630d7b2155e16cc8f5fc3cbdd18617670","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"# Ethos data-standard revisions surfaced by the desk UI (2026-09-13)\\n\\nOperator conclusion after live use of the thin slice: \\\"the standard for\\nethos data will have to be revised to make..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-13T14:38:27.985775275Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \u0026\u0026 npx --yes markdownlint-cli2 docs/ethos-data-standard-findings.md \u0026\u0026 git add docs/ethos-data-standard-findings.md \u0026\u0026 git commit -q -m \"docs: ethos data-standard revision list surfaced by desk live use\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 \[REDACTED:email]\u003e\" \u0026\u0026 echo committed","description":"Lint and commit the data-standard findings"},"tool_input_hash":"644e17ba3df37fe1bbc2b3dea342d41b470c1045bf1df091e19b169962ec2e71","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"cd ~/Coding/punt-labs/desk \\u0026\\u0026 npx --yes markdownlint-cli2 docs/ethos-data-standard-findings.md \\u0026\\u0026 git add docs/ethos-data-standard-findings.md \\u0026\\u0026 git commit -..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-13T14:38:42.092776207Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"---\nname: desk-status-and-data-standard\ndescription: Desk spike verdict (2026-09-13) — UI \"reasonable but not great\"; next big thread is revising the ethos data standard to be human-friendly\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nAs of 2026-09-13, the desk thin slice (repo `~/Coding/punt-labs/desk`,\nbranch `spike/thin-slice`, unmerged per operator rule) is live as a native\nTauri app: full-width Linear-pattern list, navigate-to-detail, two-level\ndisclosure (+L3 audit inside \"Full record\"), measured pixel values.\nOperator verdict: **\"reasonable but not great\"** — expects substantial\nfurther UX time, and ruled that **the ethos data standard must be revised\nto be human friendly**. The concrete revision list (title field, context\npromotion, criteria template hygiene, delegation role field, prose summary\ncontract, trace-log completeness, CLI JSON contracts) lives in\n`desk/docs/ethos-data-standard-findings.md`; UX rulings in\n`desk/docs/ux-teardown-2026-09-11.md` (D1–D12 + follow-ups).\n\n**How to apply:** the next major thread is an ethos-repo design round for\nthe data standard (future DES) using that findings doc as input; desk UX\nwork continues reference-anchored per [[no-freelance-design]], demos\nnative per [[desk-native-not-browser]], verification by running per\n[[verification-requires-running]].\n","file_path":"~/.claude/projects/-home-jfreeman-Coding-punt-labs-ethos/memory/desk-status-and-data-standard.md"},"tool_input_hash":"bd0ea5d858dc5f81d3ca904d5fe4da41d3ccb2e5c0c8334fe30b9beb587c85e2","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"---\\nname: desk-status-and-data-standard\\ndescription: Desk spike verdict (2026-09-13) — UI \\\"reasonable but not great\\\"; next big thread is revising the ethos data standard to be human-..."}
