{"ts":"2026-09-13T16:03:02.444612444Z","session":"00f1ab56-8e0a-4c22-8f2c-ed8da8891ca9","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"# Desk spike — what we learned\n\n**Status: closed spike (2026-09-13).** Not production code; kept for\nreference on branch `spike/thin-slice`, deliberately unmerged. Runtime\nstopped. No open workstream. If a workspace GUI is built for real, start\nfrom `PLAN.md` plus this document — not from this code.\n\n## What the spike was\n\n~One day plus fix rounds: a native Tauri 2 app (React 19 + Vite) showing\nthe ethos repo's real 155-mission store through a Go bridge daemon\n(`spike/deskd`) that shells out to the `ethos --json` CLI. Built by ethos\nmissions (edt/bwk/adb workers, dna/rsc/kth evaluators), reviewed by three\nlocal review agents, verified in the running window by the operator.\n\n## Validated\n\n- **\"GUI features are CLI features with pixels\" holds.** Four HTTP\n  endpoints over CLI output plus three predicted filesystem reads\n  (prompt.md, artifacts, delegation enumeration) fed the whole UI.\n- **Daemon-with-cache wins the transport question.** Cold `/api/missions`\n  ~314 ms (dominated by a 51-mission enrichment fan-out), warm 0–1 ms,\n  detail ~17 ms. Exec-per-request alone misses the zero-spinner bar cold.\n- **The Berd sidecar model works end-to-end**: Tauri shell spawns the Go\n  daemon, reads a stdout port/token handshake into managed state, webview\n  fetches with a bearer token; CORS (not CSP) is the localhost-fetch\n  hurdle on Linux (`http://tauri.localhost` origin, often-empty Origin\n  header → permissive headers on the daemon, token in Authorization).\n- **The agent screenshot loop is non-negotiable and works.** Its first\n  ever use caught a clipped layout no code read had found; the whole UX\n  convergence ran on read-the-PNG-next-to-the-reference iteration.\n- **Reference-literal design converges; freelancing does not.** Three\n  freehand attempts produced the same overloaded design; progress started\n  only when real Linear screens were cloned with measured values\n  (autocorrelated row height 39 px, sampled backgrounds) and every delta\n  was an explicit operator ruling (D1–D12, `docs/ux-teardown-2026-09-11.md`).\n  NN/g progressive disclosure, applied for real: two levels, one labeled\n  door (plus an operator-sanctioned third level for audit material only).\n\n## Learned the hard way\n\n- **Verification requires running the product.** The Tauri leg was called\n  \"done\" before it had ever compiled (a factual correction is filed on\n  mission m-2026-09-11-006). Host truths found only by running: Tauri 2\n  needs rustc ≥ ~1.85 (`edition2024`), webkit2gtk/gtk dev packages, and a\n  linuxbrew `pkg-config` silently shadowing the system one breaks the\n  build with misleading \"missing library\" errors.\n- **Native is the product; the browser is a test rig.** Demoing the vite\n  path where a desktop app was ruled is a category error.\n- **The UI cannot be more human than its data — the spike's biggest\n  product finding.** Rows were indistinguishable because mission records\n  have no titles and pipeline criteria are verbatim templates; a third of\n  the trace log is missing or ghosted; delegation records don't say\n  worker-vs-evaluator; prose is unbounded. The revision list is\n  `docs/ethos-data-standard-findings.md` — that, not more UI work, is the\n  successor thread.\n- **Dogfooding ethos missions found real tooling frictions**: repeated\n  `--write-set` flags override instead of append (and then block\n  `mission result`); bare `mission list` hides open missions; `session\n  --json` emits prose; `find` vs `list` disagree on the id field name.\n- **Many agents on one host contend**: ethos session-lock flakes (~50%\n  daemon-start failures under load), vite EMFILE, leaked dev servers\n  squatting ports, a harness memory guard reaping long-running windows\n  (fix: launch detached via setsid).\n\n## Disposition\n\nCode, mission records, UX teardown, and data-standard findings all live\non `spike/thin-slice`. Nothing merges; nothing is scheduled. The two\nideas that outlive the spike: revise the ethos data standard to be\nhuman-first, and — if/when a real client is built — the module-contract\narchitecture and testing pyramid in `PLAN.md`.\n","file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/desk/LEARNINGS.md"},"tool_input_hash":"032c6e14f17f88b58dfb3daf8df31c191caaa12cabe45a699a0e4e8c416fd606","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"# Desk spike — what we learned\\n\\n**Status: closed spike (2026-09-13).** Not production code; kept for\\nreference on branch `spike/thin-slice`, deliberately unmerged. Runtime\\nstopped. N..."}
